{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2088,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:08:34.108185360Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"1d5342a0-e55e-4413-b2dd-ad4438934bc7","title":"[L003] Checkpoint capture inherits patch byte ceilings","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L003.\n\n- `crates/app/peritus-daemon/src/product_run/workbench/checkpoints/capture.rs:246-254` reads each whole file with `peritus_patch::MAX_FILE_BYTES`, then maps **every** inspection error to `ControlError::StaleRevision`.\n- Selected checkpoint capture also rejects aggregate body bytes above `peritus_patch::MAX_PATCH_BYTES` at lines 53-62; checkpoint recapture does the same at lines 79-88.\n- Daily-driving blocker: checkpoints of ordinary build artifacts can fail before a command runs. The per-file bound was implicated by the prior live-run diagnosis. Exact constant definitions, automatic command caller, persistence format, and restore enforcement will be verified by complete reads in this audit.\n- Structural issue: patch payload admission limits are reused as checkpoint file/storage limits, and capacity/I/O failures become a revision-change error. Merely increasing a number would leave that coupling and misleading error path intact.\n- Exact byte declarations are now read in `peritus-patch/src/set.rs:11-16`: both `MAX_FILE_BYTES` and `MAX_PATCH_BYTES` are **8 MiB**. Automatic capture at `checkpoints/capture/automatic.rs:71-75` calls the same capped `observe_path`; manual capture at `checkpoints.rs:148` does too. Sealing a manual checkpoint recaptures every path at `automatic.rs:152-169`, and fork validation at `checkpoints.rs:68-78` likewise recaptures paths.\n- `product_run/interaction/live.rs:118-142` now verifies the live workspace-mutation hook: automatic capture failure returns an error stating that Peritus did not change the workspace. Sealing failures also stop with a durable-recording error. `peritus-product-runner/src/execution/checkpoint.rs:89-133` now verifies the observer forwards BeforeMutation to that ConversationView hook; `turn.rs:280-291` installs it on writer/fixer tools, and `executor.rs:243-257` rejects failed preflight before dispatch. The live precommand capture chain is source-verified. Durable storage and restore have been read and add independent ceilings (L013, L020, L021).\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQNsq7pIKJccqmP924S+09Av+J9d9z+qLJjZNxvwHRs6uLm8EETcEqKaQNuc3Aqo5O5cct3ApF9zwSrF358N5rAw="}
