{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2099,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:19:07.865564519Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"27df59d6-19ba-593d-b363-47e5993d64a1","title":"[L009] Canonical codec production ceilings","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L009.\n\n- `crates/foundation/peritus-codec/src/limits.rs:20-29,52-55` makes production limits the default: **16 MiB complete frame**, payload **16 MiB minus frame header**, **65,535 collection items**, **1 MiB per UTF-8 string**, **8 MiB per opaque field**, and **64 nested aggregates**.\n- `writer.rs:87-125,128-150` rejects opaque/string/collection/depth/total-payload excess before writing. `reader.rs:106-157` independently rejects opaque/string/collection/depth excess on decode. Length prefixes use `u32` representation; these structural representation bounds differ from the configured smaller ceilings.\n- Daily-driving effect depends on each caller's chosen limits and whether a representation contains a whole file, growing conversation, or transient message. Patch identity already uses these production limits (L006). Frame/message enforcement and remaining callers are pending.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQD5gESxvzaNuIheQYpiP6ZDUwj1pqC0SieDzCkztsM4pUZn/QnS4BlhzPl9oSa7U3QhhBaFOugnKixqgYhsMWAI="}
