history beyond the reported count/byte boundaries, lock contention lasting beyond the old patience window, lost commit acknowledgements followed by later progress, torn uncommitted tails and true committed corruption, then reopen and resolve exact historical receipts. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:19:07.750Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQK34+1T2GPoLRN61bFuiHUGdMD1i1tGRdrOqWfUjGTWAcXQOlZAsZqUfDQ0tsx/wSu63hFGyRTYL6tqYhIHOYgQ="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2117,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:19:07.905687878Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"efe55bd5-def2-5e1d-8003-22e7d5da2a9e","title":"[L016] Transaction manifest ancestor and decoder ceilings","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L016.\n\n- `crates/runtime/peritus-patch/src/transaction/manifest.rs:227-244` expands every operation into every ancestor path before validating manifest capacity. This includes ancestors that already exist, not just directories that a transaction will create.\n- Encoding at lines 121-147 uses L009's production codec: a created-directory collection cannot exceed **65,535** and total manifest payload must fit **16 MiB minus header**, including its checksum. Thus paths/operations within L006/L008 can still fail admission due to expanded ancestor representation.\n- Decoding at lines 150-173 and 260-269 re-enforces payload capacity, **1,024 entries**, and **8 MiB file identities**. Decode failure becomes `CorruptManifest` with `FenceWorkspace` at lines 303-310.\n- Structural consequence: admission, stored manifest, recovery reader, and expanded ancestor representation all carry the same hard policies. Raising only one limit would leave other rejection/fencing paths intact.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQA6lhpALfsAKchx0Coa5wynhuYTa9vHwJ/I7w50Kf1cWfwwC74u6ASHegYRjohVVc71OOuKj3PP1TCVehYLEPAI="}
