 usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: large-file and many-path capture/restore, divergent preimage rejection, interrupted staging/publication/restore, then reopen and continue the same conversation with an exact restored workspace. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:19:07.750Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQN1CyHWR7ojwoAIrV85EGtR3G+42h4R0pFB8zd5oXBpzbvYrcqsvcgzXnhSldwrH03/H4EgkwDW/FCRV1qrR9QU="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2119,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:19:07.910024918Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"80ada650-079c-58be-b797-75942f71f07f","title":"[L019] Control journal has a 250 ms lock-wait deadline","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L019.\n\n- `crates/app/peritus-daemon/src/product_control/storage.rs:65-80` obtains an exclusive ownership lock immediately with `try_lock`, then opens SQLite with `busy_timeout = Duration::from_millis(250)`.\n- **250 ms** is an explicit artificial database lock-wait deadline. `peritus-journal/src/sqlite/connection.rs:242-245` applies the supplied timeout directly through rusqlite. The same adapter has a separate **5-second default** at lines 17-20. Retry callers remain pending full reads; no inference is made yet about which live operation encountered it.\n- The ownership lock is a separate exclusive-writer constraint. Its Drop implementation explicitly releases ownership after journal close (lines 48-60), preserving inherited-handle behavior.\n- `product_control/error.rs:42-55` preserves typed sources internally, while public Journal failures say reconciliation is required and I/O failures conflate unavailable storage with existing ownership. A transient busy deadline may therefore be presented as a durable integrity/availability issue; adapter classification remains pending.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQJfvh2BUQg0qTF5HL+rMj5Roo9b2J6B/mPmbYSoPiJEtoY8FQoSIoY4EDFGFrT/UTfyJFoYD3OdMRsvE8+oUmQ8="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2120,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:19:07.912166160Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"80ada650-079c-58be-b797-75942f71f07f","comment_uuid":"d4fa8297-c490-4d62-b568-2aa2f87fc8d8","author":"6ME5","content":"Systemic repair plan for L019: Control journal has a 250 ms lock-wait deadline.\n\nOwning contract and implementation boundary: crates/app/peritus-daemon/src/product_control/storage.rs:65-80; peritus-journal/src/sqlite/connection.rs:242-245; product_control/error.rs:42-55. Apply the change through the constructors, live callers, durable writer and restart reader for this boundary, not as an isolated constant increase.\n\nMove journal writes behind an explicit cancellable owner queue. Treat SQLite busy/locked as contention and wait for ownership release or a user-selected cancellation, without a synthetic patience deadline. Keep the exclusive-writer file lock, distinguish busy from I/O and corruption, and preserve the same command identity while awaiting or reconciling commit.\n\nPreserve: committed command/event identity, exact causal and digest roots, exclusive ownership, atomic publication, reference-safe artifact retention and verified recovery from the last durable frontier. Separate a physical allocation/page limit and a genuine authority or integrity check from a cumulative work allowance. Keep transient contention/capacity observable and recoverable under the existing logical task; do not discard accepted state or substitute a fresh session to get around it.\n\nCompatibility/migration: retain decoders and exact receipts for previously accepted records. If representation or lifecycle semantics change, introduce a versioned migration under exclusive ownership; verify a complete replacement frontier before atomic publication and keep the old recovery root until adoption is durable. Rebuild derived projections from authoritative evidence. Update all producers, consumers and invariants together; a rejected new operation must leave the predecessor usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: history beyond the reported count/byte boundaries, lock contention lasting beyond the old patience window, lost commit acknowledgements followed by later progress, torn uncommitted tails and true committed corruption, then reopen and resolve exact historical receipts. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:19:07.750Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQMZtiWAjqiCrElScR9qAAYRAk4HNiPVhM5JilNrIzVk+5JMbEe4B+6LVd58iH3jk/10MaF+JoOF2g9BZiDSqow4="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2121,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:19:07.914303038Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"d1a900b8-6f7a-527e-bb5b-a9d059fbfe85","title":"[L020] Journal atomic-batch ceilings restrict checkpoint admission","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L020.\n\n- `crates/state/peritus-journal/src/append_plan.rs:17-28` declares **4,096 events**, **1,024 aggregate heads**, **4,096 state installs**, **4,096 outbox rows**, **4,096 outbox acknowledgements**, and **4,096 artifact dependencies** per atomic batch. `plan` calls bound validation at lines 131-138; `append_plan/validation.rs:17-39` enforces every listed count bound.\n- `product_control/storage/checkpoints.rs:214-240` creates one StateInstall per present checkpoint body. `product_control/storage.rs:207-235` adds a conversation-root state and receipt state to that same batch. This creates another admission layer beneath L010's 65,535-path manifest bound.\n- Checkpoint keys additionally cast their path index to `u16` at `storage/checkpoints.rs:243-247`.\n- Daily-driving effect: a many-file checkpoint can fit its manifest and byte limits while exceeding the atomic state-install count. The fully read validation helper confirms rejection. More than **4,094 present bodies** exceeds the 4,096-install cap after the root and receipt installs are added. Executable reproduction is pending.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQBZD2+Nz/IhBpFrLBESg88HzfAye0ZI7wyKRcwa/mbo3H6PSSeedSDLCScHOm/Bx6PUufSow0HiOloq/7F+Hawc="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2122,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:19:07.916339933Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"d1a900b8-6f7a-527e-bb5b-a9d059fbfe85","comment_uuid":"313ede1e-e9f7-409a-867c-6f1ae138fdd4","author":"6ME5","content":"Systemic repair plan for L020: Journal atomic-batch ceilings restrict checkpoint admission.\n\nOwning contract and implementation boundary: crates/state/peritus-journal/src/append_plan.rs:17-28; append_plan/validation.rs:17-39; product_control/storage/checkpoints.rs:214-240; product_control/storage.rs:207-235; storage/checkpoints.rs:243-247. Apply the change through the constructors, live callers, durable writer and restart reader for this boundary, not as an isolated constant increase.\n\nStage checkpoint bodies as immutable artifacts before one small atomic publication of their manifest, root and receipt. Journal batch ceilings should bound one database operation, not total checkpoint coverage. Page dependency evidence through durable roots with complete reachability, and validate the exact published restore manifest before accepting it.\n\nPreserve: exact snapshot/preimage identity, protected paths, ancestor and symlink safety, writable-fork coverage, conflict detection, one logical restore transaction and exact effect receipts. Separate a physical allocation/page limit and a genuine authority or integrity check from a cumulative work allowance. Keep transient contention/capacity observable and recoverable under the existing logical task; do not discard accepted state or substitute a fresh session to get around it.\n\nCompatibility/migration: retain decoders and exact receipts for previously accepted records. If representation or lifecycle semantics change, introduce a versioned migration under exclusive ownership; verify a complete replacement frontier before atomic publication and keep the old recovery root until adoption is durable. Rebuild derived projections from authoritative evidence. Update all producers, consumers and invariants together; a rejected new operation must leave the predecessor usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: large-file and many-path capture/restore, divergent preimage rejection, interrupted staging/publication/restore, then reopen and continue the same conversation with an exact restored workspace. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:19:07.750Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQFT6dwZ7FOAN1ERf+cIbe8xPYCvm35Q3oBGCsvZ83SRrb1t5+MzIJSDtQqB5eQSdJiTas3ARomqjmfd1RKtFcwk="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2123,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:19:07.918531272Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"babe9c8f-410e-592f-bd13-eaf0ffed2419","title":"[L021] Every ordinary control read re-verifies the entire growing archive","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L021.\n\n- `product_control/storage/replay.rs:14-75` implements current and historical conversation reads by loading the complete current aggregate, replaying every operation, and comparing the reconstructed state root. Each historical read still verifies the full current archive.\n- For each operation, lines 78-140 verify associated request/file/checkpoint/image/reply archives. `storage/checkpoints.rs:165-210` rereads and hashes every retained before-image for that checkpoint operation. `storage.rs:186-214` performs replay before each new transition and serializes the entire successor ConversationRecord into one capped state value (L011).\n- This is an algorithmic daily-driving risk independent of elapsed deadlines: work per ordinary read/mutation grows with all historical events and retained artifact bytes. The inspected implementation does not use a verified incremental replay cursor or a bounded append-only projection checkpoint here.\n- The journal aggregate query, conversation replay implementation, locking/presentation callers, and actual production scaling behavior remain pending; no benchmark or live lockup is attributed solely to this source finding.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQPUFUm6/nk4jo858jm457WY9BOMmvmiJLJAGSuZ669AYND1T66L7rYVx5FceTIlA/lQ3O0Hr5UYLPl5CesGhbws="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2124,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:19:07.920725270Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"babe9c8f-410e-592f-bd13-eaf0ffed2419","comment_uuid":"354d0666-4e2a-4403-82fa-78dd082741b2","author":"6ME5","content":"Systemic repair plan for L021: Every ordinary control read re-verifies the entire growing archive.\n\nOwning contract and implementation boundary: product_control/storage/replay.rs:14-75; storage/checkpoints.rs:165-210; storage.rs:186-214. Apply the change through the constructors, live callers, durable writer and restart reader for this boundary, not as an isolated constant increase.\n\nIntroduce verified incremental conversation projections keyed by journal head, with indexed historical reads and artifact integrity receipts. Routine queries and transitions should validate only the changed suffix and referenced changes; full archive verification belongs to resumable integrity work. Keep exact root comparison at projection publication and rebuild from the immutable history when a checkpoint is invalid.\n\nPreserve: canonical digest and schema identity, shared writer/reader admissibility, malformed-input rejection before allocation, exact causal ordering, actual provider/OS capability boundaries and preserved accepted historical evidence. Separate a physical allocation/page limit and a genuine authority or integrity check from a cumulative work allowance. Keep transient contention/capacity observable and recoverable under the existing logical task; do not discard accepted state or substitute a fresh session to get around it.\n\nCompatibility/migration: retain decoders and exact receipts for previously accepted records. If representation or lifecycle semantics change, introduce a versioned migration under exclusive ownership; verify a complete replacement frontier before atomic publication and keep the old recovery root until adoption is durable. Rebuild derived projections from authoritative evidence. Update all producers, consumers and invariants together; a rejected new operation must leave the predecessor usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: valid boundary values and values just beyond each synthetic cap, final wrapper/receipt growth, non-ASCII strings, arbitrarily split frames/pages, malformed or conflicting data, mixed-version decode and save/reopen round trips. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:19:07.750Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQALUCQSVXlXciX2l2Jo2sO91Aqb5a1xXkUlIBeUBWh9wWcR0WfRm+pInc71W99VrbDpWyHdepxbBVpnT9WF43gs="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2125,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:19:07.922748188Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"9690c819-b221-5295-9d01-63b716dcd8b3","title":"[L023] Synchronous global control ownership and run-state publication barriers","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L023.\n\n- `product_run/workbench.rs:298-321` holds one synchronous mutex for the whole ControlStore operation across every conversation. Current workbench queries at lines 229-245 call full replay directly; the async command path also performs synchronous control work at lines 157-175.\n- `product_run/execution.rs:22-103,106-151,340-347` holds the run registry's write lock across observation/finish work, durable persistence, checkpoint sealing, goal settlement, and reply publication. This can compose L021's full-history/file verification with blocking state/owner locks.\n- `execution.rs:25-27,113-115` drops future updates/terminal processing for a run already marked RecoveryRequired. Failed checkpoint sealing at line 133 and several persist_record calls discard the concrete error; public-reply publication failure sets persistence_failed and fails handoff.\n- Daily-driving effect: growing replay or storage work can delay unrelated UI queries/controls even without an elapsed timeout, and some failure causes are hidden. Lock order across other callers and recovery of the frozen state remain pending; no deadlock is asserted from this file alone.\n- `execution/launch.rs:96-112` explicitly sets ordinary-run `max_elapsed: None` and supplies retained resume/live-conversation handles. Its goal-clock wrapper and task recovery are separate pending paths.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQNhekjiACoOQdMviIxdDitjKCpjaGyjOqpI3gwTxfLD2OGGH/VZmgzDlyk2vY/KKFs2L+bgzvp7biQzaj2SMiAk="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2126,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:19:07.925052464Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"9690c819-b221-5295-9d01-63b716dcd8b3","comment_uuid":"87a14fc7-2edf-4c44-9ef7-e2a256f92a85","author":"6ME5","content":"Systemic repair plan for L023: Synchronous global control ownership and run-state publication barriers.\n\nOwning contract and implementation boundary: product_run/workbench.rs:298-321; product_run/execution.rs:22-103,106-151,340-347; execution.rs:25-27,113-115; execution/launch.rs:96-112. Apply the change through the constructors, live callers, durable writer and restart reader for this boundary, not as an isolated constant increase.\n\nSeparate per-conversation control ownership from the global run registry. Stage blocking replay, hashing and persistence outside registry locks; install a verified successor with an exact revision fence and a defined lock order. Record failed settlement as a resumable obligation with its original cause and continue accepting observations needed to reconcile it instead of freezing all later updates.\n\nPreserve: canonical digest and schema identity, shared writer/reader admissibility, malformed-input rejection before allocation, exact causal ordering, actual provider/OS capability boundaries and preserved accepted historical evidence. Separate a physical allocation/page limit and a genuine authority or integrity check from a cumulative work allowance. Keep transient contention/capacity observable and recoverable under the existing logical task; do not discard accepted state or substitute a fresh session to get around it.\n\nCompatibility/migration: retain decoders and exact receipts for previously accepted records. If representation or lifecycle semantics change, introduce a versioned migration under exclusive ownership; verify a complete replacement frontier before atomic publication and keep the old recovery root until adoption is durable. Rebuild derived projections from authoritative evidence. Update all producers, consumers and invariants together; a rejected new operation must leave the predecessor usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: valid boundary values and values just beyond each synthetic cap, final wrapper/receipt growth, non-ASCII strings, arbitrarily split frames/pages, malformed or conflicting data, mixed-version decode and save/reopen round trips. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:19:07.750Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQIynJXFKB83qhpS26dzSmh8hwLP8QTcCskmExhBBUgPNZu1rtM4TWHGFAJ/x8ITucsOZiBGhZrK2nbsxCXeraQU="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2127,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:19:07.927015328Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"d163455e-7704-5feb-9caf-62d8d5ad05c4","title":"[L024] SQLite native length and configurable database page ceilings","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L024.\n\n- `peritus-journal/src/sqlite/connection.rs:268-273` sets `SQLITE_LIMIT_LENGTH` to **32 MiB** and attached-database count to **zero**. The length limit is an additional hard database representation ceiling; attached-database restriction is a connection-security boundary.\n- `connection.rs:173-204` exposes `limit_storage_pages`, rejects zero/unrepresentable/below-current ceilings, and sets `max_page_count`; transactions requiring another page then fail with SQLITE_FULL. The method does not lower storage by deleting existing pages.\n- Default page-budget callers and real disk-pressure handling remain pending. A configurable page limit is not evidence that the default daemon imposes a small database quota; only the API/enforcement is established here.\n- Schema/store identity and WAL activation are admission requirements at lines 99-113,246-255,277-350. Unsupported generations require the migration owner rather than implicit reset.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQCxVbeYSsmwVyeI+XqlLNKAsH3HKkctqew2bzl05UwHGAU2kFJhT86CoEuEw1gkNujVC+JMJ/tlIyItZcCRu7Ao="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2128,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:19:07.929402366Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"d163455e-7704-5feb-9caf-62d8d5ad05c4","comment_uuid":"61c3c9e2-e191-4902-9300-f9b2941035a2","author":"6ME5","content":"Systemic repair plan for L024: SQLite native length and configurable database page ceilings.\n\nOwning contract and implementation boundary: peritus-journal/src/sqlite/connection.rs:268-273; connection.rs:173-204. Apply the change through the constructors, live callers, durable writer and restart reader for this boundary, not as an isolated constant increase.\n\nRepresent large state and bodies as paged rows/artifacts, leaving SQLite allocation bounds attached to each physical record. A selected disk quota must be explicit and adjustable, and SQLITE_FULL must retain the task and pending command for recovery. Preserve attached-database restrictions, WAL/store identity and explicit schema migration ownership.\n\nPreserve: canonical digest and schema identity, shared writer/reader admissibility, malformed-input rejection before allocation, exact causal ordering, actual provider/OS capability boundaries and preserved accepted historical evidence. Separate a physical allocation/page limit and a genuine authority or integrity check from a cumulative work allowance. Keep transient contention/capacity observable and recoverable under the existing logical task; do not discard accepted state or substitute a fresh session to get around it.\n\nCompatibility/migration: retain decoders and exact receipts for previously accepted records. If representation or lifecycle semantics change, introduce a versioned migration under exclusive ownership; verify a complete replacement frontier before atomic publication and keep the old recovery root until adoption is durable. Rebuild derived projections from authoritative evidence. Update all producers, consumers and invariants together; a rejected new operation must leave the predecessor usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: valid boundary values and values just beyond each synthetic cap, final wrapper/receipt growth, non-ASCII strings, arbitrarily split frames/pages, malformed or conflicting data, mixed-version decode and save/reopen round trips. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:19:07.750Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQMgmIthcYRe6Nh7E4MPk8gS3idxwZ4RnWg4JhmBy0VGL6mpbUTt/pbveW9irfr7vtbBGuCrnYzGp/9KskS30hAQ="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2129,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:19:07.931616646Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"a52ab344-8f4a-5166-8f03-f293bfdcf891","title":"[L025] Public activity windows and text truncation","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L025.\n\n- `peritus-daemon/src/product_run/interaction.rs:106-127,138-231,357-365` truncates activity text/detail to the imported `MAX_PRODUCT_ACTIVITY_BYTES`, chunks streamed text to that ceiling, and removes the oldest activity whenever the imported `MAX_PRODUCT_ACTIVITIES` window is full. The definitions are now read: `peritus-app-protocol/src/product/interaction.rs:75-78` sets **256 entries** and **8,192 bytes per text/detail field**. Its constructors independently reject larger fields or collections at lines 139-141 and 192-196.\n- Leading whitespace in a pending stream is discarded after 256 valid bytes at lines 174-176. Invalid UTF-8 is rejected explicitly rather than displayed. Persistence-failure presentation may evict another activity to insert its error at lines 253-302.\n- Effect: the interaction view cannot expose complete indefinitely growing activity/text history through this window. This is a presentation/history boundary; an execution-duration restriction is not established by these reads. Durable retention and client pagination remain pending.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQPqOcGN+5b1JaKwKiTZZ7okbHFyaojyB+KkZJWijbVtyifY5kCZyuRAqnYxEl8lFhMy7TjHFalYlp1MNoVZL5A0="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2130,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:19:07.933709219Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"a52ab344-8f4a-5166-8f03-f293bfdcf891","comment_uuid":"e42caacc-f37c-426d-9000-0019bbd2025f","author":"6ME5","content":"Systemic repair plan for L025: Public activity windows and text truncation.\n\nOwning contract and implementation boundary: peritus-daemon/src/product_run/interaction.rs:106-127,138-231,357-365; peritus-app-protocol/src/product/interaction.rs:75-78. Apply the change through the constructors, live callers, durable writer and restart reader for this boundary, not as an isolated constant increase.\n\nMake activities a durable sequence with paged historical retrieval and a bounded live view. Stream text as exact offset-addressed segments, report omissions and retain errors outside an evictable activity window. UTF-8 validation and presentation size limits must not change execution or discard authoritative progress.\n\nPreserve: durable logical session and run identity, exact command receipts, atomic snapshot/cursor binding, explicit authority, selected UI state, complete history retrieval and owned-effect reconciliation. Separate a physical allocation/page limit and a genuine authority or integrity check from a cumulative work allowance. Keep transient contention/capacity observable and recoverable under the existing logical task; do not discard accepted state or substitute a fresh session to get around it.\n\nCompatibility/migration: retain decoders and exact receipts for previously accepted records. If representation or lifecycle semantics change, introduce a versioned migration under exclusive ownership; verify a complete replacement frontier before atomic publication and keep the old recovery root until adoption is durable. Rebuild derived projections from authoritative evidence. Update all producers, consumers and invariants together; a rejected new operation must leave the predecessor usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: large histories and non-ASCII fields, queue/connection pressure, delayed acknowledgements, subscription gaps, disconnect/reconnect and daemon restart, proving snapshot recovery, preserved selection/context, responsive controls and no duplicate command. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:19:07.750Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQL56L24hPksUgCvAKcTwIrciO/rYm6UnXYwqOzix8kM6UpBc3cvwzwFdxFbX3vb7Qa/Sgk3pIT6sea9pzxNy7w8="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2131,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:19:07.935861741Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"f7e08b0a-c0fd-5f5a-85bd-5c585b3330d8","title":"[L026] Governance failures become persistent execution/admission barriers","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L026.\n\n- `product_run/interaction/live.rs:26-111` converts control-store/read errors into governing-context stop text, an empty reference-authority context, revision `u64::MAX`, protection of the entire workspace, and no host permissions. The error's original class is not retained by several of these fallback return values.\n- Lines 153-207 explicitly reject provider requests and input incorporation after the shared `persistence_failed` flag is set. Tool admission at lines 247-276 yields when the supplied input generation differs from durable state. Goal admission at lines 373-380 stops on Paused or Inactive.\n- `interaction.rs:235-251` uses `pending_record_input(record).unwrap_or(false)`, so an input-inspection error can become an absence of pending input. These are fail-closed authority/durability choices; their recovery and user-actionability need caller inspection before claiming a permanent lockup.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQGKPdwv9ivIEVB7SuByCUXHewS6NU2PjAInr7LSLkyRy4cl7FmN5FEtIJjye7QRDAaSYYkNQYJ5Ei8kk7CxxrAE="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2132,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:19:07.938176909Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"f7e08b0a-c0fd-5f5a-85bd-5c585b3330d8","comment_uuid":"4d7e1a23-58d0-4776-9fa2-c5b38adf9e61","author":"6ME5","content":"Systemic repair plan for L026: Governance failures become persistent execution/admission barriers.\n\nOwning contract and implementation boundary: product_run/interaction/live.rs:26-111; interaction.rs:235-251. Apply the change through the constructors, live callers, durable writer and restart reader for this boundary, not as an isolated constant increase.\n\nReplace fabricated revision/permission/context fallbacks with a typed GoverningStateUnavailable condition carrying the retained authoritative revision and recovery obligation. Suspend only effects that require unavailable authority, keep observations and controls responsive, and reconcile the same context after storage recovers. Distinguish inspection failure from an actual absence of pending input.\n\nPreserve: committed command/event identity, exact causal and digest roots, exclusive ownership, atomic publication, reference-safe artifact retention and verified recovery from the last durable frontier. Separate a physical allocation/page limit and a genuine authority or integrity check from a cumulative work allowance. Keep transient contention/capacity observable and recoverable under the existing logical task; do not discard accepted state or substitute a fresh session to get around it.\n\nCompatibility/migration: retain decoders and exact receipts for previously accepted records. If representation or lifecycle semantics change, introduce a versioned migration under exclusive ownership; verify a complete replacement frontier before atomic publication and keep the old recovery root until adoption is durable. Rebuild derived projections from authoritative evidence. Update all producers, consumers and invariants together; a rejected new operation must leave the predecessor usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: history beyond the reported count/byte boundaries, lock contention lasting beyond the old patience window, lost commit acknowledgements followed by later progress, torn uncommitted tails and true committed corruption, then reopen and resolve exact historical receipts. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:19:07.750Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQByi45CjTPuoyGd15Oz54FXe3tshT/AxKG705kdRJYA5svZ20WxgS14BmP8113tyxCNV8M9NTCOLCdzOiOBKeAQ="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2133,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:19:07.940808423Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"2f289851-d486-51e3-ab03-f37bc338e6e7","title":"[L027] Governed live execution disables semantic compaction","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L027.\n\n- `product_run/interaction/live.rs:150-152` unconditionally returns `false` from `allows_semantic_compaction` for this live conversation port.\n- Potential daily-driving effect: a growing governed conversation cannot use this automatic semantic-compaction capability. `peritus-agent/src/developer/execution.rs:94-127` now verifies this disables the **legacy semantic-compaction path** only when no local context port is in use. With a local port, context assembly runs instead; `local_context/port.rs:194-202` separately performs local compaction/checkpoint work. Explicit compaction and local capacity/recovery implementations remain pending. This declaration alone does not prove that all forms of compaction are disabled.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQFbDBYiezsoY29xLRld/J9dgdYzlGBR6KkIcF9nTFQGoSh52jaf1O/viR4Blv1bFzsOre9JD2jilxLV/r/Tl1gQ="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2134,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:19:07.943005859Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"2f289851-d486-51e3-ab03-f37bc338e6e7","comment_uuid":"d464a86d-e9fe-4a4c-811b-c02bbfec6288","author":"6ME5","content":"Systemic repair plan for L027: Governed live execution disables semantic compaction.\n\nOwning contract and implementation boundary: product_run/interaction/live.rs:150-152; peritus-agent/src/developer/execution.rs:94-127; local_context/port.rs:194-202. Apply the change through the constructors, live callers, durable writer and restart reader for this boundary, not as an isolated constant increase.\n\nGive governed conversations a host-owned compaction operation that preserves governing inputs, pending protocol obligations and exact archived lineage. Select a bounded prompt frontier independently of the complete conversation history; capability negotiation must state which local or legacy compactor owns it. Compaction failure should retain a recoverable selection state under the same context.\n\nPreserve: governing inputs, complete pending tool protocol pairs, exact source/lineage references, explicit permissions, unresolved effect truth and task-role/native-provider identity. Separate a physical allocation/page limit and a genuine authority or integrity check from a cumulative work allowance. Keep transient contention/capacity observable and recoverable under the existing logical task; do not discard accepted state or substitute a fresh session to get around it.\n\nCompatibility/migration: retain decoders and exact receipts for previously accepted records. If representation or lifecycle semantics change, introduce a versioned migration under exclusive ownership; verify a complete replacement frontier before atomic publication and keep the old recovery root until adoption is durable. Rebuild derived projections from authoritative evidence. Update all producers, consumers and invariants together; a rejected new operation must leave the predecessor usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: long productive read/write sessions through repeated compaction and segment boundaries, source/dependency changes, non-ASCII and large evidence, interrupted checkpoint publication, then reopen the same lineage and prove that valid grounding is reused and stale targets are reread. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:19:07.750Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQF8xO4KLXWnc/9Rybc1IREQbL0DvVap9Y1GzmORQ1HO3703xYiFcZC+khPVnUCJcG7pGJ3jViei+XEMEN9wBLw0="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2135,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:19:07.945268189Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"7c170f63-9de4-5493-ba0b-7863d714a6da","title":"[L028] Accounting failures cancel the active run","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L028.\n\n- `product_run/execution/goal.rs:59-96` polls durable goal progress after an initial 100 ms and then at 1,000 ms intervals while accounting remains active. These are polling cadences, not elapsed execution deadlines.\n- Any error from `observe_goal_clock` cancels both the run flag and provider cancellation and stops accounting. Lines 98-108 set `persistence_failed` and retain a goal-progress persistence error. A final observation failure records the error while returning the original execution result.\n- Structural coupling: an accounting storage failure can stop otherwise progressing model/tool work, and the resulting shared failure flag blocks subsequent admission (L026). `product_control/goal.rs:158-200,292-335` confirms that each governed progress update loads the execution record, persists a host operation, and loads state again; storage errors propagate to this cancellation path. Its reservations admit ordinary execution with no goal at lines 28-30 and 99-101. Pure goal-transition budget enforcement remains pending. Whether SQLite's 250 ms contention deadline (L019) reaches this path requires those remaining reads.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQCoOLCsXOy8kkS7zTvZS2FYi7fUKpBxEOZT/E2M5