predecessor usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: valid boundary values and values just beyond each synthetic cap, final wrapper/receipt growth, non-ASCII strings, arbitrarily split frames/pages, malformed or conflicting data, mixed-version decode and save/reopen round trips. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:19:07.750Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQNvqrr941ua/Y0/A+8T/3hwci8LwTlDEBrNAUYQYF9Jxm0WZpJ4YJX07KWDadbvMfG7TosMGAYJpncsiOvTOOgg="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2149,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:19:07.975347828Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"c66cf3d1-2096-5857-9a4c-cfd0a3379cc1","title":"[L035] Tool writes and completed-command receipts impose a tighter file ceiling","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L035.\n\n- `peritus-product-runner/src/developer_tools/executor.rs:27` defines **2 MiB per file**. `executor/effects.rs:203-208,234-253` rejects larger direct writes and larger patched final files. `checkpoint_observer.rs:129-170` repeats those checks during preflight.\n- `checkpoint_observer.rs:333-355` reads the completed command's changed scoped file and rejects its receipt above **2 MiB**, even after the command succeeded. This ceiling is tighter than the checkpoint's 8 MiB bound (L003) and independently blocks artifact-producing commands.\n- Structural issue: workspace state, file-edit payload, checkpoint capture, and post-command effect evidence have different capacities. A command can pass preflight under one capacity and fail durable settlement under another. Its later recovery/settlement caller remains pending.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQHlHSPLdPZu3XTCslOyuYdGRakkbiUwyAjAb8zhMJvsTkAwx+D4aV8lvggH8ZNgTk3XlVqQ4GSUq4VxyZKjwTQM="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2150,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:19:07.977674915Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"c66cf3d1-2096-5857-9a4c-cfd0a3379cc1","comment_uuid":"14b5014b-a12f-4f23-8eb3-9d773a96df02","author":"6ME5","content":"Systemic repair plan for L035: Tool writes and completed-command receipts impose a tighter file ceiling.\n\nOwning contract and implementation boundary: peritus-product-runner/src/developer_tools/executor.rs:27; executor/effects.rs:203-208,234-253; checkpoint_observer.rs:129-170; checkpoint_observer.rs:333-355. Apply the change through the constructors, live callers, durable writer and restart reader for this boundary, not as an isolated constant increase.\n\nUse one artifact-backed effect evidence contract across direct writes, patches, checkpoint capture and completed commands. Stream large file bodies and record their exact digests; preflight must establish durable settlement capacity before mutation. A completed command must settle its actual outcome even if a later display cannot inline its generated file.\n\nPreserve: committed command/event identity, exact causal and digest roots, exclusive ownership, atomic publication, reference-safe artifact retention and verified recovery from the last durable frontier. Separate a physical allocation/page limit and a genuine authority or integrity check from a cumulative work allowance. Keep transient contention/capacity observable and recoverable under the existing logical task; do not discard accepted state or substitute a fresh session to get around it.\n\nCompatibility/migration: retain decoders and exact receipts for previously accepted records. If representation or lifecycle semantics change, introduce a versioned migration under exclusive ownership; verify a complete replacement frontier before atomic publication and keep the old recovery root until adoption is durable. Rebuild derived projections from authoritative evidence. Update all producers, consumers and invariants together; a rejected new operation must leave the predecessor usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: history beyond the reported count/byte boundaries, lock contention lasting beyond the old patience window, lost commit acknowledgements followed by later progress, torn uncommitted tails and true committed corruption, then reopen and resolve exact historical receipts. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:19:07.750Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQBMqb7L4hCretNubgJdl+7zl7ZcYFDGrPEDd1Gq5XOdYBb1wWzOHHQEqnEB5sCqDlQL+gzpZdKeqksV8Vt7zvgg="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2151,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:19:07.980257654Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"20da7435-7f36-5874-9128-008c9e48a723","title":"[L036] Command preflight checkpoints every enrolled file","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L036.\n\n- `executor.rs:243-257` calls `prepare_effect_checkpoint` before dispatching the command. `executor/checkpoint_observer.rs:213-230` reads every current in-place scope path and invokes the pre-mutation observer for each, rejecting directory targets and scope changes.\n- Combined with the daemon live hook (L003), a build/verification command is refused when an enrolled file cannot be checkpointed, even before its actual mutation set is known. `execution/checkpoint.rs:89-133` now verifies forwarding into the daemon live ConversationView; `turn.rs:280-291` installs this observer on writer/fixer tools. The full precommand chain is verified.\n- Post-effect receipt recovery at lines 64-107 requires exact unchanged write/patch/delete results; reappearance or divergent contents require reconciliation. These effect-identity fences are recorded separately from the size limits.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQGzRi+j9MsIUGM03xyPzInSpaBgzpdW/2DxF3L8OqNnWRWCuHWrd4t1cYlESjP6ewS5Ez0IVPYWj+qnN12HevQA="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2152,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:19:07.982666837Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"20da7435-7f36-5874-9128-008c9e48a723","comment_uuid":"b532ed22-2294-436a-92f3-4d5ea1e0bff9","author":"6ME5","content":"Systemic repair plan for L036: Command preflight checkpoints every enrolled file.\n\nOwning contract and implementation boundary: executor.rs:243-257; executor/checkpoint_observer.rs:213-230; execution/checkpoint.rs:89-133; turn.rs:280-291. Apply the change through the constructors, live callers, durable writer and restart reader for this boundary, not as an isolated constant increase.\n\nSeparate the task scope from the command mutation footprint. Capture a durable baseline for authorized writable paths using streamed artifact snapshots, and derive post-command changes against that baseline; observational commands should not require unrelated files to fit an edit payload. Preserve confinement, exact changed-path evidence and before-mutation recoverability for every possible authorized write.\n\nPreserve: exact snapshot/preimage identity, protected paths, ancestor and symlink safety, writable-fork coverage, conflict detection, one logical restore transaction and exact effect receipts. Separate a physical allocation/page limit and a genuine authority or integrity check from a cumulative work allowance. Keep transient contention/capacity observable and recoverable under the existing logical task; do not discard accepted state or substitute a fresh session to get around it.\n\nCompatibility/migration: retain decoders and exact receipts for previously accepted records. If representation or lifecycle semantics change, introduce a versioned migration under exclusive ownership; verify a complete replacement frontier before atomic publication and keep the old recovery root until adoption is durable. Rebuild derived projections from authoritative evidence. Update all producers, consumers and invariants together; a rejected new operation must leave the predecessor usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: large-file and many-path capture/restore, divergent preimage rejection, interrupted staging/publication/restore, then reopen and continue the same conversation with an exact restored workspace. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:19:07.750Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQNQ/eMFjIYo1Od3Iznu6aNXygSao5KdBLCwrGhgfOAJ/RL2ytLZ3QSG8U1vpIRsckucCsa6VvUc08NXPkblPTgU="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2153,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:19:07.985155844Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"a8d5a057-130e-5027-b927-00bba4f5c0fd","title":"[L037] Selected horizons synthesize a completion reserve and clamp command execution","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L037.\n\n- `developer_tools/command_budget.rs:9,56-87,96-103` reserves **one fifth of the selected horizon**, at least one second for a whole-second horizon, at most **300 seconds**, and no more than the horizon. Remaining command time is floored to whole seconds after subtracting that reserve.\n- It clamps a requested timeout, assigns the remaining allowance when the command has no requested timeout, and refuses to start when zero remains. `executor/command.rs:42-44,67-69,167-188` enforces this allowance. `None` horizon has no reserve and preserves the optional requested timeout.\n- Explicit `timeout_seconds` must be positive and at most **u64::MAX / 1,000** for millisecond representation. Terminal dimensions are **1..65,535** at command start (defaults 24×80) and **0..65,535** at resize; downstream validation remains pending.\n- Daily-driving status: ordinary daemon launch currently has no run horizon; other horizon callers are pending. This reserve is an additional policy deadline inside any selected horizon, and timeout recovery text discourages an equivalent longer retry at `command.rs:200-206`.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQMx9k/WMBhyUk4M/o13cJ+dgmZQWk+tzqJbb8ktT23WFxcurPGSHqXCWEd6cmN17GAfJsyT9cUVmRsTHCvL9LQ8="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2154,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:19:07.987899875Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"a8d5a057-130e-5027-b927-00bba4f5c0fd","comment_uuid":"1a7a67a3-4c03-4926-a55a-ba32a1094ac5","author":"6ME5","content":"Systemic repair plan for L037: Selected horizons synthesize a completion reserve and clamp command execution.\n\nOwning contract and implementation boundary: developer_tools/command_budget.rs:9,56-87,96-103; executor/command.rs:42-44,67-69,167-188; command.rs:200-206. Apply the change through the constructors, live callers, durable writer and restart reader for this boundary, not as an isolated constant increase.\n\nRemove synthetic fractions reserved from an explicitly selected horizon. Model active execution and finalization as distinct owned states with durable completion obligations; only the actual requested command/task deadline may end execution. Preserve positive representable explicit timeouts and terminal dimensions, and report the original stop cause without discouraging a legitimate recovered retry.\n\nPreserve: canonical digest and schema identity, shared writer/reader admissibility, malformed-input rejection before allocation, exact causal ordering, actual provider/OS capability boundaries and preserved accepted historical evidence. Separate a physical allocation/page limit and a genuine authority or integrity check from a cumulative work allowance. Keep transient contention/capacity observable and recoverable under the existing logical task; do not discard accepted state or substitute a fresh session to get around it.\n\nCompatibility/migration: retain decoders and exact receipts for previously accepted records. If representation or lifecycle semantics change, introduce a versioned migration under exclusive ownership; verify a complete replacement frontier before atomic publication and keep the old recovery root until adoption is durable. Rebuild derived projections from authoritative evidence. Update all producers, consumers and invariants together; a rejected new operation must leave the predecessor usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: valid boundary values and values just beyond each synthetic cap, final wrapper/receipt growth, non-ASCII strings, arbitrarily split frames/pages, malformed or conflicting data, mixed-version decode and save/reopen round trips. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:19:07.750Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQLxIz9VjseTUKbjjA2/xAjK9vKyIC2y3QQhzKLoW1AdeII3IeH8N75REC2vh7MjMDh0SRTa5R9DxavELQrx38g0="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2155,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:19:07.990305774Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"5879176d-05f1-5856-b26f-5722804eff38","title":"[L038] Inspection-loop feedback has a finite observation window and does not enforce convergence","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L038.\n\n- `executor.rs:28-30` and `executor/effects.rs:120-159` issue feedback after **12 tools without delivery progress**, at most **two nudges** until a qualifying workspace mutation or successful declared external effect resets them. Read-only modes bypass this delivery-progress check.\n- `executor/inspection_progress.rs:9-10,50-59,79-108` retains **16 distinct inspection fingerprints** and warns on the first identical repeat still visible to the model. It clears/reset state on qualifying mutation or new evidence; evidence no longer visible can be reread without a repeat warning.\n- Effect: these numbers bound detection/feedback, not task execution. The code returns warnings and continues; it supplies no durable stage convergence rule. A changing or sufficiently wide inspection loop can evade exact-repeat feedback. Model-loop response and retained-stage behavior remain pending.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQLAJ6DTcX1P30tSN/Pjn1TbO7h50DmgN0ppLZLOdwQuuny1Bs/ldUj65VFnUMpGpgK5xJI2RA0I/r8J/AEzCsQs="}
