iants together; a rejected new operation must leave the predecessor usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: valid boundary values and values just beyond each synthetic cap, final wrapper/receipt growth, non-ASCII strings, arbitrarily split frames/pages, malformed or conflicting data, mixed-version decode and save/reopen round trips. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:19:07.750Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQLzCRp1B6aseq8W4gy3Sgh3Vl0XlQpKtFnQmVfnfBuAUJ14dV5Dv0X5LNudNPRL07ZWWoV7meiLAxLGC+NWOBwE="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2157,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:19:07.994569796Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"c1bb97dc-b885-5cac-a735-a9b4f95e10ec","title":"[L039] Tool authority and mode gates can suppress process work","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L039.\n\n- `developer_tools/executor.rs:142-155,200-239` requires Read+Write+Process for command start/stdin/resize/signal, even if a particular requested command is observational. Owned command polling/recovery/cancel remain available after permission revocation.\n- Read-only mode permits only list/search/read; it rejects every process/mutation tool before effect dispatch. Access policy and grounding add separate task-scope restrictions. These are explicit authority boundaries, not counted as artificial deadlines, but their effect on review/planning verification is recorded.\n- Actual user permission defaults, mode selection, protected-path refresh, and usable recovery from revoked/failed control state remain pending.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQI+KXfb7J9/M4IvzyCINYVwDPeMYmrBPPDalWqB1eUjt5mIopgPilgLtpu4l1ea2OvYhOR2siK/jgrO5p6126As="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2158,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:19:07.996686211Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"c1bb97dc-b885-5cac-a735-a9b4f95e10ec","comment_uuid":"acb5d456-0ef5-487b-b616-d2784cfe06f7","author":"6ME5","content":"Systemic repair plan for L039: Tool authority and mode gates can suppress process work.\n\nOwning contract and implementation boundary: developer_tools/executor.rs:142-155,200-239. Apply the change through the constructors, live callers, durable writer and restart reader for this boundary, not as an isolated constant increase.\n\nSeparate observational process authority, mutation authority and owned-process control capabilities. Admit local verification when the selected backend can enforce its declared read-only footprint; retain cancellation and reconciliation capabilities after permission revocation. Derive mode admission from durable explicit permissions and backend capabilities rather than granting blanket process writes.\n\nPreserve: exact process birth/tree identity, confined authority, one-use dispatch receipts, monotonic cancel intent, truthful terminal/ownership settlement, complete output accounting and platform OS constraints. Separate a physical allocation/page limit and a genuine authority or integrity check from a cumulative work allowance. Keep transient contention/capacity observable and recoverable under the existing logical task; do not discard accepted state or substitute a fresh session to get around it.\n\nCompatibility/migration: retain decoders and exact receipts for previously accepted records. If representation or lifecycle semantics change, introduce a versioned migration under exclusive ownership; verify a complete replacement frontier before atomic publication and keep the old recovery root until adoption is durable. Rebuild derived projections from authoritative evidence. Update all producers, consumers and invariants together; a rejected new operation must leave the predecessor usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: long-running commands, output and stdin pressure, stalled helper/input readers, control-queue saturation, late start/exit races, parent loss and restart, proving cancellation responsiveness, no PID-reuse adoption and no duplicate process dispatch. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:19:07.750Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQC2xFEzKxIlUeJW54yTWYZRU5o2GqJWPFKPKZbDHiYndlGwlH11b8u06WcH2Gw7K5pwXYpwvp0dTRYa1v9ktlQE="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2159,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:19:07.998796203Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"04ce8b3a-f2ae-5746-910e-a9ce1f1b7c7a","title":"[L040] Build concurrency heuristic is enforced as an execution ceiling","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L040.\n\n- `developer_tools/resources.rs:10-11,23-33` estimates **2 GiB per build job** and clamps recommended parallelism to **1..8**, regardless of a larger usable host. It samples available CPU/cgroup and memory once when the tool executor is constructed.\n- Lines 45-61 reject recognized cargo/cmake/make/gmake/ninja/ninja-build job flags above that recommendation. Bare `-j`/`--jobs` is treated as `usize::MAX` when no integer follows, while CMake's bare `--parallel` can return no requested value (lines 82-107).\n- Lines 66-78 inject concurrency environment defaults across languages; **CARGO_BUILD_JOBS is separately capped at 2**. `executor/command.rs:158` calls authorization before any command starts and passes these bindings into the runtime.\n- Daily-driving effect: a heuristic recommendation becomes a hard refusal even when the user/host could safely run more workers. Real OS/cgroup limits and the added fixed/heuristic policy are distinct. Runtime environment merge/override behavior remains pending.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQIn03jL/x6UAZf3QMzALjSLP7F9Q+kTwRGwUqIp71M6hiYUNfuD64wd8rLiYCee8N7pkgQANRVwLooVZw5BtDgA="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2160,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:19:08.000867996Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"04ce8b3a-f2ae-5746-910e-a9ce1f1b7c7a","comment_uuid":"7d51a961-30c0-44c7-8231-34f7e20555d4","author":"6ME5","content":"Systemic repair plan for L040: Build concurrency heuristic is enforced as an execution ceiling.\n\nOwning contract and implementation boundary: developer_tools/resources.rs:10-11,23-33; executor/command.rs:158. Apply the change through the constructors, live callers, durable writer and restart reader for this boundary, not as an isolated constant increase.\n\nMake resource-derived parallelism advisory and expose explicit user overrides within actual OS/cgroup capacity. Remove fixed language-specific job refusals and the independent Cargo cap; refresh resource evidence when launching instead of binding it once per executor. Use consistent command flag parsing and report real resource exhaustion as a recoverable capacity condition.\n\nPreserve: canonical digest and schema identity, shared writer/reader admissibility, malformed-input rejection before allocation, exact causal ordering, actual provider/OS capability boundaries and preserved accepted historical evidence. Separate a physical allocation/page limit and a genuine authority or integrity check from a cumulative work allowance. Keep transient contention/capacity observable and recoverable under the existing logical task; do not discard accepted state or substitute a fresh session to get around it.\n\nCompatibility/migration: retain decoders and exact receipts for previously accepted records. If representation or lifecycle semantics change, introduce a versioned migration under exclusive ownership; verify a complete replacement frontier before atomic publication and keep the old recovery root until adoption is durable. Rebuild derived projections from authoritative evidence. Update all producers, consumers and invariants together; a rejected new operation must leave the predecessor usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: valid boundary values and values just beyond each synthetic cap, final wrapper/receipt growth, non-ASCII strings, arbitrarily split frames/pages, malformed or conflicting data, mixed-version decode and save/reopen round trips. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:19:07.750Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQPWXP1Yzxn6WLrKhSIBOJsMXw8NLrtM2tAmyhPhO4yRXbVTytqnOTyODeiQFy3iG6VL4Fia6v8WTT7MM2Y6alAs="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2161,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:19:08.002823635Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"a4ae29fd-a719-55d1-bbe7-36f56ecfc1e6","title":"[L041] Workspace inspection truncates or omits evidence","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L041.\n\n- `developer_tools/inspection.rs:31-68` lists at default depth **3**, clamped to **1..12**, and stops after **2,000 entries** with `truncated=true`. The response provides no continuation cursor in this file; callers can target narrower paths. Child errors are skipped.\n- Search at lines 99,127-150 returns default **200**, at most **1,000 matches**, silently skips files above **2 MiB**, unsupported/non-UTF-8 content and child I/O errors, and stops with `truncated=true` at its result ceiling.\n- Read at lines 168-185 defaults to **500 lines** and rejects an entire file above 2 MiB unless a line range was explicit. Selected individual line accumulation above **2 MiB** fails at lines 220-224. Multiple line output can grow before a separate `effect::limit` truncates it; `effect.rs:9,49-54` now verifies the separate **512 KiB output-prefix cap plus a truncation marker**; read replies retain the requested line interval despite that cut.\n- Effect: broad grounding can omit relevant files/content. Read replies retain requested start/end fields even after output truncation rather than the exact last displayed line in this function. Explicit pagination/narrowing can help, but this implementation does not establish full coverage from one successful observation.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1Y