{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2175,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:19:08.032728602Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"bb806f1b-b137-562e-88e7-fa90ea2afc70","title":"[L048] File ownership can require a new run for deletion","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L048.\n\n- `developer_tools/ownership.rs:101-111` refuses removal of a file outside the starting baseline/direct creation/observed command creation sets and tells the user to start a new run explicitly requesting deletion. Direct-folder reads enroll exact file ownership at lines 46-50.\n- Baseline tree enumeration at lines 151-176 skips ignored directories and child errors, while untracked Git paths that are non-UTF-8 are skipped at lines 139-146. These omissions affect ownership/admission, even though no numeric inventory cap appears here.\n- This is an authority/evidence restriction rather than a session expiry timer. Whether durable resumed ownership and explicit same-session user authorization can resolve it remains pending.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQAny62TXfKEnob3dlQzxdO3VS7uJh9XrOROT4qxMO/3ivIY3u2Sbi+QFBbH5A/iCQ0xqcungwl7zGwtjZmk5mQ0="}
