{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2187,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:19:08.058963250Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"b88fd5a4-5453-5cbb-a8f8-0548bd3a105c","title":"[L054] Selected run horizons also impose a separate phase-finalization reserve","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L054.\n\n- `peritus-product-runner/src/execution/deadline.rs:7-8,21-22,25-57` reserves **one tenth of the selected horizon**, clamped between **one second and 60 seconds**, each capped by the horizon. It subtracts this from active time and refuses Design/Writer/Reviewer/Fixer phase admission when remaining time is at or below the reserve.\n- This differs from the command completion reserve (one fifth/up to 300 seconds, L037); one user-selected horizon therefore feeds multiple independent derived cutoffs. `None` horizon paired with `None` remaining admits work without this reserve. Mismatched Some/None states fail closed.\n- Actual phase/driver caller enforcement is pending. Conversation execution at `execution/conversation.rs:77-80,116-123` only wraps a selected remaining horizon in tokio::timeout; no wrapper is applied when absent.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQOKn/3/DyW5E67unzxepuVoJoAmC8N2gOpwbwxAL/kIDteqTVsuL74pvLNq1r8RsM/DYN0iX/iojzc3YD4T2Dgs="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2188,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:19:08.061203603Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"b88fd5a4-5453-5cbb-a8f8-0548bd3a105c","comment_uuid":"d4ab0c08-ea75-47bd-b3e1-b4eb1fa4a95e","author":"6ME5","content":"Systemic repair plan for L054: Selected run horizons also impose a separate phase-finalization reserve.\n\nOwning contract and implementation boundary: peritus-product-runner/src/execution/deadline.rs:7-8,21-22,25-57; execution/conversation.rs:77-80,116-123. Apply the change through the constructors, live callers, durable writer and restart reader for this boundary, not as an isolated constant increase.\n\nRemove the extra phase-finalization reserve derived from a selected horizon. Admit phases against the actual explicit user deadline and model finalization as durable settlement of already owned effects. Centralize horizon interpretation so phases and command tools cannot impose competing earlier cutoffs.\n\nPreserve: canonical digest and schema identity, shared writer/reader admissibility, malformed-input rejection before allocation, exact causal ordering, actual provider/OS capability boundaries and preserved accepted historical evidence. Separate a physical allocation/page limit and a genuine authority or integrity check from a cumulative work allowance. Keep transient contention/capacity observable and recoverable under the existing logical task; do not discard accepted state or substitute a fresh session to get around it.\n\nCompatibility/migration: retain decoders and exact receipts for previously accepted records. If representation or lifecycle semantics change, introduce a versioned migration under exclusive ownership; verify a complete replacement frontier before atomic publication and keep the old recovery root until adoption is durable. Rebuild derived projections from authoritative evidence. Update all producers, consumers and invariants together; a rejected new operation must leave the predecessor usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: valid boundary values and values just beyond each synthetic cap, final wrapper/receipt growth, non-ASCII strings, arbitrarily split frames/pages, malformed or conflicting data, mixed-version decode and save/reopen round trips. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:19:07.750Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQIkM7Z5bfSvEuwKraNOn5Vgm44OpeX/yzce/r30FXEpJR+nPeFXb6+QcFWkWwo8Rovv5eYdrdHmKfH+HWDApzwI="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2189,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:19:08.063469944Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"bfd6c0f6-a617-567b-9d1c-2841490f8913","title":"[L055] Conversation request identity narrows the durable revision range","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L055.\n\n- `execution/conversation.rs:245-252` converts the durable `u64` conversation revision to `u32` when building its request prefix and rejects overflow. Thus revisions above **4,294,967,295** cannot enter this conversation path even though the governing port exposes `u64` revisions.\n- This is a representation mismatch, not a plausible near-term elapsed deadline. The full audit records it rather than silently overlooking a remote-range boundary.\n- Ordinary conversation tools do **not** delegate the underlying workspace grounding required-tool/completion blockers (`conversation/tools.rs:36-77`), allowing direct answers without source tools. Do not generalize writer/fixer grounding barriers to every conversational answer; segment policy text still tells the model to re-ground (`conversation.rs:236-239`).\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQN6z7swLcSTgnw66Q8Ql8jlIQjAurLRnE+rChHsebo1+tX8A0GmcSdN2TnQ6LJRXDMFilRQdTGykyTatAQDjeAM="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2190,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:19:08.065574046Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"bfd6c0f6-a617-567b-9d1c-2841490f8913","comment_uuid":"bedba646-5474-44c6-aecd-c82ab95aca47","author":"6ME5","content":"Systemic repair plan for L055: Conversation request identity narrows the durable revision range.\n\nOwning contract and implementation boundary: execution/conversation.rs:245-252; conversation/tools.rs:36-77; conversation.rs:236-239. Apply the change through the constructors, live callers, durable writer and restart reader for this boundary, not as an isolated constant increase.\n\nCarry the complete durable revision type through conversation request identity. Use a versioned full-width or epoch-plus-offset identity without lossy u64-to-u32 conversion, with old IDs retained for exact retry lookup. Keep ordinary conversational answers separate from writer mutation grounding requirements.\n\nPreserve: committed command/event identity, exact causal and digest roots, exclusive ownership, atomic publication, reference-safe artifact retention and verified recovery from the last durable frontier. Separate a physical allocation/page limit and a genuine authority or integrity check from a cumulative work allowance. Keep transient contention/capacity observable and recoverable under the existing logical task; do not discard accepted state or substitute a fresh session to get around it.\n\nCompatibility/migration: retain decoders and exact receipts for previously accepted records. If representation or lifecycle semantics change, introduce a versioned migration under exclusive ownership; verify a complete replacement frontier before atomic publication and keep the old recovery root until adoption is durable. Rebuild derived projections from authoritative evidence. Update all producers, consumers and invariants together; a rejected new operation must leave the predecessor usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: history beyond the reported count/byte boundaries, lock contention lasting beyond the old patience window, lost commit acknowledgements followed by later progress, torn uncommitted tails and true committed corruption, then reopen and resolve exact historical receipts. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:19:07.750Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQCaxrV1M5RQnnvYF97aB+5a4GlBgArzonB8x2M2tjzeLoKr+XRIjIgIBF/NQYbAxWG67yIni4iQNE4u55RY3kAI="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2191,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:19:08.067749262Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"feecb16a-18c3-5277-a730-7cfa7f4a9f9a","title":"[L056] Local-memory ownership has a separate 250 ms acquisition deadline","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L056.\n\n- `peritus-product-runner/src/local_context/storage.rs:178-190` retries the lineage owner file lock only while elapsed time is below **250 ms**, sleeping **5 ms** between attempts. It then returns “lineage already has an owner or cannot be locked,” without preserving the original lock error class.\n- The comment accounts for brief inherited descriptors during process fork. A still-live owner is an exclusive-writer constraint; the fixed 250 ms patience limit is an added deadline and can turn temporary fork/owner handoff contention into context admission failure.\n- Local memory also sets its SQLite busy timeout to **250 ms** at lines 80-85, separately from the control-store instance in L019. Caller failure propagates as a context error rather than silently choosing a fresh memory store (`local_context/driver.rs`, L043/L049).\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQJazQZm/h75IufMhMvPG3xZB1sRlgrbFSlg6f62KbkvZqIYtgFSANDl7IxCqy4IPDrznCkc6qlVU8BLgtBSZXgA="}
