econcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: long productive read/write sessions through repeated compaction and segment boundaries, source/dependency changes, non-ASCII and large evidence, interrupted checkpoint publication, then reopen the same lineage and prove that valid grounding is reused and stale targets are reread. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:19:07.750Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQIAvZM2hLj2T6cM908HIkRik9HzmwLRUqV1RTqGJbvvGD/6kPj/cfKaOl8sLxN/0/bYa4wWtWUgp4w2c2rTQngc="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2193,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:19:08.071691854Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"3a48b567-5e09-57c7-9238-f1c99deeb0cc","title":"[L057] Local context archive, record, and artifact storage capacities","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L057.\n\n- `local_context/storage.rs:30,86-90,133-175` configures **64 MiB per artifact** and a **1 GiB total artifact-store quota**; store/read reject larger objects. `peritus-artifact-store/src/store.rs:75-91,229-239` and `quota.rs:74-85` now verify quota enforcement: a new digest reserves its expected bytes and rejects used-plus-reserved growth beyond the configured total. Existing digests reserve zero. Reclamation/reference catalog and database option interactions remain pending full reads.\n- `local_context/record.rs:169-186` independently rejects canonical serialized host records above **32 MiB**. Growing transcript/source-index/checkpoint values use this serializer; local event frames use the production codec (**16 MiB**, L009) at `storage.rs:110-123`. `local_context/storage/append.rs:22-26` now verifies **each host event payload is framed directly with the 16 MiB production codec**, lower than its 32 MiB serializer admission. Checkpoint publication also inherits the 16 MiB StateInstall ceiling and its atomic artifact dependency list inherits 4,096 (L020). Growing index/state artifact layouts remain pending.\n- `record.rs:69-80` limits archived tool call IDs to **256 bytes** and tool names to **128 bytes**. Missing or mismatched source locators stop recovery rather than inventing evidence.\n- Potential persistent-session blocker: archiving indefinitely into a quota-backed store and whole growing serialized indexes can hit lifetime limits without a session timeout. This audit has established declarations; actual quota/reclamation/recovery callers are pending.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQPMyszvIWOptbMxpXskodbR4ZfB6GkVCQYOjK8CFhZ4qF4FAD2EuH2qt+kDDdRGyhYObkFo3x7TZLzITFYb07w0="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2194,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:19:08.074041729Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"3a48b567-5e09-57c7-9238-f1c99deeb0cc","comment_uuid":"eab02665-ec86-4286-9e99-c74f2312f6b5","author":"6ME5","content":"Systemic repair plan for L057: Local context archive, record, and artifact storage capacities.\n\nOwning contract and implementation boundary: local_context/storage.rs:30,86-90,133-175; peritus-artifact-store/src/store.rs:75-91,229-239; quota.rs:74-85; local_context/record.rs:169-186; storage.rs:110-123; local_context/storage/append.rs:22-26; record.rs:69-80. Apply the change through the constructors, live callers, durable writer and restart reader for this boundary, not as an isolated constant increase.\n\nStore context history, source indexes and working snapshots as paged artifacts with one small atomic root. Separate explicit physical storage policy from lifetime session history; support safe root retirement/compaction and an observable storage wait. Align record serialization, journal frames, StateInstall and artifact dependencies before publication so accepted memory always reopens.\n\nPreserve: governing inputs, complete pending tool protocol pairs, exact source/lineage references, explicit permissions, unresolved effect truth and task-role/native-provider identity. Separate a physical allocation/page limit and a genuine authority or integrity check from a cumulative work allowance. Keep transient contention/capacity observable and recoverable under the existing logical task; do not discard accepted state or substitute a fresh session to get around it.\n\nCompatibility/migration: retain decoders and exact receipts for previously accepted records. If representation or lifecycle semantics change, introduce a versioned migration under exclusive ownership; verify a complete replacement frontier before atomic publication and keep the old recovery root until adoption is durable. Rebuild derived projections from authoritative evidence. Update all producers, consumers and invariants together; a rejected new operation must leave the predecessor usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: long productive read/write sessions through repeated compaction and segment boundaries, source/dependency changes, non-ASCII and large evidence, interrupted checkpoint publication, then reopen the same lineage and prove that valid grounding is reused and stale targets are reread. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:19:07.750Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQIgmXapuJ7ZmqdlBkq85CnqFBuuksmcSwhuvLu0AbePjfFrayOnUglIArcvqNLL0MRCZgIzszOSsE/9C+vagOwU="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2195,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:19:08.076642835Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"8b4c91ef-b8b4-5754-801c-bd17de76c5a7","title":"[L058] Local working-memory defaults and configuration admission","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L058.\n\n- `context_config.rs:99-114` defaults to **85% input trigger**, **eight recent messages**, **4,096 preferred working-state tokens**, **4,096 retrieved-evidence tokens**, **32 update operations**, **2,048 bytes per entry**, and **16,384 bytes per evidence-read response**. Completed batches publish checkpoints by default.\n- Validation at lines 123-142 allows trigger **1..100%**, recent preference **1..128**, working token preference **1..16,384**, retrieved tokens **0..16,384**, and read bytes **256..65,536**. `working/limits.rs` now identifies the actual dimensions: **65,535 observation locators**, **512 working entries**, caller entry bytes, **32 items per source/dependency/file-validity list**, and caller update count. Its constructor can only narrow the hard envelope (L061); actual reducer/assembly enforcement remains pending.\n- Preferences can omit optional evidence, while required closure may borrow headroom per the field contract. Do not treat preferred retention as deletion or assume all these dimensions are terminal quotas before reading the reducer/assembly callers.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQBSz3l4SIKFIJtHS6TDdW4fCw7z/canjL19/4C2lwjXCkYe/V5ldvGGUqPjMN0OoRQcmqN