{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2197,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:19:08.081302527Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"ae6b613d-749a-5b21-aa3d-20b0114b11ad","title":"[L059] Optional local semantic subprocess envelope","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L059.\n\n- `context_config.rs:146-158` requires an explicitly supplied positive timeout in milliseconds, input **1..1,048,576 bytes**, output **1..262,144 bytes**, and memory **16 MiB..64 GiB**. No default semantic process is enabled: the default backend is Disabled (lines 24-27,104-105).\n- Absolute executable/weights/native-sandbox paths and a delegated Linux cgroup rather than the host root are admission requirements (lines 149-154,188-205). These authority/resource requirements are separate from the fixed maximum payload and configuration-memory ranges.\n- Actual process execution/cancellation and deterministic fallback behavior remain pending. This declaration is a caller-selected deadline for an optional capability, not evidence of an ordinary provider timeout.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQHkoxQSTTfJ7OICpvXIwOAno7KVkeyTxe/FJgWg2CX5y32GDNIL1QMMTexBmwuqTo3XgmYx0i5eAEipT51ynIAI="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2198,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:19:08.083466836Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"ae6b613d-749a-5b21-aa3d-20b0114b11ad","comment_uuid":"75a213ce-d86b-481c-b1f4-925585aec883","author":"6ME5","content":"Systemic repair plan for L059: Optional local semantic subprocess envelope.\n\nOwning contract and implementation boundary: context_config.rs:146-158. Apply the change through the constructors, live callers, durable writer and restart reader for this boundary, not as an isolated constant increase.\n\nMake optional semantic-process deadlines/resources explicitly selected policies with an unlimited duration option; transport pages must not impose a total semantic-history cap. Stream input/output and bind model/weights/backend identity to the recorded proposal. Preserve delegated cgroup and path authority; deterministic fallback remains available without abandoning the main provider task.\n\nPreserve: governing inputs, complete pending tool protocol pairs, exact source/lineage references, explicit permissions, unresolved effect truth and task-role/native-provider identity. Separate a physical allocation/page limit and a genuine authority or integrity check from a cumulative work allowance. Keep transient contention/capacity observable and recoverable under the existing logical task; do not discard accepted state or substitute a fresh session to get around it.\n\nCompatibility/migration: retain decoders and exact receipts for previously accepted records. If representation or lifecycle semantics change, introduce a versioned migration under exclusive ownership; verify a complete replacement frontier before atomic publication and keep the old recovery root until adoption is durable. Rebuild derived projections from authoritative evidence. Update all producers, consumers and invariants together; a rejected new operation must leave the predecessor usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: long productive read/write sessions through repeated compaction and segment boundaries, source/dependency changes, non-ASCII and large evidence, interrupted checkpoint publication, then reopen the same lineage and prove that valid grounding is reused and stale targets are reread. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:19:07.750Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQPTuaZhJhAXRyV0mWrUHzsm5Kbn12C2FDa+XjwXHLmvb/sY+gOr8dADl1WnwRigFXK9UoHiFqDRFZiRDRrBaigA="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2199,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:19:08.085887080Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"58de5743-3329-50b3-99a1-56648ffec30a","title":"[L060] Recovered torn trace data still blocks new context work","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L060.\n\n- `local_context/memory.rs:114-127` recovers valid local-memory observations from the trace but returns an error if the trace reader reports a torn tail: “trace repair required before new work.” That error stops opening the retained memory lineage.\n- A torn write can therefore block daily driving despite recoverable preceding history. Exact trace-tail detection and explicit safe repair/restart paths remain pending; no claim is made yet that repair does not exist elsewhere.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQMgMRJTKvwDKWPQz10og1TmFY+yxvrlAzVzGIM1qwXWGVzH15GX854g1GNiFkI7Grj4a9Eu+XTRAJNWDIe+bkw8="}
