{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2209,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:19:08.107275766Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"bf7282d2-d486-5d29-9dc5-785bd7a0adf5","title":"[L065] Logical artifact quota blocks writes independently of physical free space","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L065.\n\n- `peritus-artifact-store/src/quota.rs:21-37,74-85` rejects used-plus-reserved bytes above the selected quota and arithmetic overflow. `store.rs:75-91,99-114` calls this before beginning a new artifact write; existing digest metadata selects a zero-byte reservation.\n- `store/capacity.rs:41-55` observes physical filesystem space but makes no admission decision. Thus local memory's fixed **1 GiB logical quota** (L057) can refuse further archival work even with substantial free disk.\n- `store.rs:247-265` exposes explicit garbage-collection planning/application; write admission does not automatically invoke it in this implementation. `references.rs:117-150` retains journal/evidence roots. Catalog persistence and collection rules are now source-verified (L066/L067); external reference-release callers and reachability of each historical checkpoint remain pending.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQCDGmvrqY9IF4bN5AqjZBSsZpAuWDpfbd5RYo/OQ81DzVwNOlJy2/uP6bDvGBMnW60Pv2FqmlmSAUY9VgjndHgY="}
