{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2215,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:19:08.119893663Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"fcb9d28a-cbb1-54a0-b43e-325f7197a070","title":"[L068] Artifact writer has bounded temporary-name allocation and fatal write admission","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L068.\n\n- `writer.rs:149-173,181-235` requires expected bytes <= positive declared bytes <= configured maximum, rejects overflow or excess chunks, and makes the writer unusable after a write failure. Exact final size/digest is an integrity requirement distinct from the configurable byte cap.\n- `writer.rs:323-342` attempts at most **1,024** unique temporary names before returning Retry-class I/O failure. This is a finite collision-retry limiter, not a run-duration deadline.\n- Final publication occurs before catalog recording (`writer.rs:246-279`). A newly published object is removed for quota/arithmetic failure; other catalog errors are returned after publication. `recovery.rs:179-199` contains uncataloged published bytes by quarantining them, then removes them on a subsequent recovery pass; this does not repair the failed local-context publication automatically.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQI0KS0037qG35dhUFQzpj8G0Ye/z+y9LAEdXeYb6z2PaWn/grfja4F1EvBIFPWsh2I9FIbx2J5cLzkrD6aPJ8ww="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2216,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:19:08.121903184Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"fcb9d28a-cbb1-54a0-b43e-325f7197a070","comment_uuid":"a7361404-c91f-4760-b9a4-cd1b0cfb578a","author":"6ME5","content":"Systemic repair plan for L068: Artifact writer has bounded temporary-name allocation and fatal write admission.\n\nOwning contract and implementation boundary: writer.rs:149-173,181-235; writer.rs:323-342; writer.rs:246-279; recovery.rs:179-199. Apply the change through the constructors, live callers, durable writer and restart reader for this boundary, not as an isolated constant increase.\n\nUse atomic unique temporary creation with a checked durable writer identity rather than a fixed collision-attempt policy. Persist Prepared/Published/Cataloged phases so catalog contention after publication can be reconciled idempotently. A failed stream stays unusable, but its logical write intent can resume safely from verified content without duplicate accounting or deleting accepted bytes.\n\nPreserve: governing inputs, complete pending tool protocol pairs, exact source/lineage references, explicit permissions, unresolved effect truth and task-role/native-provider identity. Separate a physical allocation/page limit and a genuine authority or integrity check from a cumulative work allowance. Keep transient contention/capacity observable and recoverable under the existing logical task; do not discard accepted state or substitute a fresh session to get around it.\n\nCompatibility/migration: retain decoders and exact receipts for previously accepted records. If representation or lifecycle semantics change, introduce a versioned migration under exclusive ownership; verify a complete replacement frontier before atomic publication and keep the old recovery root until adoption is durable. Rebuild derived projections from authoritative evidence. Update all producers, consumers and invariants together; a rejected new operation must leave the predecessor usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: long productive read/write sessions through repeated compaction and segment boundaries, source/dependency changes, non-ASCII and large evidence, interrupted checkpoint publication, then reopen the same lineage and prove that valid grounding is reused and stale targets are reread. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:19:07.750Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQEXOPu8u8bsv/2IYguaILrlalQAn+JG8WMtMAinTgm4EpwD1A9sVRa6E9U7eMx8magbnv2LbFch5KwLTmZ4HkAU="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2217,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:19:08.124378531Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"93c008a9-6542-53b7-85b5-506a8e7cc03d","title":"[L069] Artifact recovery fences the store on missing bytes or malformed layout","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L069.\n\n- `recovery.rs:108-199` materializes the complete durable inventory, verifies each recorded object, and scans both digest trees. Missing recorded bytes abort recovery (`157,174,309-314`); noncanonical names, nonregular entries, or unexpected temporary-directory contents also abort it (`231-291`). These are integrity barriers rather than synthetic runtime deadlines.\n- An uncataloged object left after publication is quarantined on the first recovery and removed on the next (`179-199`). Cataloged corruption is marked and contained; some duplicate/missing corruption layouts still terminate recovery (`203-216`). Startup callers and operator repair affordances remain pending.\n- `finalize.rs:52-98` independently rejects an artifact read above its caller-selected maximum and allocates the complete accepted artifact in memory. `hash_file` uses a 16 KiB streaming buffer without a total-size/time cap (`128-154`); the buffer is not a limiter.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQBKhewafvuHPID+JnSLRZ2MrAFCAo+edfKOb+a2fZOEZmyDXIut/HHaoGAZY72htvLej8RbsfwscIn3d5/6tqgI="}
