{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2225,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:19:08.141464530Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"5eb3c485-2e91-50fc-adf2-d0892b722603","title":"[L073] Working-state wire format has a separate eight-MiB envelope","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L073.\n\n- `working/wire/mod.rs:15,42-60` hardcodes **8 MiB frame/payload**, **65,535 collection items**, **2,048-byte string/opaque fields**, and nesting depth **8**. These capacities are independent of the local host's 32 MiB serialized-artifact allowance (L057).\n- `wire/state.rs:12-22` encodes the entire observation prefix, environment, entry history, and protocol pins as one snapshot. Combined bytes can exhaust the wire envelope even before separate domain lists reach their maxima; no rollover/partitioning exists in this encoder.\n- Decode permits only limits at or below the supplied maximum and validates every retained source/dependency/supersession (`33-88`). Unsupported version, corrupt graph, or invalid retained status prevents snapshot restoration. Integrity validation is separate from the artificial allocation envelope.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQNP1df4dCLxwbmzwxbIR3ptVPqAViv04QsgBMbwERmpdaaPnIkz3qrphHeD1k0inSzZSJ2wH3PlvS6OVqSCfkgU="}
