{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2231,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:19:08.154879608Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"d3153143-ec76-51cb-9bed-2dabe7a5ba3f","title":"[L076] Remembered-file hashing has a 64-MiB synthetic stop","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L076.\n\n- `local_context/memory/environment.rs:73-87` hashes file dependencies with an **8 KiB buffer** but aborts after **64 MiB total bytes**. Streaming itself does not require this total-size ceiling.\n- `capture:50-70` omits paths rejected by protected-file validation and propagates other file-read/hash failures into context refresh; a remembered large file can therefore prevent assembling the next request. The exact upstream refresh/error recovery path is recorded separately; this source gate is additional to workspace/checkpoint/tool size limits.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQNb6bHkx3WbHN56on69TQBi4TX72Y+QvuHcm4HpGIPqLQPVV8iQHGgOzIW2/Pfp7Gs3uz7bsiyeT0oYMtqrPBw8="}
