ion: long-running commands, output and stdin pressure, stalled helper/input readers, control-queue saturation, late start/exit races, parent loss and restart, proving cancellation responsiveness, no PID-reuse adoption and no duplicate process dispatch. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:19:07.750Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQKhDoKMNXlauh5s0xRfoHKx/+NAsevrKklvsOHoQox27lMuJR5IyDK67I7RdLU46qVEL5TSS6VRKTqBqH5MaIA4="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2279,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:19:08.261221230Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"bc359ec3-230a-5fa7-ad53-ca2763788496","title":"[L100] Native observation histories have a hard 4,096-entry lifecycle gate","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L100.\n\n- `native/observation.rs:88-124` refuses empty histories or histories above **4,096 observations**. Every observation must retain contiguous sequence and exact plan/backend binding; full history is rescanned at prepared/activated/terminated/released validation.\n- Lifecycle validity permits repeated resource/capability/fault observations while active, so the count bound can reject an otherwise valid observation stream. An over-limit history becomes Supervisor/CancelAndReap rather than an evicted telemetry window. Actual backend emission frequency/retention is pending before claiming a fixed elapsed lifetime.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQJz527aNGpCE7eWqKIAU0yT5yEtLBXHoK8siPEknnrdgSF1aWzGU6vTqOJkpq1leCAlwAKL76kE7IZuoz8/eSAM="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2280,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:19:08.263342745Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"bc359ec3-230a-5fa7-ad53-ca2763788496","comment_uuid":"7209f2c5-8b57-4b9b-8af8-05ef8f6dd407","author":"6ME5","content":"Systemic repair plan for L100: Native observation histories have a hard 4,096-entry lifecycle gate.\n\nOwning contract and implementation boundary: native/observation.rs:88-124. Apply the change through the constructors, live callers, durable writer and restart reader for this boundary, not as an isolated constant increase.\n\nSeparate immutable native lifecycle evidence from the bounded live telemetry view. Persist paged contiguous observations and validate lifecycle transitions incrementally against an exact frontier. Repeated legitimate resource observations must advance that frontier rather than become CancelAndReap at 4096 entries; binding or sequence conflicts remain integrity failures.\n\nPreserve: exact process birth/tree identity, confined authority, one-use dispatch receipts, monotonic cancel intent, truthful terminal/ownership settlement, complete output accounting and platform OS constraints. Separate a physical allocation/page limit and a genuine authority or integrity check from a cumulative work allowance. Keep transient contention/capacity observable and recoverable under the existing logical task; do not discard accepted state or substitute a fresh session to get around it.\n\nCompatibility/migration: retain decoders and exact receipts for previously accepted records. If representation or lifecycle semantics change, introduce a versioned migration under exclusive ownership; verify a complete replacement frontier before atomic publication and keep the old recovery root until adoption is durable. Rebuild derived projections from authoritative evidence. Update all producers, consumers and invariants together; a rejected new operation must leave the predecessor usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: long-running commands, output and stdin pressure, stalled helper/input readers, control-queue saturation, late start/exit races, parent loss and restart, proving cancellation responsiveness, no PID-reuse adoption and no duplicate process dispatch. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:19:07.750Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQAiRwJwTi19Ru5He1Jtz3lX26MzfB9teuG4rBgIb5F6mcM6okN8bsAf0HQxXi3Ipt6NOF4GjYTsAGdcrPmj14Qo="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2281,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:19:08.266107086Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"f419043d-73c4-5a6f-a178-1533a5b2b2c5","title":"[L101] Native recovery cannot settle certain live or unobservable process identities","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L101.\n\n- `native/probe/windows.rs:38-50` recognizes an exact live root but refuses termination because no reopenable durable job handle is persisted. `recovery/reconcile.rs:138` propagates that error, aborting the whole scan rather than returning completed outcomes for later records. Native Windows live control cannot be reconstructed through this path.\n- Linux/macOS zombie roots are classified Unverifiable, not safely absent (`native/probe/linux.rs:25-26`, `macos.rs:33-34`); missing birth/containment facts, inaccessible observations, and PID mismatch also remain indeterminate. These are exact-identity requirements, but unresolved state can persist and contribute to L088 admission/quiescence barriers.\n- Unix termination freshly rechecks identity before sending SIGKILL. No additional elapsed timer exists in the probes themselves; the separate watchdog reobservation cutoff is L099. Recovery must preserve exact identity while supplying a usable settlement/adoption path.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQFJDzyYqnsYr5pdXdGP5dCy8HuIcfCXyPpfVYHNuG0LE01aBDkl9CW111qANJWhwZEVxw0hQCgYB1UjC7UNcVwg="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2282,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:19:08.268241657Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"f419043d-73c4-5a6f-a178-1533a5b2b2c5","comment_uuid":"f1487033-a663-478f-805e-f646ce33ff22","author":"6ME5","content":"Systemic repair plan for L101: Native recovery cannot settle certain live or unobservable process identities.\n\nOwning contract and implementation boundary: native/probe/windows.rs:38-50; recovery/reconcile.rs:138; native/probe/linux.rs:25-26; macos.rs:33-34. Apply the change through the constructors, live callers, durable writer and restart reader for this boundary, not as an isolated constant increase.\n\nPersist a reopenable native job/supervisor authority and exact containment identity for Windows adoption or cancellation. Classify Unix zombies with birth and parent-reaping evidence rather than conflating them with arbitrary unverifiable PIDs. Return per-record reconciliation outcomes and retain unresolved obligations so one inaccessible process does not abort recovery of every other record.\n\nPreserve: exact process birth/tree identity, confined authority, one-use dispatch receipts, monotonic cancel intent, truthful terminal/ownership settlement, complete output accounting and platform OS constraints. Separate a physical allocation/page limit and a genuine authority or integrity check from a cumulative work allowance. Keep transient contention/capacity observable and recoverable under the existing logical task; do not discard accepted state or substitute a fresh session to get around it.\n\nCompatibility/migration: retain decoders and exact receipts for previously accepted records. If representation or lifecycle semantics change, introduce a versioned migration under exclusive ownership; verify a complete replacement frontier before atomic publication and keep the old recovery root until adoption is durable. Rebuild derived projections from authoritative evidence. Update all producers, consumers and invariants together; a rejected new operation must leave the predecessor usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: long-running commands, output and stdin pressure, stalled helper/input readers, control-queue saturation, late start/exit races, parent loss and restart, proving cancellation responsiveness, no PID-reuse adoption and no duplicate process dispatch. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:19:07.750Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQC8PfET/1BM5G4mXcYHXVgtawXDZ7hPQy5LHD3/brhsVQMlwR3+zFkZu9z7MGC/fZs5WURFnGeVMjbl/OQ/6sg4="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2283,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:19:08.270531227Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"06970f4b-6eef-5bbf-834d-b136596dffc9","title":"[L102] Product command acceptance contracts still declare a synthetic one-millisecond gate timeout","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L102.\n\n- `command_runtime/contract.rs:23-35` builds every internal command's minimal acceptance contract with `GateExecutionPlan::new(..., 1, ...)`. Reading its actual constructor confirms that this argument is **timeout milliseconds**, stored as Some(1) (`peritus-spec/src/gate.rs:53-79`), not a count or placeholder with another meaning.\n- This is an artificial deadline declaration even when the separately constructed process/tool call has no selected wall deadline. The inspected `command_runtime/kernel.rs:22-138` uses the contract for C0 Open/StartRun/StartAttempt/StartTurn/Propose/Authorize/Dispatch commitments; it does **not** execute the contract gate there. No one-millisecond process kill is claimed from this declaration. Remaining gate callers/recovery consumers must resolve its consequences.\n- The generic gate API already supports `with_optional_timeout(..., None, ...)` and rejects only Some(0). Graph canonical ordering, complete dependency references, and acyclicity are integrity conditions; the read graph constructor adds no fixed gate-count maximum.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQOWN8cWbWzELIb9OYSzN+DrJAPzSMOZCaAEP6rRCMd/lFiB5MreTTOEY214ibZktggSPPu88CpC6XivmMV0CKQA="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2284,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:19:08.272830980Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"06970f4b-6eef-5bbf-834d-b136596dffc9","comment_uuid":"57228286-2222-467c-ad6a-e159b2f290eb","author":"6ME5","content":"Systemic repair plan for L102: Product command acceptance contracts still declare a synthetic one-millisecond gate timeout.\n\nOwning contract and implementation boundary: command_runtime/contract.rs:23-35; peritus-spec/src/gate.rs:53-79; command_runtime/kernel.rs:22-138. Apply the change through the constructors, live callers, durable writer and restart reader for this boundary, not as an isolated constant increase.\n\nConstruct minimal command acceptance contracts with an absent timeout unless a real deadline was explicitly selected. Carry that optionality through canonical encoding, kernel commitments, recovery and actual gate execution, avoiding a synthetic one-millisecond placeholder. Preserve graph dependencies and exact target binding, and verify untimed contracts round-trip and remain accepted by every consumer.\n\nPreserve: exact process birth/tree identity, confined authority, one-use dispatch receipts, monotonic cancel intent, truthful terminal/ownership settlement, complete output accounting and platform OS constraints. Separate a physical allocation/page limit and a genuine authority or integrity check from a cumulative work allowance. Keep transient contention/capacity observable and recoverable under the existing logical task; do not discard accepted state or substitute a fresh session to get around it.\n\nCompatibility/migration: retain decoders and exact receipts for previously accepted records. If representation or lifecycle semantics change, introduce a versioned migration under exclusive ownership; verify a complete replacement frontier before atomic publication and keep the old recovery root until adoption is durable. Rebuild derived projections from authoritative evidence. Update all producers, consumers and invariants together; a rejected new operation must leave the predecessor usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: long-running commands, output and stdin pressure, stalled helper/input readers, control-queue saturation, late start/exit races, parent loss and restart, proving cancellation responsiveness, no PID-reuse adoption and no duplicate process dispatch. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:19:07.750Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQIl3+LJ0At+jFQFzKrWtNmhqZXqC3yq+ryczIcBP4d7wzkuCKQcAc0ZLaQ6Zy3i4kkm/J91s3LPm1lbgn3pyxg8="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2285,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:19:08.275090435Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"7b5fdd5b-2d1a-54f9-a7f9-3735c46a62dd","title":"[L103] Tool JSON envelopes have production ceilings that callers cannot widen","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L103.\n\n- `peritus-tool-protocol/src/limits.rs:22-27,40-53` fixes production JSON at **256 KiB canonical bytes**, **depth 32**, **4,096 aggregate members**, and **64 KiB per string/property name**. `JsonLimits::new` can only narrow those values. `schema/canonical.rs:10-26,81-90,239-288` enforces both raw input and canonical bytes, recursively counts members/depth, and bounds UTF-8 strings. These are independent of L042's separate developer argument parser depth. Numbers must be signed i64 integers; floating point or larger unsigned values reject the envelope (`42-47`).\n- `call.rs:46-74,108-117` requires positive non-time output/model/human/progress/artifact ceilings and makes every call fit its immutable descriptor. Wall time can be absent only when the descriptor allows absence; a timed descriptor rejects an unbounded call. Actual descriptor defaults and result validation are pending.\n- `control.rs:104-128` separately bounds each stdin control by the supplied maximum and represents terminal dimensions with positive u16 values. Control-set/cancellation enums alone do not add a timer.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQMZlfV2UPsn1Mdi7XuGtqHOElqY9eb/nHhQd4+NNig2nY707Fs+ZGCfz2k1R8mZ0aB/rsdiI2KGm0zmQIPySLQY="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2286,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:19:08.277277271Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"7b5fdd5b-2d1a-54f9-a7f9-3735c46a62dd","comment_uuid":"c639456f-ab21-4ebc-a877-41eec5e58ab7","author":"6ME5","content":"Systemic repair plan for L103: Tool JSON envelopes have production ceilings that callers cannot widen.\n\nOwning contract and implementation boundary: peritus-tool-protocol/src/limits.rs:22-27,40-53; schema/canonical.rs:10-26,81-90,239-288; call.rs:46-74,108-117; control.rs:104-128. Apply the change through the constructors, live callers, durable writer and restart reader for this boundary, not as an isolated constant increase.\n\nMake tool JSON a negotiated per-frame contract with referenced large arguments/results and shared descriptor/call/parser admissibility. Model no selected wall deadline explicitly when supported; positive physical chunk/window bounds remain separate. Add exact numeric types required by tools instead of rejecting valid domain numbers through an incidental i64-only envelope.\n\nPreserve: exact process birth/tree identity, confined authority, one-use dispatch receipts, monotonic cancel intent, truthful terminal/ownership settlement, complete output accounting and platform OS constraints. Separate a physical allocation/page limit and a genuine authority or integrity check from a cumulative work allowance. Keep transient contention/capacity observable and recoverable under the existing logical task; do not discard accepted state or substitute a fresh session to get around it.\n\nCompatibility/migration: retain decoders and exact receipts for previously accepted records. If representation or lifecycle semantics change, introduce a versioned migration under exclusive ownership; verify a complete replacement frontier before atomic publication and keep the old recovery root until adoption is durable. Rebuild derived projections from authoritative evidence. Update all producers, consumers and invariants together; a rejected new operation must leave the predecessor usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: long-running commands, output and stdin pressure, stalled helper/input readers, control-queue saturation, late start/exit races, parent loss and restart, proving cancellation responsiveness, no PID-reuse adoption and no duplicate process dispatch. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:19:07.750Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQL0SXA3fF+aO7WZXKJPTVC+M6nXaH7qT7wr9Bx35QJfZV25ezUMidR51Nb//qWdXxHbmdCrNgX9qsjlfBwiicQw="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2287,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:19:08.279653769Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"f806d920-9a41-5943-b88a-7c9f1c054af0","title":"[L104] Tool schemas add fixed property/enum bounds and byte-based exported string cardinality","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L104.\n\n- `schema/validate.rs:8-10,38-79` caps each object schema at **256 properties**, property names at **256 bytes**, each enumeration at **256 values**, and validation depth at **32**. Canonical uniqueness/order and required-field checks are integrity/schema requirements; fixed counts/depth are implementation ceilings.\n- `schema.rs:237-250` permits u32 string/array cardinalities, but actual `BoundedJson` still must fit L103's smaller global envelope/string/member ceilings. Declaring a wider field schema does not widen those parser limits.\n- Internal string cardinality counts UTF-8 **bytes** (`validate.rs:117-123`), while export writes those numbers as JSON Schema `minLength`/`maxLength` (`canonical.rs:140-143`). This unit mismatch can let a provider submit multibyte text it believes fits, then receive a validation refusal. External validators/provider usage are pending; the differing implementation units are verified.\n- Compatibility accepts only exact schemas or added optional object properties (`compatibility.rs:16-40`); other changes are Breaking. This is version-contract admission, not an execution deadline.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQB+F