{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2288,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:19:08.282127535Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"f806d920-9a41-5943-b88a-7c9f1c054af0","comment_uuid":"4a9d4443-77fd-4fc8-9a18-ea256f7b3ac7","author":"6ME5","content":"Systemic repair plan for L104: Tool schemas add fixed property/enum bounds and byte-based exported string cardinality.\n\nOwning contract and implementation boundary: schema/validate.rs:8-10,38-79; schema.rs:237-250; validate.rs:117-123; canonical.rs:140-143; compatibility.rs:16-40. Apply the change through the constructors, live callers, durable writer and restart reader for this boundary, not as an isolated constant increase.\n\nDeclare string size units consistently in exported schemas and host validation, including multibyte text. Share a versioned schema/canonical parser contract and page large enums/properties where the provider protocol permits references. Preserve uniqueness, ordering and compatibility classification; a wider advertised field must be genuinely admitted by every enclosing parser.\n\nPreserve: exact process birth/tree identity, confined authority, one-use dispatch receipts, monotonic cancel intent, truthful terminal/ownership settlement, complete output accounting and platform OS constraints. Separate a physical allocation/page limit and a genuine authority or integrity check from a cumulative work allowance. Keep transient contention/capacity observable and recoverable under the existing logical task; do not discard accepted state or substitute a fresh session to get around it.\n\nCompatibility/migration: retain decoders and exact receipts for previously accepted records. If representation or lifecycle semantics change, introduce a versioned migration under exclusive ownership; verify a complete replacement frontier before atomic publication and keep the old recovery root until adoption is durable. Rebuild derived projections from authoritative evidence. Update all producers, consumers and invariants together; a rejected new operation must leave the predecessor usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: long-running commands, output and stdin pressure, stalled helper/input readers, control-queue saturation, late start/exit races, parent loss and restart, proving cancellation responsiveness, no PID-reuse adoption and no duplicate process dispatch. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:19:07.750Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQJLZw0H07w0TPOqZddGdcYBPWjGrbCwh16eOZrQuz4ZfAo0mZaA6FVZEUHPQ808M5joRrCSpDlYf3/XqY/zBiAg="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2289,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:19:08.284349145Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"4cc4f4da-1624-5f08-95cc-e2d1645cf3f3","title":"[L105] Tool terminal/progress construction can fail after an effect because of rendering and output totals","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L105.\n\n- `result.rs:327-351` adds **all referenced artifact sizes plus canonical structured-result bytes**, then refuses the terminal envelope if that sum exceeds the call output allowance. Human/model renderings, progress count, and artifact count are separately checked. The allowance therefore includes result metadata as well as the underlying archived command bytes; concrete adapter behavior is being followed.\n- `identity.rs:6-8,20-22,141-158` hard-caps all BoundedText at **16 KiB**, implementation identity at **256 bytes**, and idempotency keys at **128 bytes**. BoundedText rejects empty text and NUL rather than truncating; descriptor model/human ceilings cannot widen this type's maximum.\n- `progress.rs:48-56` rejects sequence at or above selected progress count, oversized rendering, or changed authority epoch. This is total invocation progress admission, not a rolling telemetry window; actual adapters determine whether exhaustion terminates or drops updates. The shell adapter suppresses updates once its 4096-event ceiling is reached and marks progress truncated; it does not cancel the process (`peritus-tools-shell/src/execution/active.rs:111-119`). Resource samples consume this same allowance (`execution/progress.rs:67-73`).\n- Protocol diagnostics separately cap paths at **8 KiB** (truncate with a suffix) and static details at **4 KiB** (replace oversized detail), potentially hiding exact nested causes (`error.rs:117-138`). Caller-defined transport limits are enforced by envelope parsing; protocol version is currently exactly one (`envelope.rs:25-37`).\n- Artifact references disallow zero-byte objects (`artifact.rs:67-74`) and require exact invocation provenance at result construction. Zero output belongs in structured output through this protocol. These are representation/provenance restrictions, distinct from artificial elapsed deadlines.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQL+XrncJM85KT2nP4tkQs1LkJ/au+zDzJxDCgTE5KtUAj+D6BZb0F27/HDPoV5QkpDPU8qA/TxU1Aduq5sXdbA0="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2290,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:19:08.286497792Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"4cc4f4da-1624-5f08-95cc-e2d1645cf3f3","comment_uuid":"5e90995c-dc7a-4d71-a4e4-806084180566","author":"6ME5","content":"Systemic repair plan for L105: Tool terminal/progress construction can fail after an effect because of rendering and output totals.\n\nOwning contract and implementation boundary: result.rs:327-351; identity.rs:6-8,20-22,141-158; progress.rs:48-56; peritus-tools-shell/src/execution/active.rs:111-119; execution/progress.rs:67-73; error.rs:117-138; envelope.rs:25-37; artifact.rs:67-74. Apply the change through the constructors, live callers, durable writer and restart reader for this boundary, not as an isolated constant increase.\n\nSeparate archived artifact bytes, structured terminal metadata and display previews in result accounting. Prevalidate the final terminal representation before effect dispatch, and persist effect completion before fallible rendering. Page progress history and retain exact artifact provenance, so presentation or envelope pressure cannot erase a successful owned effect.\n\nPreserve: exact process birth/tree identity, confined authority, one-use dispatch receipts, monotonic cancel intent, truthful terminal/ownership settlement, complete output accounting and platform OS constraints. Separate a physical allocation/page limit and a genuine authority or integrity check from a cumulative work allowance. Keep transient contention/capacity observable and recoverable under the existing logical task; do not discard accepted state or substitute a fresh session to get around it.\n\nCompatibility/migration: retain decoders and exact receipts for previously accepted records. If representation or lifecycle semantics change, introduce a versioned migration under exclusive ownership; verify a complete replacement frontier before atomic publication and keep the old recovery root until adoption is durable. Rebuild derived projections from authoritative evidence. Update all producers, consumers and invariants together; a rejected new operation must leave the predecessor usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: long-running commands, output and stdin pressure, stalled helper/input readers, control-queue saturation, late start/exit races, parent loss and restart, proving cancellation responsiveness, no PID-reuse adoption and no duplicate process dispatch. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:19:07.750Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQPlkEB/wH1xvhnf5VzdwJ6a58Ci3YKKKtYBqTUoN83eHskNXeSiSAJiGPb5FvTCXqKX7ISA9m2f8IWAtbWLmFwo="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2291,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:19:08.288779998Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"b8f6f49f-45b3-5d39-84fd-f9e097e7a2ae","title":"[L106] Shell output can exhaust its result envelope after successful command completion","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L106.\n\n- Shell descriptors allow **8 MiB total output** (`crates/tools/peritus-tools-shell/src/catalog.rs:89-97`), and the product process plan admits an **8 MiB spool** (L083). Shell terminal rendering includes every published stream artifact's full byte size plus mandatory nonempty structured metadata (`execution/terminal.rs:29-76,79-163`).\n- Combined with the protocol sum check in L105, an invocation that archives exactly 8 MiB cannot construct a result within an 8 MiB allowance. Output close to that size may also fail because no metadata headroom is reserved. This is a source-confirmed cross-layer mismatch; a runtime reproduction has not been run during the read-only audit.\n- This defeats the intended truncation policy: the process continues while dropping excess bytes (L090), and the shell explicitly permits a successful exit with truncated output (`execution/terminal.rs:175-263,339-347`). The result constructor nevertheless returns `shell-result-envelope` after execution/publication. `execution/failure.rs:59-68` classifies this as Failed/Protocol/Never/None. The router turns it into a terminal failed envelope, completes replay state, and removes the active execution (`peritus-tool-router/src/router.rs:272-333`); normalization carries neither structured output nor artifact references (`normalization.rs:27-42`). Product projection then exposes failed status, empty streams, null exit code and unknown disposition (`peritus-product-runner/src/developer_tools/command_runtime/result.rs:26-81`). Thus successful command completion becomes a failed tool observation without its published output references. Whole-run continuation after this observation remains under examination.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQGs8EuV+4CjoEc/wGKpOw3oVNdlteOGDwPK+MdJm7bNEMrEdVrc2kf6H/Z9Ar9GQscau87xwP7fSCUdUqEoCPg8="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2292,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:19:08.290949278Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"b8f6f49f-45b3-5d39-84fd-f9e097e7a2ae","comment_uuid":"e1f30d1c-39e6-4d8b-898c-163db928d40c","author":"6ME5","content":"Systemic repair plan for L106: Shell output can exhaust its result envelope after successful command completion.\n\nOwning contract and implementation boundary: crates/tools/peritus-tools-shell/src/catalog.rs:89-97; execution/terminal.rs:29-76,79-163; execution/terminal.rs:175-263,339-347; execution/failure.rs:59-68; peritus-tool-router/src/router.rs:272-333; normalization.rs:27-42; peritus-product-runner/src/developer_tools/command_runtime/result.rs:26-81. Apply the change through the constructors, live callers, durable writer and restart reader for this boundary, not as an isolated constant increase.\n\nGive shell completion a durable outcome receipt independent of the model/human envelope. Account metadata separately from referenced spool content, and stream or reference large output rather than requiring archive bytes plus metadata to fit the same allowance. Router and product projection must preserve exit status, disposition and artifact references even when display construction needs recovery.\n\nPreserve: exact process birth/tree identity, confined authority, one-use dispatch receipts, monotonic cancel intent, truthful terminal/ownership settlement, complete output accounting and platform OS constraints. Separate a physical allocation/page limit and a genuine authority or integrity check from a cumulative work allowance. Keep transient contention/capacity observable and recoverable under the existing logical task; do not discard accepted state or substitute a fresh session to get around it.\n\nCompatibility/migration: retain decoders and exact receipts for previously accepted records. If representation or lifecycle semantics change, introduce a versioned migration under exclusive ownership; verify a complete replacement frontier before atomic publication and keep the old recovery root until adoption is durable. Rebuild derived projections from authoritative evidence. Update all producers, consumers and invariants together; a rejected new operation must leave the predecessor usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: long-running commands, output and stdin pressure, stalled helper/input readers, control-queue saturation, late start/exit races, parent loss and restart, proving cancellation responsiveness, no PID-reuse adoption and no duplicate process dispatch. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:19:07.750Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQPfQedobtkKpoZeD7G9j8GQ0H3mtMglgIZNNg/0zbmfJPoyTwxT5cpn9mIy564kr5pJeQQHfmGbwTjDai7CTvg0="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2293,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:21:37.581959168Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"d6317395-0c32-52c7-bc70-949291777461","title":"[L107] Shell finalization consumes recovery ownership before fallible result construction","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L107.\n\n- `crates/tools/peritus-tools-shell/src/execution/active.rs:123-144` takes the owned process out of the active invocation before waiting for publication and building the terminal tool result. If result construction fails (including L106), the execution has neither its owner nor a stored terminal result.\n- A subsequent poll sees the underlying terminal state and attempts finalization again, which fails with `shell-owner-missing`. The adapter's `recover` path only polls this same object (`active.rs:203-213`); it does not reconstruct the result or adopt the process. This blocks recovery within this execution object after an envelope failure. In ordinary router polling, the first error is normalized to a terminal failed result and the execution object is dropped (L106), so the second finalization is not normally reached. Router recovery instead marks the outcome indeterminate and removes the active owner (`router.rs:228-268`). Higher-level durable recovery remains under examination.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQBkPvEx3JQdjWCTFc0SDvHMJj/Xl59FCZ/rzaoL55jtbqXKjQZ6vgVu5z6cadF/3wC3oCUmr5ta7kgM8ic3dDgQ="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2294,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:21:37.585362609Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"d6317395-0c32-52c7-bc70-949291777461","comment_uuid":"7b1ef59a-6ee0-4a23-bd78-5a7f25764ac2","author":"6ME5","content":"Systemic repair plan for L107: Shell finalization consumes recovery ownership before fallible result construction.\n\nOwning contract and implementation boundary: crates/tools/peritus-tools-shell/src/execution/active.rs:123-144; active.rs:203-213; router.rs:228-268. Apply the change through the constructors, live callers, durable writer and restart reader for this boundary, not as an isolated constant increase.\n\nPersist terminal process evidence and publication receipts before consuming active ownership. Make result construction an idempotent projection from that evidence, retaining the owner or reconciliation obligation until all fallible settlement steps complete. A rendering failure must be retryable without polling a missing owner or losing the original successful process outcome.\n\nPreserve: exact process birth/tree identity, confined authority, one-use dispatch receipts, monotonic cancel intent, truthful terminal/ownership settlement, complete output accounting and platform OS constraints. Separate a physical allocation/page limit and a genuine authority or integrity check from a cumulative work allowance. Keep transient contention/capacity observable and recoverable under the existing logical task; do not discard accepted state or substitute a fresh session to get around it.\n\nCompatibility/migration: retain decoders and exact receipts for previously accepted records. If representation or lifecycle semantics change, introduce a versioned migration under exclusive ownership; verify a complete replacement frontier before atomic publication and keep the old recovery root until adoption is durable. Rebuild derived projections from authoritative evidence. Update all producers, consumers and invariants together; a rejected new operation must leave the predecessor usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: long-running commands, output and stdin pressure, stalled helper/input readers, control-queue saturation, late start/exit races, parent loss and restart, proving cancellation responsiveness, no PID-reuse adoption and no duplicate process dispatch. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:21:37.467Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQFQaz+7KpDZ/+E6IjR7wZjifnfTDvrHip5Jt+aRsZncTGz+Va3Ftf1xuHF5OA/+jNHJJzSX5iRB/o7dkrxCPHg4="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2295,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:21:37.587934045Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"e8b8eabd-0cb7-5ba1-a433-54b154b85b24","title":"[L108] Shell schemas advertise inputs that the shared parser cannot admit","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L108.\n\n- `crates/tools/peritus-tools-shell/src/catalog.rs:62` advertises scripts up to **256 KiB**, but its JSON limits cap each string token at **64 KiB**. The actual parser enforces that smaller bound (L103), so scripts over 64 KiB fail before the advertised script maximum.\n- Argument arrays advertise **4096 entries**, while the shared parser also caps the aggregate number of object properties and array members at **4096**. With the two required exec object properties, the effective maximum is 4094 argument entries. The four-property script form shares at most 4092 entries across its argument arrays when all four properties are supplied. Optional extra properties consume further capacity.\n- These are declaration/enforcement mismatches rather than selected user budgets. `input.rs:119-136` inserts the script as one C2 argument, independently subject to the **64 KiB argument cap** (L096), so even constructing typed input without the JSON parser cannot reach the advertised 256 KiB script size. Tests and callers are still being read before any repair.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQDr3OsZO6b7fk1qDXOiFxFTKYK9o9epem5lS0scNngb6ezEqc8TkTuywpglK9Z3PZNC4xdq+8Qvi1XrT0Uf/uwQ="}
