usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: long-running commands, output and stdin pressure, stalled helper/input readers, control-queue saturation, late start/exit races, parent loss and restart, proving cancellation responsiveness, no PID-reuse adoption and no duplicate process dispatch. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:21:37.467Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQHvfRXkUuRPJPaW9Zw4mGqM6WJA5cUL4UYlX9VOEiffNfucC+jHLEM1KBY53FHe+s3uUooqwMOkSA/3PE+2MagI="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2297,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:21:37.594141573Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"e6184f9f-1860-50ff-ae94-f8ce7b214da0","title":"[L109] Persisted direct-command parsing excludes quoted paths and ordinary shell syntax","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L109.\n\n- `crates/tools/peritus-tools-shell/src/input.rs:44-58,94-99` rejects any control character, quote, backtick, dollar sign, pipe, ampersand, semicolon, redirection, parentheses, braces or hash in a persisted direct command. It splits only on ASCII whitespace and rejects an executable containing `=`.\n- A quoted executable/path or argument containing spaces cannot be represented through this string entry point. Known shell command-string flags are separately rejected by `ExecInput` and require the independently authorized `shell.script` route (`input.rs:185-205`). This is an intentional authority/representation distinction, not an elapsed quota; whether the product exposes an adequate structured alternative for persisted run instructions is pending caller inspection.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQMAVCx6R8VLjWlGXzLa9dfjoJHeBkWXbbtB5AGLW6Gy+pfAZ6GaZCwaEbv90Alslb40myWdpkMEYf8QicTJ/2wI="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2298,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:21:37.596488501Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"e6184f9f-1860-50ff-ae94-f8ce7b214da0","comment_uuid":"8c79968f-bad1-4586-8c88-359a8894f920","author":"6ME5","content":"Systemic repair plan for L109: Persisted direct-command parsing excludes quoted paths and ordinary shell syntax.\n\nOwning contract and implementation boundary: crates/tools/peritus-tools-shell/src/input.rs:44-58,94-99; input.rs:185-205. Apply the change through the constructors, live callers, durable writer and restart reader for this boundary, not as an isolated constant increase.\n\nExpose persisted structured executable/argument vectors as the primary direct-command representation, so spaces and quoted paths do not require a shell parser. Route actual scripts through an explicitly authorized script artifact. Preserve NUL/authority checks and exact canonical argv identity; do not repair this by accepting arbitrary shell syntax into the direct-exec authority path.\n\nPreserve: exact process birth/tree identity, confined authority, one-use dispatch receipts, monotonic cancel intent, truthful terminal/ownership settlement, complete output accounting and platform OS constraints. Separate a physical allocation/page limit and a genuine authority or integrity check from a cumulative work allowance. Keep transient contention/capacity observable and recoverable under the existing logical task; do not discard accepted state or substitute a fresh session to get around it.\n\nCompatibility/migration: retain decoders and exact receipts for previously accepted records. If representation or lifecycle semantics change, introduce a versioned migration under exclusive ownership; verify a complete replacement frontier before atomic publication and keep the old recovery root until adoption is durable. Rebuild derived projections from authoritative evidence. Update all producers, consumers and invariants together; a rejected new operation must leave the predecessor usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: long-running commands, output and stdin pressure, stalled helper/input readers, control-queue saturation, late start/exit races, parent loss and restart, proving cancellation responsiveness, no PID-reuse adoption and no duplicate process dispatch. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:21:37.467Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQDkY4hG62BX/Y/5kuW7jR/lfZtdfrOiGpf1rppcHeB2a0SBqoZ3Ka8qENH5M9W1EjWwLCEptSE0q7GjvvzdGEwQ="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2299,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:21:37.599059067Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"19696a5d-fa27-52d3-93ee-7de213bcc87d","title":"[L110] Tiny selected shell preview limits cannot contain the mandatory empty-output marker","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L110.\n\n- `crates/tools/peritus-tools-shell/src/render.rs:16-34,51-61` first applies the selected preview tail allowance, then substitutes **11 bytes** of `(no output)` whenever the rendering is empty. Selected model/human limits may be smaller than that nonempty marker (L103).\n- The terminal protocol checks the rendering against the selected allowance (L105), so an otherwise successful empty-output command can fail result construction when a caller selects a preview allowance below 11 bytes. This is another source-confirmed constructor/validator mismatch; ordinary product defaults are 16 KiB and do not trigger this case.\n- Product output projection separately limits each archived stream to **512 KiB** of head/tail with an added omission marker (`command_runtime/result.rs:9-10,116-126`). It reads the complete admitted artifact before producing the preview. The marker and lossy UTF-8 expansion are not included in that byte ceiling, so this is a preview policy rather than a strict encoded response-size bound.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQBWxLBvS/sWoQP2lFZFmSp87bka2tWfDZw/VzcmJWSPUTrpXCaoHWhNYC48uQbv1Pb1dPZ5f1EPIkHdMFjpyDAo="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2300,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:21:37.601478945Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"19696a5d-fa27-52d3-93ee-7de213bcc87d","comment_uuid":"8dee739b-ccda-4296-b99e-ce6fea2f0ec0","author":"6ME5","content":"Systemic repair plan for L110: Tiny selected shell preview limits cannot contain the mandatory empty-output marker.\n\nOwning contract and implementation boundary: crates/tools/peritus-tools-shell/src/render.rs:16-34,51-61; command_runtime/result.rs:9-10,116-126. Apply the change through the constructors, live callers, durable writer and restart reader for this boundary, not as an isolated constant increase.\n\nMake empty output a typed terminal value independent of a mandatory display marker. Construct previews against their actual final UTF-8 encoded length, including omission markers, and use a compact valid empty rendering or a referenced display when the selected allowance is tiny. Terminal effect truth must remain valid even when no nonempty text fits.\n\nPreserve: exact process birth/tree identity, confined authority, one-use dispatch receipts, monotonic cancel intent, truthful terminal/ownership settlement, complete output accounting and platform OS constraints. Separate a physical allocation/page limit and a genuine authority or integrity check from a cumulative work allowance. Keep transient contention/capacity observable and recoverable under the existing logical task; do not discard accepted state or substitute a fresh session to get around it.\n\nCompatibility/migration: retain decoders and exact receipts for previously accepted records. If representation or lifecycle semantics change, introduce a versioned migration under exclusive ownership; verify a complete replacement frontier before atomic publication and keep the old recovery root until adoption is durable. Rebuild derived projections from authoritative evidence. Update all producers, consumers and invariants together; a rejected new operation must leave the predecessor usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: long-running commands, output and stdin pressure, stalled helper/input readers, control-queue saturation, late start/exit races, parent loss and restart, proving cancellation responsiveness, no PID-reuse adoption and no duplicate process dispatch. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:21:37.467Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQIqDA7ofs+GH82k8poEyHwj98ulL45uO86c+lV/wk4r9TZUJ7PaIdA8SuC2S4JhAznFo3c9bBdmJw3EaaghyqwA="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2301,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:21:37.604028073Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"87566473-ee5e-59eb-a234-b7210b563793","title":"[L111] Router turns recoverable active-control errors into terminal closure and owner loss","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L111.\n\n- `crates/tools/peritus-tool-router/src/router.rs:272-333` removes an active entry, invokes poll/control/cancel, and converts **any** `DispatchFailure` into a terminal result. It completes the replay record and does not return the active owner, even if the error came from a rejected control request rather than process termination.\n- The shell maps C2 `CorrectRequest` (including a full 64-entry control queue, L092) to Failed/Execution/NewAction/Reauthorize (`peritus-tools-shell/src/execution/failure.rs:12-19`). Dropping the still-owned process initiates cancellation and join (L091). A transient backpressure error can therefore cancel the command and prevent further control of the original invocation.\n- If normalization itself fails (for example invalid cross-epoch timing), the replay record is marked indeterminate and the active entry is also dropped. Explicit recovery likewise removes ownership on a lost/error observation (`router.rs:228-268`). Identity fences are necessary, but these failure paths do not preserve a recoverable owner or separate control rejection from terminal execution truth.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQJgYQPZOj1lq9mz4NQS3a8RbpA1c8ZlAUSzPk/1wGEzQbZHXfujii1WZSeX/JxRstdhPrYHehdsGnUXnrKowRAs="}
