itative evidence. Update all producers, consumers and invariants together; a rejected new operation must leave the predecessor usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: long-running commands, output and stdin pressure, stalled helper/input readers, control-queue saturation, late start/exit races, parent loss and restart, proving cancellation responsiveness, no PID-reuse adoption and no duplicate process dispatch. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:21:37.467Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQJn6fX6uGZaOCm+/MMnWef5Fwh+BCAUEZCLSYIxF+uoMf7lShEqYDTdW+u1J1kQAVY0fnIivdyggVcfljrmVjAU="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2303,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:21:37.608768090Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"f73db1eb-2b32-5a15-a94c-5fada51e86c7","title":"[L112] Optional local inference still requires elapsed/CPU ceilings and fixed resource limits","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L112.\n\n- `crates/app/peritus-product-runner/src/developer_tools/command_runtime/compactor.rs:88-97,143-155` always passes the configured local-inference timeout as **Some**, derives CPU milliseconds as **four times** that timeout, and sets fixed **16 MiB scratch disk**, **32 processes**, **256 file descriptors**, and **one slot**. It adds **100 ms graceful termination** and **2000 ms reap** bounds. This path has no untimed selection in the read implementation; `context_config.rs:48-66,146-158` confirms a mandatory positive u64 timeout whenever LocalProcess is selected, with no None/zero untimed form. The semantic backend is disabled by default (`context_config.rs:99-106`); there is no default local-inference deadline because enabling it requires explicit configuration.\n- Output overflow uses **Terminate**, rather than the ordinary command path's ContinueIncomplete (`compactor.rs:113-122`), and only complete zero-exit output is accepted. Input and output retain the configured byte ceilings (L059), and **8192** process events are retained. These are auxiliary inference limits; the caller records inference failure and continues the main request (L080), so they are not themselves a main-run deadline.\n- The installed executable and model must be regular files outside both editable workspace and run-state roots, paths must be UTF-8, and a matching native restricted backend is mandatory. The isolated contract denies network/secrets, clears the environment, permits **31 descendants**, and exposes only exact inputs, scratch space and platform runtime-library roots (`compactor/sandbox.rs:17-153`). These are explicit isolation requirements, not removable synthetic time limits.\n- macOS backend discovery selects a fixed **250 ms probe timeout** (`compactor/backend.rs:36-43`). Its probe enforcer and failure recovery remain pending full-file reads; no elapsed behavior is inferred from this declaration alone.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQK6qJbfS13kIdcZg4w1xyL8KCy60CCobJrMgDKzU4/WV9yhlLckibciR3PPjgznqTCOWg8goo3pDuX9l8G925wg="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2304,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:21:37.611041940Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"f73db1eb-2b32-5a15-a94c-5fada51e86c7","comment_uuid":"adacb5fc-d8eb-424a-ad1a-3f5f87d69fa1","author":"6ME5","content":"Systemic repair plan for L112: Optional local inference still requires elapsed/CPU ceilings and fixed resource limits.\n\nOwning contract and implementation boundary: crates/app/peritus-product-runner/src/developer_tools/command_runtime/compactor.rs:88-97,143-155; context_config.rs:48-66,146-158; context_config.rs:99-106; compactor.rs:113-122; compactor/sandbox.rs:17-153; compactor/backend.rs:36-43. Apply the change through the constructors, live callers, durable writer and restart reader for this boundary, not as an isolated constant increase.\n\nMake semantic-process wall/CPU limits optional explicitly selected policies, and separate in-flight isolation limits from total inference lifetime. Stream output with backpressure instead of killing the invocation on an arbitrary transport cap. Preserve network/secret denial, protected inputs and native containment; optional inference failure must retain a deterministic main-task continuation and exact attempt receipt.\n\nPreserve: exact process birth/tree identity, confined authority, one-use dispatch receipts, monotonic cancel intent, truthful terminal/ownership settlement, complete output accounting and platform OS constraints. Separate a physical allocation/page limit and a genuine authority or integrity check from a cumulative work allowance. Keep transient contention/capacity observable and recoverable under the existing logical task; do not discard accepted state or substitute a fresh session to get around it.\n\nCompatibility/migration: retain decoders and exact receipts for previously accepted records. If representation or lifecycle semantics change, introduce a versioned migration under exclusive ownership; verify a complete replacement frontier before atomic publication and keep the old recovery root until adoption is durable. Rebuild derived projections from authoritative evidence. Update all producers, consumers and invariants together; a rejected new operation must leave the predecessor usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: long-running commands, output and stdin pressure, stalled helper/input readers, control-queue saturation, late start/exit races, parent loss and restart, proving cancellation responsiveness, no PID-reuse adoption and no duplicate process dispatch. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:21:37.467Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQMrI88EN/v0kY4HOPoBXwEi1ph08QdddM0RGJ8RqJL2w35Uz2EKk2Rgqiyjr7IHndSpAmUb5ASKxNuDeBkeazgc="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2305,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:21:37.613459918Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"c26d9b22-400c-5ecf-a723-60791bc542f5","title":"[L113] Registered-folder authority has a fixed minute window expressed on a logical clock","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L113.\n\n- `crates/app/peritus-product-runner/src/developer_tools/command_runtime/folder_patch.rs:23,194-205` supplies a fixed **60000 ms** authority window to kernel and mutation-lease commitment, independently of user-selected process deadlines. The request observes fixed logical tick **20** (`folder_patch.rs:78-90`), so this is not evidence of a one-minute wall-clock patch cancellation.\n- This still declares an artificial expiry/active-effect allowance in the committed authority model. Its relationship to settlement and recovery needs full downstream inspection (L084). The folder-patch ordinal is separately checked for u64 overflow, and plans cannot be committed by another runtime instance even with the same nominal run ID; those are representation and ownership integrity requirements.\n- Per-command authority SQLite opens use **250 ms busy timeout** (`command_runtime/journal.rs:16-26`) and collapse storage errors to string diagnostics. This is a finite contention wait, not an execution deadline. Retry treatment remains pending caller/recovery inspection.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQF/3fmEh0/ysQw+8ITx2B7wl2iSPV6Y3ymPzLdvDka1wuSffrqLSWD8eKagUKWA4m8AU4nL