{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2306,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:21:37.616052091Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"c26d9b22-400c-5ecf-a723-60791bc542f5","comment_uuid":"d4a22aa5-24ba-4a8e-91cd-5e66ba049c79","author":"6ME5","content":"Systemic repair plan for L113: Registered-folder authority has a fixed minute window expressed on a logical clock.\n\nOwning contract and implementation boundary: crates/app/peritus-product-runner/src/developer_tools/command_runtime/folder_patch.rs:23,194-205; folder_patch.rs:78-90; command_runtime/journal.rs:16-26. Apply the change through the constructors, live callers, durable writer and restart reader for this boundary, not as an isolated constant increase.\n\nRepresent folder mutation as a durable scoped authority grant and renewable fenced transaction ownership, independent of a fixed logical minute allowance. Settle the exact authorized effect and retain historical receipts. Remove the separate SQLite patience deadline through cancellable contention handling; preserve runtime-instance ownership and exact preimage/revision checks.\n\nPreserve: exact process birth/tree identity, confined authority, one-use dispatch receipts, monotonic cancel intent, truthful terminal/ownership settlement, complete output accounting and platform OS constraints. Separate a physical allocation/page limit and a genuine authority or integrity check from a cumulative work allowance. Keep transient contention/capacity observable and recoverable under the existing logical task; do not discard accepted state or substitute a fresh session to get around it.\n\nCompatibility/migration: retain decoders and exact receipts for previously accepted records. If representation or lifecycle semantics change, introduce a versioned migration under exclusive ownership; verify a complete replacement frontier before atomic publication and keep the old recovery root until adoption is durable. Rebuild derived projections from authoritative evidence. Update all producers, consumers and invariants together; a rejected new operation must leave the predecessor usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: long-running commands, output and stdin pressure, stalled helper/input readers, control-queue saturation, late start/exit races, parent loss and restart, proving cancellation responsiveness, no PID-reuse adoption and no duplicate process dispatch. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:21:37.467Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQISTmV1wVBLM6+Oi0OxJx/WFBHEtGx1EtgSmLIEBDG3TEk2NEYSwpYIJjEG5M3HyW3OLwcLEV4ku056jRgeGsAY="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2307,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:21:37.618369109Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"62e24ed6-e089-5fbb-8526-f6fce1dc960d","title":"[L114] Every production gate phase requires network authority, even for local checks","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L114.\n\n- `crates/app/peritus-product-runner/src/execution/cycle.rs:198-212` requires **Read, Write, Process and Network** before any exact-target gate launch. It makes no distinction based on whether the discovered commands use network. A run with network permission disabled cannot proceed to otherwise local verification through this path.\n- Failure is `InvalidPrecondition`; `execution/driver.rs:84-87` treats that category as fatal and returns before normal terminal settlement. Permissions are valid authority constraints, but requiring an unused capability is a broader admission blocker and bypassing ordinary retained-work settlement makes recovery less direct. Caller permission defaults and alternative local-check paths remain pending.\n- The same cycle calls phase-window checks for design/writer/fixer. The driver only starts an elapsed timer when accounting has a caller-selected remaining horizon (`driver.rs:49-82`); None has no timer here. These callers confirm L054 rather than adding an implicit main-run deadline.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQBX8AxmQ44T0bujYWwErpq2XlVStAlJdQFc+O9v9pq0/Eq6zXQmmiYOtMs9yVIswtttTtbSquVtISxdjXZ+V8As="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2308,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:21:37.620643680Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"62e24ed6-e089-5fbb-8526-f6fce1dc960d","comment_uuid":"6c1c8fe2-4c84-46c0-ba7c-c68619c9ac5a","author":"6ME5","content":"Systemic repair plan for L114: Every production gate phase requires network authority, even for local checks.\n\nOwning contract and implementation boundary: crates/app/peritus-product-runner/src/execution/cycle.rs:198-212; execution/driver.rs:84-87; driver.rs:49-82. Apply the change through the constructors, live callers, durable writer and restart reader for this boundary, not as an isolated constant increase.\n\nDerive gate permissions from the actual discovered command/backend plan. Local checks must run in a confined no-network environment without requiring unused Network authority; network-using checks need explicit network permission. Missing capability enters a retained actionable phase rather than bypassing candidate settlement as fatal InvalidPrecondition.\n\nPreserve: exact process birth/tree identity, confined authority, one-use dispatch receipts, monotonic cancel intent, truthful terminal/ownership settlement, complete output accounting and platform OS constraints. Separate a physical allocation/page limit and a genuine authority or integrity check from a cumulative work allowance. Keep transient contention/capacity observable and recoverable under the existing logical task; do not discard accepted state or substitute a fresh session to get around it.\n\nCompatibility/migration: retain decoders and exact receipts for previously accepted records. If representation or lifecycle semantics change, introduce a versioned migration under exclusive ownership; verify a complete replacement frontier before atomic publication and keep the old recovery root until adoption is durable. Rebuild derived projections from authoritative evidence. Update all producers, consumers and invariants together; a rejected new operation must leave the predecessor usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: long-running commands, output and stdin pressure, stalled helper/input readers, control-queue saturation, late start/exit races, parent loss and restart, proving cancellation responsiveness, no PID-reuse adoption and no duplicate process dispatch. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:21:37.467Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQBHjEKTnAwYEG9+9BZ6Fw2P1gsUZYqE7Br7hXoG/Awa6W0MSNwLz/+tA/ydMwve7UcEbZQWHifRVMYwoA6/0JgQ="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2309,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:21:37.622942673Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"ec7b5417-c7d2-5b7c-810c-095a5be22c9d","title":"[L115] Durable continuation is a whole-state payload with an exact version gate","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L115.\n\n- `crates/app/peritus-product-runner/src/execution/resume/durable.rs:20,89-117,133-190` clones and serializes the full baseline, design, every fixer summary, findings, diff, gates, review, developer evidence and successful command list into one JSON payload. There is no local size cap, paging, or retirement of accumulated fixer summaries in this encoder; the outer control record has a **16 MiB** representation ceiling (L021). This is a growing whole-payload admission risk, not an observed threshold crossing in the current run.\n- Decode accepts exactly **version 2**, rejects unknown fields and malformed internal tags, and contains no older-version migration here. Exact integrity checks are appropriate, but continuation from another serialized version has no repair route in this module. No specific historical session version is inferred without inspecting it.\n- `execution/summary.rs:47` and `execution/obligations.rs:114` independently truncate displayed summary/obligation text at **256 KiB**. Resume retains the individual fixer summaries even after the combined summary is truncated. The underlying bundle truncation and outer persistence callers are pending full-file inspection.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW5