Update all producers, consumers and invariants together; a rejected new operation must leave the predecessor usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: large histories and non-ASCII fields, queue/connection pressure, delayed acknowledgements, subscription gaps, disconnect/reconnect and daemon restart, proving snapshot recovery, preserved selection/context, responsive controls and no duplicate command. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:21:37.467Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQCxGhkRZwQL9sFAZaPJHWi7fclcUHCf/F/0yEdOWbeMXL5t9jGu7XK7kBD80QnKErM0XUkFZax2juPCAzH7pJQA="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2319,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:21:37.650320487Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"f6471562-c2b4-5c5f-9d2a-7061488566da","title":"[L120] Resource observation scans the whole managed tree and stops measuring at two million entries","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L120.\n\n- `crates/app/peritus-product-runner/src/resource_probe.rs:10,47-82` walks the managed workspace for initial accounting and each role/settlement sample. It skips `.git` but has no build/dependency cache exclusion, incremental update or page continuation. At more than **2000000 entries**, it returns **u64::MAX** instead of continuing measurement. Current run accounting no longer treats workspace growth as a quota (`budget.rs:122-130`), so this count bound stops observation rather than canceling the run.\n- Nested unreadable directories, entry-read failures and metadata errors are silently omitted; an unreadable root or byte/counter overflow aborts the sample as Budget, which is then reported as Deadline (L117). This can both hide unavailable measurements and turn a filesystem observation error into an apparent timeout.\n- Direct-folder accounting avoids recursive inventory and reports workspace metrics as unmeasured zero (`budget/folder.rs:7-18`, `resource_probe.rs:30-34`). Memory observation errors also become zero; on non-Linux Unix the synchronous `ps` subprocess has no elapsed bound (`resource_probe.rs:101-108`). These are measurement/liveness semantics, not justification for adding another run deadline.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1