from authoritative evidence. Update all producers, consumers and invariants together; a rejected new operation must leave the predecessor usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: valid boundary values and values just beyond each synthetic cap, final wrapper/receipt growth, non-ASCII strings, arbitrarily split frames/pages, malformed or conflicting data, mixed-version decode and save/reopen round trips. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:21:37.467Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQMhOGXBOyplQDaMyCpCHPrvl0v/1XLaZ5nt6k6sg2601BZNcwd1VOhEHE9OBH4MZJ84JqlANMEBN3FLHg0HxTQQ="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2321,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:21:37.655250963Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"90f8e1d0-74b0-56a4-bcb4-a331b7e79779","title":"[L121] Exact-target gates execute synchronously outside durable command ownership","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L121.\n\n- `crates/app/peritus-product-runner/src/gates.rs:72-142` launches external gate commands with synchronous `std::process::Command::output()`, rather than the owned C2/C4 command runtime. There is no supplied cancellation handle, process-tree owner, progress stream, stdin control, or elapsed policy at this boundary. It forces **CARGO_BUILD_JOBS=2** (also L040).\n- This function runs synchronously inside the async product loop (`execution/cycle.rs:219-226`). A blocked gate cannot observe user cancellation here, and a surrounding Tokio timeout cannot interrupt synchronous code while it is executing. Removing arbitrary elapsed deadlines must be paired with cancellable durable ownership; this path currently supplies neither. The exact operating-system behavior has not been reproduced during this read-only audit.\n- `output()` captures complete stdout/stderr in memory before applying a **512 KiB** preview per gate (`gates.rs:120-132`). The combined displayed report is then **1 MiB** (`gates.rs:217-257`). These are post-execution presentation limits, not bounded capture/backpressure. Complete program binaries are reread into memory while fingerprinting execution context (`gates.rs:179-205`).\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW