{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2322,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:21:37.657834659Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"90f8e1d0-74b0-56a4-bcb4-a331b7e79779","comment_uuid":"7b9ce914-47a9-46cb-80d8-416bc5f26d9b","author":"6ME5","content":"Systemic repair plan for L121: Exact-target gates execute synchronously outside durable command ownership.\n\nOwning contract and implementation boundary: crates/app/peritus-product-runner/src/gates.rs:72-142; execution/cycle.rs:219-226; gates.rs:120-132; gates.rs:217-257; gates.rs:179-205. Apply the change through the constructors, live callers, durable writer and restart reader for this boundary, not as an isolated constant increase.\n\nRun exact-target gates through the durable owned command runtime with cancellation, progress, output spooling and exact candidate/executable identity. Keep gate completion evidence bound to its actual process receipt, and make resource parallelism advisory. Removing timers must preserve a responsive control path throughout launch, execution and tree settlement.\n\nPreserve: exact candidate revision and artifact binding, complete finding/provenance conservation, independent reviewer evidence, truthful gate outcomes, protected user constraints and acceptance fail-closed on invalid evidence. Separate a physical allocation/page limit and a genuine authority or integrity check from a cumulative work allowance. Keep transient contention/capacity observable and recoverable under the existing logical task; do not discard accepted state or substitute a fresh session to get around it.\n\nCompatibility/migration: retain decoders and exact receipts for previously accepted records. If representation or lifecycle semantics change, introduce a versioned migration under exclusive ownership; verify a complete replacement frontier before atomic publication and keep the old recovery root until adoption is durable. Rebuild derived projections from authoritative evidence. Update all producers, consumers and invariants together; a rejected new operation must leave the predecessor usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: large and multi-file candidates, repeated valid repair cycles, changed candidate facts, delayed reviews, local/offline verification, restart mid-gate and cancellation, proving correct repair handoff without accepting a failed candidate or rereading unchanged evidence forever. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:21:37.467Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQJTt007YkRvrq07bDgsvlNwdVusH7umiWYVd4nyL1LOSPEZX+WUulOT8h7u8X0pahXSpG+ipdTvAX9tr7VV5XAU="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2323,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:21:37.660436208Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"1aece6cb-c742-5202-8d10-0a575a0e65fb","title":"[L122] Review diff omits large untracked files and truncates the candidate at one MiB","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L122.\n\n- `crates/app/peritus-product-runner/src/bundle.rs:10,74-109,152-197` includes untracked text only when each file is at most **192 KiB**, readable UTF-8, regular, and outside generated filters. It silently skips other untracked files. This specific omission path applies the fallback Git baseline; the managed-baseline branch delegates to its patch exporter (`bundle.rs:17-20`), whose enforcement remains pending.\n- Every managed or fallback diff returned by this file is prefix-truncated at **1 MiB**, potentially before later files (`bundle.rs:12-39`). The exact changed-path metadata is prepended and may itself consume this allowance. Role review receives this displayed diff, while host gate/identity paths track a broader candidate; truncation must not be mistaken for full content review.\n- `limit_text` retains the requested prefix and then appends a truncation marker outside the nominal maximum (`bundle.rs:231-237`). Diff and candidate Git subprocesses are synchronous full-output reads with no elapsed bound or cancellation hook; source-inspection errors abort the enclosing checkpoint/review boundary. These are observation and representation limits, not added wall-clock deadlines.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQEKw8Vj4t3xylhxlA6mooq+xEQbN8kDq4Zkm889XVyAAYxzNQfSLQO3ntQlJAwyVmvLEsrVJpvTnuai+Q9/3NwY="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2324,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:21:37.662815078Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"1aece6cb-c742-5202-8d10-0a575a0e65fb","comment_uuid":"578652f8-e470-4eac-a15e-41875110d825","author":"6ME5","content":"Systemic repair plan for L122: Review diff omits large untracked files and truncates the candidate at one MiB.\n\nOwning contract and implementation boundary: crates/app/peritus-product-runner/src/bundle.rs:10,74-109,152-197; bundle.rs:17-20; bundle.rs:12-39; bundle.rs:231-237. Apply the change through the constructors, live callers, durable writer and restart reader for this boundary, not as an isolated constant increase.\n\nRepresent the complete candidate as a digest-bound changed-path index with retrievable per-file diff/content pages, including large/binary/untracked changes and explicit exclusions. Review uses exact scope and can request omitted evidence by identity; a bounded preview is never full review coverage. Move Git reads into owned cancellable work and preserve final encoded page sizes.\n\nPreserve: exact candidate revision and artifact binding, complete finding/provenance conservation, independent reviewer evidence, truthful gate outcomes, protected user constraints and acceptance fail-closed on invalid evidence. Separate a physical allocation/page limit and a genuine authority or integrity check from a cumulative work allowance. Keep transient contention/capacity observable and recoverable under the existing logical task; do not discard accepted state or substitute a fresh session to get around it.\n\nCompatibility/migration: retain decoders and exact receipts for previously accepted records. If representation or lifecycle semantics change, introduce a versioned migration under exclusive ownership; verify a complete replacement frontier before atomic publication and keep the old recovery root until adoption is durable. Rebuild derived projections from authoritative evidence. Update all producers, consumers and invariants together; a rejected new operation must leave the predecessor usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: large and multi-file candidates, repeated valid repair cycles, changed candidate facts, delayed reviews, local/offline verification, restart mid-gate and cancellation, proving correct repair handoff without accepting a failed candidate or rereading unchanged evidence forever. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:21:37.467Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQEVO+YWBT4TcuvATRei7S4XbMeQSEtlLs8vxou8jgF5zhi8q2fQDQb3qG5Iwh13Ou//bgzW2XC2hBSI+w01GjwM="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2325,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:21:37.665154046Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"83ad3a39-df61-59e8-bdf6-e793bf34d168","title":"[L123] Mandatory design shape and unlimited validation retries can repeat grounding forever","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L123.\n\n- `peritus-product-runner/src/design.rs:20-21,229-248` requires a provider-generated design to contain **512 bytes through 1 MiB**, a level-one title, and at least **four level-two sections**. These requirements apply before the writer can begin, including small requests; explicit non-in-place artifact scope instead takes the deterministic design path. Grounding text is appended after the size check at lines 166-173, so the checked maximum is not the final published design size.\n- The designer uses **48 turns and 512 tool calls per segment**, but segment exhaustion continues the outer loop. Invalid design or failed grounding also retries without a total validation-attempt ceiling (`design.rs:75-173`). Each outer attempt creates fresh read-only workspace tools at lines 92-95, requiring grounding again. The correction at lines 221-225 mentions the heading requirements but omits the minimum and maximum byte requirements.\n- Daily-driving effect: a designer can return a structurally plausible but too-short design, be told to fix its headings, reread the workspace, and repeat without reaching the writer. This is a source-confirmed nonprogress path, not a claim that it caused the currently observed live run. Removing elapsed deadlines alone does not make validation retries progress-aware.\n- Scope admission at lines 192-209 recognizes only a manifest with exactly the expected version/kind keys. Missing, malformed, or extended scope metadata silently chooses source workflow, potentially bringing a request back into mandatory provider design.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQA+m+5VbKwcjamzvmTxzc0SDUBYHrS8I4h9X+jVjyLwA0GucY8/hRb9rpJqi+jm/IESOpQFegWRWKiuodBZO7AM="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2326,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:21:37.667411735Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"83ad3a39-df61-59e8-bdf6-e793bf34d168","comment_uuid":"aef38c8f-ebf8-46bd-be6b-f58f843814e5","author":"6ME5","content":"Systemic repair plan for L123: Mandatory design shape and unlimited validation retries can repeat grounding forever.\n\nOwning contract and implementation boundary: peritus-product-runner/src/design.rs:20-21,229-248; design.rs:75-173. Apply the change through the constructors, live callers, durable writer and restart reader for this boundary, not as an isolated constant increase.\n\nReplace mandatory document length/heading shape with task-fit typed design obligations and a minimal deterministic path for small tasks. Retain grounding and accepted design evidence across validation retries, return every actual violated criterion, and drive the unresolved obligation toward a writer handoff. Validate final published design plus wrappers, and treat malformed scope metadata explicitly instead of silently selecting the provider-design workflow.\n\nPreserve: governing inputs, complete pending tool protocol pairs, exact source/lineage references, explicit permissions, unresolved effect truth and task-role/native-provider identity. Separate a physical allocation/page limit and a genuine authority or integrity check from a cumulative work allowance. Keep transient contention/capacity observable and recoverable under the existing logical task; do not discard accepted state or substitute a fresh session to get around it.\n\nCompatibility/migration: retain decoders and exact receipts for previously accepted records. If representation or lifecycle semantics change, introduce a versioned migration under exclusive ownership; verify a complete replacement frontier before atomic publication and keep the old recovery root until adoption is durable. Rebuild derived projections from authoritative evidence. Update all producers, consumers and invariants together; a rejected new operation must leave the predecessor usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: long productive read/write sessions through repeated compaction and segment boundaries, source/dependency changes, non-ASCII and large evidence, interrupted checkpoint publication, then reopen the same lineage and prove that valid grounding is reused and stale targets are reread. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:21:37.467Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQLpoYUkJHWRScLt95XvtniUSpLsR2Jfg1FxCJEr/pW+H29KObSNl6xTfzdqQ9tdkRoqQFtu+G8mg8RUsv+nYFAw="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2327,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:21:37.669770620Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"57ade670-48eb-54d1-aa19-900c57503967","title":"[L124] Artifact navigation samples 2,000 entries after collecting entire directories","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L124.\n\n- `peritus-product-runner/src/design/artifact.rs:10,48-52,122-127` limits the deterministic artifact navigation sample to **2,000 entries** and explicitly tells the model when the sample is truncated. It excludes Git/build/dependency cache names rather than claiming exhaustive workspace coverage.\n- Each visited directory is collected and sorted in full before the sample bound is applied. A very large flat directory can therefore consume unbounded inventory time and allocation relative to the 2,000-entry sample. Directory enumeration or metadata failures abort design rather than returning a partial inventory with an error entry.\n- This artifact path includes the full stable conversation in its generated document and bypasses the provider-design 1 MiB normalization check (L123). This file has no elapsed deadline; cancellation/revision checks occur around inventory, not inside each synchronous directory operation. No performance reproduction has been run.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQJvFrYqoVQT+OCvKz9y5xnm1EI8uwfCl0szDuJAsTC6pKrbesVdoKHCnAiQ+aggC3QsxAVjXO8MIz/laiO+u4Qs="}
