{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2329,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:21:37.674065201Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"d6f6d455-a5b5-57d8-a34e-67ed96ba825a","title":"[L125] Reviewer segments and output are bounded while invalid submissions can trigger unlimited fresh reads","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L125.\n\n- `peritus-product-runner/src/reviewer_turn.rs:11-12,213-216` sets **32 turns**, **256 tool calls**, and **4,096 output tokens** for a reviewer segment. Segment exhaustion starts another segment; these are segment/output ceilings, not a total run duration.\n- Failed grounding or strict typed-review parsing at lines 113-121 and 173-177 retries without a total validation-attempt limit. Each attempt creates fresh read-only workspace tools (line 58); the correction at lines 205-211 demands a fresh workspace listing and authoritative file reads. Even a grounded review with a malformed submission can therefore return to mandatory reading rather than advancing.\n- `review.rs` denies unknown JSON fields and admits every finding through the review-domain constructors. Their additional count/text ceilings remain pending full reads of `peritus-review`. Source confirms this retry structure; the actual live-run cause and whether the 4,096-token output limit triggers repeated invalid JSON are not yet reproduced.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQEvLYgT9j135B3fIEWdeH76ahN0z6BtKOSs6bq0qCGiyM5gRGBtIgvuSYWxZhbReGoG7hUo5tV9Lqy0InPTlkQQ="}
