ence. Update all producers, consumers and invariants together; a rejected new operation must leave the predecessor usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: large and multi-file candidates, repeated valid repair cycles, changed candidate facts, delayed reviews, local/offline verification, restart mid-gate and cancellation, proving correct repair handoff without accepting a failed candidate or rereading unchanged evidence forever. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:21:37.467Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQGktIsAFs2pul2SIFpS9MM9a/JNyGxnmYuKMDeuVq5HjkmC/EVMfgmud2B9GjtYnbONeQrOZXpDMUtI7xWGxgwg="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2349,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:21:37.717456112Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"29f1c480-5d5e-56db-9654-381a7ea6d4df","title":"[L135] D2 quorum requires fresh context and evaluates all retained current reviews together","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L135.\n\n- `peritus-review/src/quorum.rs:55-124,187-196` requires the submitted count, complete category coverage, all selected identity/provider/model/ancestry independence dimensions, and a **fresh-context attestation on every current submitted assignment**. Fresh context is unconditional here; the other independence requirements depend on contract policy.\n- Uniqueness is evaluated over all current submissions, not a sufficient independent subset. Adding a duplicate actor/context/provider/family under an enabled dimension can therefore make a previously sufficient collection fail. A submitted cycle cannot be cancelled by `reducer/apply.rs:306-318`; advancing the candidate invalidates all previous current cycles rather than selectively replacing one. Caller policy selection and connection to native provider session reuse remain pending.\n- This is reviewer-independence acceptance policy, distinct from expiring the user's conversation or a writer's provider context. It is recorded because fresh-context/retained-review requirements can become an admission barrier; no assumption is made that every role must be ephemeral.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQEpyvVW