{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2350,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:21:37.719549628Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"29f1c480-5d5e-56db-9654-381a7ea6d4df","comment_uuid":"44973305-3414-43be-85f9-1c8291e4975e","author":"6ME5","content":"Systemic repair plan for L135: D2 quorum requires fresh context and evaluates all retained current reviews together.\n\nOwning contract and implementation boundary: peritus-review/src/quorum.rs:55-124,187-196; reducer/apply.rs:306-318. Apply the change through the constructors, live callers, durable writer and restart reader for this boundary, not as an isolated constant increase.\n\nRepresent reviewer independence as a contract-specific attestation for an assignment, separate from writer/task context persistence. Evaluate a valid sufficient quorum subset while explicitly recording excluded/duplicate submissions; support replacement or withdrawal of an unusable review without discarding valid independent evidence. Preserve required independence dimensions and candidate-binding freshness.\n\nPreserve: governing inputs, complete pending tool protocol pairs, exact source/lineage references, explicit permissions, unresolved effect truth and task-role/native-provider identity. Separate a physical allocation/page limit and a genuine authority or integrity check from a cumulative work allowance. Keep transient contention/capacity observable and recoverable under the existing logical task; do not discard accepted state or substitute a fresh session to get around it.\n\nCompatibility/migration: retain decoders and exact receipts for previously accepted records. If representation or lifecycle semantics change, introduce a versioned migration under exclusive ownership; verify a complete replacement frontier before atomic publication and keep the old recovery root until adoption is durable. Rebuild derived projections from authoritative evidence. Update all producers, consumers and invariants together; a rejected new operation must leave the predecessor usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: long productive read/write sessions through repeated compaction and segment boundaries, source/dependency changes, non-ASCII and large evidence, interrupted checkpoint publication, then reopen the same lineage and prove that valid grounding is reused and stale targets are reread. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:21:37.467Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQKCDi9jNyO9IRDytFDRzbA3QbKVjFzFQnRG5WJKxVstNHPLKS36rd/UL+Oo8069wqdV9NIjjoU6yG02ZBp3+AgA="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2351,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:21:37.721806898Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"c62f071b-109c-5296-bede-a8d2d8f5ff06","title":"[L136] D2 errors truncate diagnostics and do not distinguish exhausted history from correctable input","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L136.\n\n- `peritus-review/src/error.rs:73-80,150-159` truncates error detail to **4,096 UTF-8 bytes** without an omission marker. Source errors remain available through the error chain, but Display prints only the category and truncated detail.\n- `reject` at lines 125-145 labels **LimitExceeded** as **CorrectInput**, including immutable aggregate/count-history exhaustion where this engine provides no history-retirement action. Stale fences and replay mismatches are classified **Quarantine** rather than a simple reload, while quorum/conservation failures ask for another review. Actual caller interpretation and user-facing diagnostics remain pending; no retry storm has been demonstrated.\n- `disposition.rs:375-382` confirms every ordinary finding/fixer/confirmation evidence set must be nonempty, canonical, and at most the selected **4,096 production reference cap**; authority-request/initial-open records permit empty evidence. These integrity and authority constraints are distinct from artificial elapsed limits.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQAVdwUx02mGsYdbZRq5DG5aUSXI79ypSopQRhqOiiax9GfW+wbZwFbyG21MY+/5wyFMYDoZ3COSf8KKQXM43XQg="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2352,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:21:37.724085974Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"c62f071b-109c-5296-bede-a8d2d8f5ff06","comment_uuid":"1f6729c7-9926-4287-b7c2-bb2a6cbf4c11","author":"6ME5","content":"Systemic repair plan for L136: D2 errors truncate diagnostics and do not distinguish exhausted history from correctable input.\n\nOwning contract and implementation boundary: peritus-review/src/error.rs:73-80,150-159; disposition.rs:375-382. Apply the change through the constructors, live callers, durable writer and restart reader for this boundary, not as an isolated constant increase.\n\nReturn typed recovery actions for transient capacity, immutable old binding, stale frontier and actual corruption. Retain full structured diagnostics in referenced evidence and mark display omissions. History growth must route to paged continuation/migration rather than CorrectInput retries, while invalid identity or provenance remains a concrete integrity barrier.\n\nPreserve: exact candidate revision and artifact binding, complete finding/provenance conservation, independent reviewer evidence, truthful gate outcomes, protected user constraints and acceptance fail-closed on invalid evidence. Separate a physical allocation/page limit and a genuine authority or integrity check from a cumulative work allowance. Keep transient contention/capacity observable and recoverable under the existing logical task; do not discard accepted state or substitute a fresh session to get around it.\n\nCompatibility/migration: retain decoders and exact receipts for previously accepted records. If representation or lifecycle semantics change, introduce a versioned migration under exclusive ownership; verify a complete replacement frontier before atomic publication and keep the old recovery root until adoption is durable. Rebuild derived projections from authoritative evidence. Update all producers, consumers and invariants together; a rejected new operation must