{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2355,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:21:37.730966679Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"b4eead25-d62b-577b-a1b2-5a6ae11fb527","title":"[L138] Review bindings can be encoded with more producers than restart decoding accepts","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L138.\n\n- `peritus-review/src/wire/mod.rs:299-346` caps each producer-actor and producer-ancestry list at **1,024**, reusing the finding provenance maximum. `binding.rs:35-80,197-223` requires canonical nonempty producers but does not enforce those producer counts. `wire/mod.rs:266-296` writes them using the broader production codec collection bound (**65,535**).\n- `wire/state.rs:60-91` encodes the whole state without adding the missing producer check; only decode at lines 99-157 calls inert validation after the narrower wire checks. A small 1,025-producer binding can fit byte admission and be written, yet its command/event/checkpoint fails to decode after restart. This is a source-confirmed constructor/encoder/decoder mismatch; no executable reproduction or production caller with that producer count has been run.\n- All three review frame families require schema **v1** and closed tags. `wire/state/summary.rs:68-87` caps oscillation reasons at five because there are five named reason variants; this closed-vocabulary bound is separate from arbitrary history ceilings.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQJIbhildkN1z3BX7ZRp3CUbf7Plw1FARjcAf9VRs9AWxNnMPiojrT8mh8lT753uL