{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2363,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:21:37.750001058Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"1c961e20-873c-558d-8da4-ae1b5abe95a5","title":"[L144] Managed capture requires a complete representable Git snapshot and waits synchronously for helper processes","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L144.\n\n- **Source:** `crates/app/peritus-product-runner/src/candidate/managed.rs:51-103,106-148,152-208`; `candidate/managed/capture.rs:22-123,127-205`; `capture/directories.rs:7-70`.\n- **Blockers/enforcement:** All Git path bytes must decode as UTF-8; relative paths cannot contain `.git` components or non-normal path components. Every baseline object must be a 40- or 64-character hexadecimal Git ID, and file modes are restricted to regular/executable files, symlinks, or gitlinks. A single non-file/non-directory/non-symlink candidate, unreadable metadata, corrupt nested HEAD, or incomplete hash result aborts the whole capture. Nested repositories are captured recursively. No file-byte/count ceiling or recursion-depth ceiling exists here; 128-path hashing chunks are batching, not a total limit.\n- **Progress/recovery behavior:** Fingerprint, changed-path, and patch operations recapture the full baseline using synchronous Git children. Helper stdout/stderr and input vectors are buffered in full, with no cancellation/progress observer in this layer. Removing synthetic deadlines does not make a hung Git helper observable or recoverable. Baseline JSON is loaded fully and rejects unknown fields; there is no version migration here. Retained snapshots create Git refs that keep preimages reachable; release/retention consumers remain under review.\n- **Classification:** Representation and integrity checks plus synchronous lifecycle blockers; not an invented run timeout. These paths require cancellation/reattachment design, not a replacement hidden wall-clock deadline. No live hang or unsupported-path reproduction has been claimed.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQEfOTxyRt+uWvEIsiTIel/+U3JEnTgVEj787R5ybGwM2HQnI5AQx5fbtBVsy76y+36s8OrvONj0XLl8xbeEQEwk="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2364,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:21:37.752095139Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"1c961e20-873c-558d-8da4-ae1b5abe95a5","comment_uuid":"43c6c502-67a2-41c1-a4db-faf1a4c2b81a","author":"6ME5","content":"Systemic repair plan for L144: Managed capture requires a complete representable Git snapshot and waits synchronously for helper processes.\n\nOwning contract and implementation boundary: crates/app/peritus-product-runner/src/candidate/managed.rs:51-103,106-148,152-208; candidate/managed/capture.rs:22-123,127-205; capture/directories.rs:7-70. Apply the change through the constructors, live callers, durable writer and restart reader for this boundary, not as an isolated constant increase.\n\nCapture a versioned digest-bound Git snapshot using native path identities and paged inventory, with typed per-path unsupported facts. Execute helper hashing and Git reads as owned cancellable work and preserve the same capture intent through restart. Keep object-format, index/mode and exact baseline integrity checks; unsupported metadata cannot be silently omitted from a promised complete snapshot.\n\nPreserve: exact process birth/tree identity, confined authority, one-use dispatch receipts, monotonic cancel intent, truthful terminal/ownership settlement, complete output accounting and platform OS constraints. Separate a physical allocation/page limit and a genuine authority or integrity check from a cumulative work allowance. Keep transient contention/capacity observable and recoverable under the existing logical task; do not discard accepted state or substitute a fresh session to get around it.\n\nCompatibility/migration: retain decoders and exact receipts for previously accepted records. If representation or lifecycle semantics change, introduce a versioned migration under exclusive ownership; verify a complete replacement frontier before atomic publication and keep the old recovery root until adoption is durable. Rebuild derived projections from authoritative evidence. Update all producers, consumers and invariants together; a rejected new operation must leave the predecessor usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: long-running commands, output and stdin pressure, stalled helper/input readers, control-queue saturation, late start/exit races, parent loss and restart, proving cancellation responsiveness, no PID-reuse adoption and no duplicate process dispatch. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:21:37.467Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQP7yaxfnlcJw62HaaGbNKDD9pGeRks2G/1+V5KHgH9pjwiin73PrS9Jn/LJKfdmfV2YnVmMwbNs/aXj2WZ2sdAs="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2365,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:21:37.754266378Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"2ff6b2ef-362e-5b8d-8646-2e54ca55c75f","title":"[L145] Managed restore refuses unowned structural conflicts instead of overwriting them","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L145.\n\n- **Source:** `crates/app/peritus-product-runner/src/candidate/managed/paths.rs:10-130`; `git_path.rs:7-32`; `index.rs:54-87,109-138`.\n- **Blockers/enforcement:** A non-directory or symlink parent is never traversed. Restore refuses unowned conflicting parents and any foreign file inside a directory to be structurally replaced; empty-directory cleanup refuses remaining files. Relative Git paths must be UTF-8. Retained index stages are limited to Git's 0..3 representation, cannot duplicate a path/stage, and cannot combine stage 0 with unresolved stages; all referenced blobs must remain available.\n- **Recovery boundary:** These authority/integrity checks preserve unrelated user files and unresolved merges. They are not arbitrary workload or session quotas and should not be removed as synthetic limiters. Actual transactional recovery and error presentation are being read next. Recursive directory validation has no explicit depth, entry, time, or cancellation bound here.\n- **Classification:** Real ownership conflicts can block restore; safe resolution must preserve the conflicting files and durable recovery evidence. No live restore conflict reproduction claimed.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAA