{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2366,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:21:37.756316202Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"2ff6b2ef-362e-5b8d-8646-2e54ca55c75f","comment_uuid":"835ae9c4-a557-4d00-8fc6-9e6b46f1034f","author":"6ME5","content":"Systemic repair plan for L145: Managed restore refuses unowned structural conflicts instead of overwriting them.\n\nOwning contract and implementation boundary: crates/app/peritus-product-runner/src/candidate/managed/paths.rs:10-130; git_path.rs:7-32; index.rs:54-87,109-138. Apply the change through the constructors, live callers, durable writer and restart reader for this boundary, not as an isolated constant increase.\n\nKeep the unowned-file and structural-conflict fences. Add a durable conflict-resolution workflow that preserves foreign files and binds explicit user authorization to the exact conflicting preimages before continuing the same restore. Make recursive verification cancellable and progress-addressed; native path representation must not weaken symlink/ancestor safety or unresolved-merge preservation.\n\nPreserve: exact snapshot/preimage identity, protected paths, ancestor and symlink safety, writable-fork coverage, conflict detection, one logical restore transaction and exact effect receipts. Separate a physical allocation/page limit and a genuine authority or integrity check from a cumulative work allowance. Keep transient contention/capacity observable and recoverable under the existing logical task; do not discard accepted state or substitute a fresh session to get around it.\n\nCompatibility/migration: retain decoders and exact receipts for previously accepted records. If representation or lifecycle semantics change, introduce a versioned migration under exclusive ownership; verify a complete replacement frontier before atomic publication and keep the old recovery root until adoption is durable. Rebuild derived projections from authoritative evidence. Update all producers, consumers and invariants together; a rejected new operation must leave the predecessor usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: large-file and many-path capture/restore, divergent preimage rejection, interrupted staging/publication/restore, then reopen and continue the same conversation with an exact restored workspace. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:21:37.467Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQJVFxPP6azFPBkKJ5aTPX51tuny4hOOT1d0+PMrWxYc9QVT9zLuv9xQOI/02chPApxfMNNNjQLPhjsTKpZg2vgM="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2367,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:21:37.758346622Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"515eb153-80a6-5c47-938c-7fc7c8e79baf","title":"[L146] Discard holds Git locks across restoration and can wait indefinitely without a control channel","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L146.\n\n- **Source:** `crates/app/peritus-product-runner/src/candidate/managed/head/prepared.rs:69-132,142-198`; `head.rs:37-118`; `restore.rs:24-57,109-159,183-219`; `recovery.rs:52-105`.\n- **Blockers/enforcement:** HEAD preparation starts a synchronous `git update-ref --stdin` transaction and waits for exact `start: ok`, `prepare: ok`, and `commit: ok` lines. Its locks remain held through source/index restoration. Neither these reads nor child waits have cancellation or reattachment here; Drop closes stdin and then synchronously waits too. Failure diagnostics read at most 8,192 stderr bytes without a truncation marker. Symbolic HEAD restoration requires an ordinary HEAD file, exclusive HEAD.lock, unchanged observed HEAD, and a fresh absent restored-branch name.\n- **Recovery constraints:** Preflight verifies all required source/index blobs and nested repositories before restoration. New repository recovery uses filesystem rename into the owner's `.git/peritus/discarded` directory; a cross-filesystem rename or denied permission fails instead of falling back to a copy. Windows symlink restoration accepts only UTF-8 file-link targets and requires OS support/permission. These environment constraints can block discard, with retained paths included in relevant errors.\n- **Persistence distinction:** Recovery directories and displaced commit refs are deliberately retained; branches are not rewritten. There is no elapsed expiry or automatic cleanup of archived repositories here. Retained-repository consumers are fully read: `retention/store.rs:18-68,139-187` requires the correct SHA-1/SHA-256 store and an exact source-tree/index manifest match; `retention/restore.rs:91-115,165-251` explicitly refuses cross-filesystem reconstruction on Unix and preserves recreated destinations. Transactional restart consumers are being read next.\n- **Classification:** Synchronous process-control gaps and authority/environment fences. No proposed repair should reintroduce an arbitrary kill timer to mask them. Source confirmed, not a demonstrated live lockup.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQBEs8q0rCYjyyHAqZzt+Bx/21PFIpjjXn5ISU6/idQ59KNRhDUobMkyBxnYpB1KpWeU5SlQA6+Lr3XxuSPxMJgs="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2368,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:21:37.760692465Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"515eb153-80a6-5c47-938c-7fc7c8e79baf","comment_uuid":"f8ca8e8a-ceb3-4144-9f58-77349e93777c","author":"6ME5","content":"Systemic repair plan for L146: Discard holds Git locks across restoration and can wait indefinitely without a control channel.\n\nOwning contract and implementation boundary: crates/app/peritus-product-runner/src/candidate/managed/head/prepared.rs:69-132,142-198; head.rs:37-118; restore.rs:24-57,109-159,183-219; recovery.rs:52-105; retention/store.rs:18-68,139-187; retention/restore.rs:91-115,165-251. Apply the change through the constructors, live callers, durable writer and restart reader for this boundary, not as an isolated constant increase.\n\nModel discard as a durable transaction with owned Git handshake, preparation, workspace/index restoration and final publication phases. Keep controls responsive while exact Git locks are held, and reconcile interruption from recorded before/after facts. Support a verified staged-copy fallback for cross-filesystem archives when authorized, preserving displaced repositories and commits rather than force-overwriting conflicts.\n\nPreserve: exact snapshot/preimage identity, protected paths, ancestor and symlink safety, writable-fork coverage, conflict detection, one logical restore transaction and exact effect receipts. Separate a physical allocation/page limit and a genuine authority or integrity check from a cumulative work allowance. Keep transient contention/capacity observable and recoverable under the existing logical task; do not discard accepted state or substitute a fresh session to get around it.\n\nCompatibility/migration: retain decoders and exact receipts for previously accepted records. If representation or lifecycle semantics change, introduce a versioned migration under exclusive ownership; verify a complete replacement frontier before atomic publication and keep the old recovery root until adoption is durable. Rebuild derived projections from authoritative evidence. Update all producers, consumers and invariants together; a rejected new operation must leave the predecessor usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: large-file and many-path capture/restore, divergent preimage rejection, interrupted staging/publication/restore, then reopen and continue the same conversation with an exact restored workspace. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:21:37.467Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQO/SasJywrejQVb0U1hb2ReeWqm6lH0Mbarq92RWaTt86ddCDgvFp48zccLjAzc3AFooSn3zRFRU64ERA+R6BQo="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2369,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:21:37.763160815Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"a6002d2f-f8b5-560a-af15-1892d5b7b42d","title":"[L147] Retained repository recovery depends on exact local metadata and has no migration or cancellation here","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L147.\n\n- **Source:** `crates/app/peritus-product-runner/src/candidate/managed/retention.rs:20-31,42-109`; `retention/linked.rs:42-65`; `retention/metadata.rs:44-102,104-159`; `retention/store.rs:18-68,70-175,190-249`; `retention/restore.rs:48-115,254-301`.\n- **Blockers/enforcement:** Only SHA-1 (40-character) and SHA-256 (64-character) Git object formats are accepted. Retained manifests reject unknown fields, source-tree/index mismatch, invalid modes/object/path IDs, a path serving as both file and directory, and file parents. Linked recovery requires its original administrative database to remain accessible through ordinary directory ancestors; it does not independently relocate or duplicate that shared database. Unsupported Git metadata node types, non-UTF-8 names, missing backups, or replaced parents abort reconstruction.\n- **Persistence/work behavior:** Entire ref and reflog root sets are pinned and fetched locally; fetch explicitly disables automatic GC. Complete metadata trees are retained except object directories and specified transient lock files. No count, byte, depth, expiry, or cancellation bound exists in these retention functions; 64-root fetch batches are not a total limit. Whole JSON manifests and most helper outputs are buffered. All this work is synchronous and can delay recovery without progress events at this layer.\n- **Classification:** Exact-identity/integrity fences and synchronous recovery gaps, distinct from synthetic workload caps. Durable retained data should support compatible evolution and explicit conflict resolution; there is no version migration or alternate linked-database recovery in these files. Fully read `tests/retained.rs:225-241` establishes the narrow legacy behavior: a baseline missing the optional retained property can restore an existing child, while deleted-child recovery fails without an independent backup. Caller-facing restart handling remains under review. No live failure reproduction claimed.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQGQ+rPovTnzRvfQsWT4DuqdfD4dZ2SH13kKE1QuoCi0uUkR/tibMbwXqKTBiAYGA3tVw6+5vbgqMTq2rBZPTLgY="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2370,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:21:37.765294097Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"a6002d2f-f8b5-560a-af15-1892d5b7b42d","comment_uuid":"c0aa567e-093c-4733-b115-ca6b7ef80df0","author":"6ME5","content":"Systemic repair plan for L147: Retained repository recovery depends on exact local metadata and has no migration or cancellation here.\n\nOwning contract and implementation boundary: crates/app/peritus-product-runner/src/candidate/managed/retention.rs:20-31,42-109; retention/linked.rs:42-65; retention/metadata.rs:44-102,104-159; retention/store.rs:18-68,70-175,190-249; retention/restore.rs:48-115,254-301; tests/retained.rs:225-241. Apply the change through the constructors, live callers, durable writer and restart reader for this boundary, not as an isolated constant increase.\n\nVersion retained-repository manifests and persist exact backup roots for linked administrative databases when recovery promises deleted-child restoration. Reconstruct through cancellable paged metadata/ref operations with progress receipts and explicit relocation/adoption. Preserve Git object format, source-tree/index equivalence, modes and foreign structural conflicts; missing backup evidence remains a scoped repair obligation.\n\nPreserve: committed command/event identity, exact causal and digest roots, exclusive ownership, atomic publication, reference-safe artifact retention and verified recovery from the last durable frontier. Separate a physical allocation/page limit and a genuine authority or integrity check from a cumulative work allowance. Keep transient contention/capacity observable and recoverable under the existing logical task; do not discard accepted state or substitute a fresh session to get around it.\n\nCompatibility/migration: retain decoders and exact receipts for previously accepted records. If representation or lifecycle semantics change, introduce a versioned migration under exclusive ownership; verify a complete replacement frontier before atomic publication and keep the old recovery root until adoption is durable. Rebuild derived projections from authoritative evidence. Update all producers, consumers and invariants together; a rejected new operation must leave the predecessor usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: history beyond the reported count/byte boundaries, lock contention lasting beyond the old patience window, lost commit acknowledgements followed by later progress, torn uncommitted tails and true committed corruption, then reopen and resolve exact historical receipts. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:21:37.467Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQP7wXplTqz2+M5YCaYmhrvkrEKfMsSzx9yYruuuxfw55wyQSRPUcsBMp0/mKBUVXoJKVpci2j2yFnu5igmLXFQw="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2371,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:21:37.767569465Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"f2ff7f7c-41d0-5eff-a4df-0a9049d945f0","title":"[L148] Managed discard recovery adds a fixed 64 MiB whole-state ceiling","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L148.\n\n- **Source:** `crates/app/peritus-product-runner/src/candidate/managed/transaction/state.rs:13-15,19-29,76-124`; `transaction/mod.rs:25-73,90-112,144-197`.\n- **Limits/enforcement:** Every checksummed discard-state JSON payload is limited to 64 MiB; readers accept at most that payload plus a 40-byte header and reject oversize/corrupt/unknown-field records. The document contains BOTH the original baseline and the before-discard snapshot, plus all root identities, owners, owned paths, assets, HEAD facts, and recovery records. Each registration/seal/recovery/phase update serializes and rewrites the entire document before checking its final size.\n- **Failure/recovery:** Initial admission fails if the complete plan exceeds this fixed ceiling. An initially valid plan can later exceed it as preparation/recovery evidence grows; a late save failure stops the operation, including after some restore effects. There is no chunked journal, spill storage, caller configuration, state migration beyond version 1, or alternate recovery representation here. `execute` can retry Prepared/Restoring from retained evidence and returns Completed idempotently, subject to all validation and cleanup barriers.\n- **Classification:** Product-selected storage ceiling, separate from checksum/authority requirements and available disk space. Source-confirmed; no 64 MiB boundary fixture or live reproduction executed.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQKhEgaz0FT6xNzIfWVA8DcKE16zTex4Zywg8qZKc4FkShaxSPTohKtEN9dbJYKiheq3VxVzs6T483EUn1dmixgI="}
