st leave the predecessor usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: large-file and many-path capture/restore, divergent preimage rejection, interrupted staging/publication/restore, then reopen and continue the same conversation with an exact restored workspace. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:21:37.467Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQNv6EM+kW6+whfEvHUP7lMKJxLT7Kx+mbvgY5tuYxFTJBwEV5UjwJJQUAUcBxMao7qDfAdGQjeai9AJinEWldgw="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2373,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:21:37.772057545Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"46992279-83bc-5ddb-9f40-1833df28b0c4","title":"[L149] Incomplete or changed discard preparation blocks restart cleanup with no repair operation in this module","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L149.\n\n- **Source:** `crates/app/peritus-product-runner/src/candidate/managed/transaction/owned.rs:52-75,92-168,176-235,244-303`; `transaction/mod.rs:95-109,200-232`; preparation callers `restore/sources.rs:93-118` and `restore/prepared.rs:200-229`.\n- **Blockers/enforcement:** Restart checks EVERY recorded staging asset before cleaning any of them. Assets require an exact 90-byte ownership nonce, expected names/ancestors, a closed set of leaf filenames, and a matching sealed directory digest once payload leaves exist. A crash after writing a payload but before persisting its seal leaves `sealed=None`; the next cleanup rejects that asset as incomplete or changed. A foreign entry, changed marker/parent, or replaced Git lock similarly blocks the entire retry. The owner-file lock uses immediate `try_lock`, with no queue/retry here. Marker reading takes 257 bytes for identity checking, not a source-file limit.\n- **Recovery distinction:** Preserving foreign or uncertain data is necessary; deleting it would violate ownership. However, this module exposes inspect/execute/prepare, without an explicit path to preserve an uncertain asset separately and then resume recovery. Whether callers expose such resolution remains pending. Test-only publication barriers are compiled out of shipped builds and are not runtime synthetic deadlines.\n- **Classification:** Persistent recovery dead-end candidate, rooted in state/ownership transitions rather than an elapsed timeout. The unsealed crash interval is source-confirmed; the crash tests are now fully read, not run. `transaction/tests/crash.rs:33-40,74-96` kills at Prepared and each completed publication barrier, after preparation seals are recorded; it does not inject a kill between payload write and seal save. `transaction/tests.rs:194-208` confirms uncertain/replaced staging is preserved and refuses execution.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQL0tgVBETaB5WZk3YORFyEmn8x4RqmxYJlLgweSxwqTMX4aJLGJQ+sL0GJBC14UsgcTes+fdploHKhf0fQNg7wI="}
