p the old recovery root until adoption is durable. Rebuild derived projections from authoritative evidence. Update all producers, consumers and invariants together; a rejected new operation must leave the predecessor usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: large-file and many-path capture/restore, divergent preimage rejection, interrupted staging/publication/restore, then reopen and continue the same conversation with an exact restored workspace. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:21:37.467Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQDtdwbGA+soSLlHIyJMYQnK9EmGDiXkU+xxKqQqfcenBuKEJ8J/cLDMx12byC+IQ9Pmu2+5fJl+1nephX0h3yAk="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2375,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:21:37.776545298Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"45267f3d-31e8-5869-b28c-dfa3a289d4a1","title":"[L150] Discard restart accepts only recorded before/after states and rechecks the entire workspace","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L150.\n\n- **Source:** `crates/app/peritus-product-runner/src/candidate/managed/transaction/validation.rs:130-171,194-315`; `validation/paths.rs:63-130,139-179`; `validation/directories.rs:18-75`.\n- **Blockers/enforcement:** Each recorded repository's HEAD selection, administrative path, and permissions must equal its before or admitted after state; owned source/index entries must likewise equal their original or restored values. A partial archive gap is accepted only with the retained directory's exact content/permission digest. New repositories moving as a unit cannot contain unrecorded partial edits. Facts restrict permissions to 0o7777 and Git refs/objects to valid representations. Source changes outside the owned path set remain preserved; repository identity changes are independently fenced.\n- **Work/recovery behavior:** Every transition/postimage validation recaptures the complete managed workspace with a retained index and rechecks all roots. Archive proof hashes the entire archived tree, including all regular-file bytes and sorted directory entries; the 64 KiB read buffer is streaming, not a file cap. Unsupported filesystem nodes abort. No cancellation, entry, depth, or elapsed bound exists in these functions. Unrecorded conflicts are preserved and returned as errors, without automatic reconciliation here.\n- **Classification:** Integrity/authority fences are necessary; potential recovery latency and conflict resolution gaps should be repaired without discarding user edits or inventing replacement deadlines. Source confirmed; caller-facing conflict recovery remains pending.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQFjpPYyGMsOYfTkA7mUAoW0IYsfxmTnsgp97qj2crhQyJiVaxZPUaCTrERlsaqt3MPRTAMzgGeeohEeUzu3RHAc="}
