ers, consumers and invariants together; a rejected new operation must leave the predecessor usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: large-file and many-path capture/restore, divergent preimage rejection, interrupted staging/publication/restore, then reopen and continue the same conversation with an exact restored workspace. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:21:37.467Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQKsUuXaH24UebnS4EpFsGuPpwHOlOTc/u3Kz7r+dB9Fez9vg6vfPQV5KxTd9wBje8bEE67mhBmoHKKnu4OoMkAY="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2377,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:21:37.781477741Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"80cdf3c8-7131-5fb6-9031-9b8f0fb58763","title":"[L152] Trace append has no size limit but local-context recovery refuses traces above 1 GiB","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L152.\n\n- **Source:** `crates/app/peritus-product-runner/src/trace.rs:207-215`; `trace/local_memory.rs:59-65,76-131`; related torn-tail behavior L060.\n- **Limits/enforcement:** The trace writer continually appends complete provider/tool/checkpoint records without checking total size. Local-memory observation replay refuses the entire trace once file length exceeds 1 GiB and refuses each scoped-tool frame above 64 MiB. These checks occur before selecting the requested scope; scoped frames for other scopes are also deserialized and version/sequence checked first. Schema version must equal 1, invocation/sequence must be nonzero, and records reject unknown fields; reconstructed arguments/output must meet production canonical-JSON bounds.\n- **Failure/recovery:** A run can write successfully for a long time and then become unrecoverable through this reader after restart. Traces are shared across records/scopes at this path, so unrelated retained history contributes to the total limit. The reader returns torn-tail presence and requires append work to stop pending recovery; it does not repair that tail. There is no rotation, indexed scope seek, paging, compatible migration, or configurable growth policy in these files.\n- **Classification:** Fixed recovery-only storage limits create a persistence mismatch. Genuine malformed/torn data needs safe recovery, while ordinary retained growth should not invalidate the session. Source confirmed; no 1 GiB reproduction or live causal attribution claimed.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQFtW33GSKvXbX9ciNqpLgrYREnmlSDBIhYFHPLzfIABYBv/ksaIV/wzEEzklHXU1AapbPIhaAHKsOy+T9sPrbQY="}
