root until adoption is durable. Rebuild derived projections from authoritative evidence. Update all producers, consumers and invariants together; a rejected new operation must leave the predecessor usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: valid boundary values and values just beyond each synthetic cap, final wrapper/receipt growth, non-ASCII strings, arbitrarily split frames/pages, malformed or conflicting data, mixed-version decode and save/reopen round trips. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:21:37.467Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQPctQ0ddl4rntEgDE+Fi+asbPRUK7LNQL/GW1DG+7Jf15m56rgJjgvpqhkr/QgpUhHvOkjEgIVUoOczk6en47wI="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2389,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:21:37.807758007Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"a8cc5bd2-3a32-5c95-9e97-9f4962e40355","title":"[L158] Pinning a queued input prevents later edit, hold, or withdrawal until the old pin is explicitly cleared","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L158.\n\n- **Source:** `crates/app/peritus-product-runner/src/control/context.rs:80-108,119-127`; `control/record/transition/mutations.rs:132-145,148-170`; `control/record/transition.rs:29-60`; `control/record/projection.rs:206-214`.\n- **Blockers/enforcement:** Input pins name an exact latest revision and require Queued/Incorporated state. Queue/brief edits refresh brief bindings but leave context pins unchanged. Every successor validates all pins, so changing a pinned revision or holding/withdrawing it causes the entire control operation to fail InvalidInput. Clearing a preference also validates its target before removal; an already-invalid imported pin cannot be repaired through ordinary apply because current validation runs first.\n- **Recovery distinction:** Atomic successor planning prevents the ordinary edit from persisting invalid state. A user can clear a still-valid pin first, then edit or hold the input; this is a two-step workflow obstruction, not evidence that normal edits persist a permanently invalid record. No automatic pin rebinding or explicit stale-pin repair exists in these functions.\n- **Classification:** Context-preference lifecycle blocker/diagnostic gap; exact historical identity should be preserved while source treatment evolves. Source confirmed; dedicated pin/edit reproduction and caller/UI resolution remain pending.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQBbHFdvuqIfj8JIkCh0mlJVtudDiL3fxgBsG0IYGhvCl7Awtwe3Dz+cz/oc0+5Dbg7Ct3/63zOYIsZyElURo9AA="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2390,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:21:37.810028324Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"a8cc5bd2-3a32-5c95-9e97-9f4962e40355","comment_uuid":"a00724a1-1a77-4cea-ae13-b7e0b6648e15","author":"6ME5","content":"Systemic repair plan for L158: Pinning a queued input prevents later edit, hold, or withdrawal until the old pin is explicitly cleared.\n\nOwning contract and implementation boundary: crates/app/peritus-product-runner/src/control/context.rs:80-108,119-127; control/record/transition/mutations.rs:132-145,148-170; control/record/transition.rs:29-60; control/record/projection.rs:206-214. Apply the change through the constructors, live callers, durable writer and restart reader for this boundary, not as an isolated constant increase.\n\nMake input revision/treatment and context-pin rebinding one atomic operation. Editing, holding or withdrawing a pinned input must retain the historical pin meaning while explicitly updating or suspending its active treatment. Add a scoped stale-pin repair transition that validates exact source history without requiring an already-valid current projection.\n\nPreserve: durable logical session and run identity, exact command receipts, atomic snapshot/cursor binding, explicit authority, selected UI state, complete history retrieval and owned-effect reconciliation. Separate a physical allocation/page limit and a genuine authority or integrity check from a cumulative work allowance. Keep transient contention/capacity observable and recoverable under the existing logical task; do not discard accepted state or substitute a fresh session to get around it.\n\nCompatibility/migration: retain decoders and exact receipts for previously accepted records. If representation or lifecycle semantics change, introduce a versioned migration under exclusive ownership; verify a complete replacement frontier before atomic publication and keep the old recovery root until adoption is durable. Rebuild derived projections from authoritative evidence. Update all producers, consumers and invariants together; a rejected new operation must leave the predecessor usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: large histories and non-ASCII fields, queue/connection pressure, delayed acknowledgements, subscription gaps, disconnect/reconnect and daemon restart, proving snapshot recovery, preserved selection/context, responsive controls and no duplicate command. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:21:37.467Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQIyEbC0FaSX6vl77AoCdgVCShJaZdI+Joly0ZT5pck4qJHPMxU1Xdu89WvT8Dg1plQsxHF2nwMU1Z+dJxW1JyQE="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2391,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:21:37.812102174Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"2fe71a8d-d12e-5467-939b-fe51d482a697","title":"[L159] Input admission retains and revalidates all history, with 65,535-item dependency and incorporation lists","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L159.\n\n- **Source:** `crates/app/peritus-product-runner/src/control/inputs/transition.rs:29-47,78-123,177-272`; `control/inputs.rs:57-67,193-200`; enclosing whole-record storage limits L021/L154/L157.\n- **Limits/enforcement:** Each input dependency list and each invocation's incorporated selection list must fit u16, at most 65,535 items. Every input uses an 8,192-byte text type. Revision and generation increments are checked u64. All superseded, withdrawn, incorporated revisions and invocation bindings remain in the same aggregate; no pruning occurs here. Every queue change clones and validates the entire history, including repeated linear earlier/latest/exact searches, before/after mutation.\n- **Workflow barriers:** Incorporated inputs cannot be edited or withdrawn; corrections append a new dependent identity. A pending input cannot be withdrawn while another pending/held item depends on it. Reordering must include the entire pending/held identity set in dependency order. Historical branch snapshots convert queued inputs to Held until explicitly released. These lifecycle/dependency requirements are separate from synthetic history-capacity limits.\n- **Classification:** Per-list representation caps plus fixed whole-state/request ceilings on indefinitely retained history. Potential increasing validation cost is source-derived, not benchmarked. No elapsed expiry or automatic session deletion exists here.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQEPgAEsKeUXfNDGUpHRl+x1fhyei32XmA8/bWh3EaHnq6zGdEA5m0ujskWIrD78Cq1vAOH24BwtySbF5LxZN3wQ="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2392,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:21:37.814385826Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"2fe71a8d-d12e-5467-939b-fe51d482a697","comment_uuid":"ac91eee3-97ab-44e5-aa86-b9ae1a414e51","author":"6ME5","content":"Systemic repair plan for L159: Input admission retains and revalidates all history, with 65,535-item dependency and incorporation lists.\n\nOwning contract and implementation boundary: crates/app/peritus-product-runner/src/control/inputs/transition.rs:29-47,78-123,177-272; control/inputs.rs:57-67,193-200. Apply the change through the constructors, live callers, durable writer and restart reader for this boundary, not as an isolated constant increase.\n\nSeparate immutable input revision/dependency history from the indexed active queue and incorporation frontier. Page large dependency/selection sets and validate affected edges incrementally. Preserve dependent ordering, incorporated-input immutability and explicit correction provenance without cloning or revalidating every historical record on each queue edit.\n\nPreserve: durable logical session and run identity, exact command receipts, atomic snapshot/cursor binding, explicit authority, selected UI state, complete history retrieval and owned-effect reconciliation. Separate a physical allocation/page limit and a genuine authority or integrity check from a cumulative work allowance. Keep transient contention/capacity observable and recoverable under the existing logical task; do not discard accepted state or substitute a fresh session to get around it.\n\nCompatibility/migration: retain decoders and exact receipts for previously accepted records. If representation or lifecycle semantics change, introduce a versioned migration under exclusive ownership; verify a complete replacement frontier before atomic publication and keep the old recovery root until adoption is durable. Rebuild derived projections from authoritative evidence. Update all producers, consumers and invariants together; a rejected new operation must leave the predecessor usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: large histories and non-ASCII fields, queue/connection pressure, delayed acknowledgements, subscription gaps, disconnect/reconnect and daemon restart, proving snapshot recovery, preserved selection/context, responsive controls and no duplicate command. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:21:37.467Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQLBfjl3LYwYXmyU3ClMIu+CBrpFhpqBwrOImLlmHR7zghoZ6afRwdI10k7fhwE5eUFxpqxKE4YL09bIhc7ebKAo="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2393,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:21:37.816586228Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"2a52df1b-186c-5f7c-a7e1-f5102beee11a","title":"[L160] Clearing a goal cancels its record but does not permit a new goal in the same conversation through these controls","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L160.\n\n- **Source:** `crates/app/peritus-product-runner/src/control/record/transition/goal.rs:71-100,219-264`; previously read goal lifecycle L031-L034.\n- **Blockers/enforcement:** StartExecution rejects archived conversations, any existing execution, zero run ID, or an empty eligible pending input view. StartGoal rejects ANY existing goal record and requires exact equality with the current brief objective before starting execution. ClearGoal invokes `goal.cancel` rather than removing the goal/execution bindings; this module exposes no transition that clears either retained binding. Therefore a fresh StartGoal/StartExecution after cancellation is refused by these controls, even though the cancelled evidence is correctly retained.\n- **Recovery distinction:** Existing execution/goal continuation has separate controls, and caller/UI behavior has not yet been traced. This finding does not assert all follow-up messages fail; it identifies the explicit new-run/new-goal path and its lack of a successor lineage transition. Fork/new conversation may provide an alternate path, but should not be assumed equivalent to continuing the user's session/context.\n- **Classification:** Persistent lifecycle/authority ownership obstruction, not a quota or timeout. Exact lineage must be preserved while replacement authority can be explicitly admitted. Source confirmed; caller reproduction pending.\n\n- Daemon continuation traced: `crates/app/peritus-daemon/src/product_run/lifecycle.rs:148-158` explicitly permits retrying WaitingForUser or Complete when new pending chat input exists, and explicit goal resume has its own idle allowance. Existing conversation execution can continue; the earlier finding concerns replacement StartGoal/StartExecution binding, not all follow-up turns.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQPVHIBplaOGOi+RJbezuOkTH+Ghp2SyavDxA0FYCYXv7Xewm8cYfqug6BxjvRJMduF9N9dpSXkW2C/1m4DEBQw0="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2394,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:21:37.818747683Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"2a52df1b-186c-5f7c-a7e1-f5102beee11a","comment_uuid":"55184439-3f62-4426-8867-bc581df1e4b2","author":"6ME5","content":"Systemic repair plan for L160: Clearing a goal cancels its record but does not permit a new goal in the same conversation through these controls.\n\nOwning contract and implementation boundary: crates/app/peritus-product-runner/src/control/record/transition/goal.rs:71-100,219-264; crates/app/peritus-daemon/src/product_run/lifecycle.rs:148-158. Apply the change through the constructors, live callers, durable writer and restart reader for this boundary, not as an isolated constant increase.\n\nModel goals/executions as successor epochs within one durable conversation rather than an optional field that can never be replaced. Clearing a goal settles its authority while retaining historical accounting and evidence; explicitly admit a new objective epoch after prior owned effects are reconciled. Preserve same-session context and distinguish follow-up continuation from a new goal grant.\n\nPreserve: durable logical session and run identity, exact command receipts, atomic snapshot/cursor binding, explicit authority, selected UI state, complete history retrieval and owned-effect reconciliation. Separate a physical allocation/page limit and a genuine authority or integrity check from a cumulative work allowance. Keep transient contention/capacity observable and recoverable under the existing logical task; do not discard accepted state or substitute a fresh session to get around it.\n\nCompatibility/migration: retain decoders and exact receipts for previously accepted records. If representation or lifecycle semantics change, introduce a versioned migration under exclusive ownership; verify a complete replacement frontier before atomic publication and keep the old recovery root until adoption is durable. Rebuild derived projections from authoritative evidence. Update all producers, consumers and invariants together; a rejected new operation must leave the predecessor usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: large histories and non-ASCII fields, queue/connection pressure, delayed acknowledgements, subscription gaps, disconnect/reconnect and daemon restart, proving snapshot recovery, preserved selection/context, responsive controls and no duplicate command. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:21:37.467Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQP8SDMT40okEDduM2kl+Zs6ExG3NHBGFKknePyZ43d0me7BH9XLCidiEDRHS+hr0YpBZhAxh0Znov27u6VPLWAw="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2395,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:21:37.820800925Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"2821142e-9374-5df0-bc7f-e094b722791d","title":"[L161] A historical fork with a pinned queued input fails its own child-state validation","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L161.\n\n- **Source:** `crates/app/peritus-product-runner/src/control/record/seed.rs:31-53`; `control/inputs/transition.rs:10-18`; `control/context.rs:119-127`; child creation `control/record/transition.rs:94-106,57-58`; aggregate validation `control/record/projection.rs:206-210`.\n- **Blocker/enforcement:** Historical seed generation converts queued inputs to Held so a child cannot silently inherit pending execution. It clones the source context-preference ledger unchanged, including exact input pins. Pins require Queued or Incorporated state. Installing such a seed in the child and validating it therefore rejects a queued input's retained pin as InvalidInput. A valid source conversation can generate a seed that cannot become a valid fork.\n- **Recovery distinction:** Clearing the pin before forking can avoid the mismatch but changes the user's selected context treatment. The root cause is incompatible transformations of queue lifecycle and context treatment, not missing deadline configuration. No automatic reconciliation preserves the pin's historical meaning in the child here.\n- **Classification:** Source-confirmed fork/context lifecycle blocker; no runtime reproduction claimed. Independent child execution authority must remain separate while copied public context becomes internally valid.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signa