{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2401,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:21:37.833544357Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"03a399b2-b897-527e-96ff-3dba9a9f79b1","title":"[L164] Hunk leave-alone feedback protects the whole path until explicit dismissal","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L164.\n\n- **Source:** `crates/app/peritus-product-runner/src/control/review.rs:231-255,314-316`; `control/review/ledger.rs:26-45,109-155,235-247`; related command blocker L044.\n- **Blockers/enforcement:** Even a hunk-level LeaveAlone anchor makes the complete path protected because the backend cannot safely confine command writes to line ranges. Every undismissed such comment remains a hard constraint independently of projected diff staleness. Rebinding explicitly changes the protected path; dismissal explicitly releases it and appends a correction after incorporation. Explain/KeepBehavior are read-only/semantic preferences, not execution grants; pending pipeline preference derives from the newest queued anchored comment's feedback kind.\n- **Classification:** User-selected authority narrowing, not an arbitrary session quota. Preserve its protection during repairs; improving confinement and clear release/rebind behavior can remove unnecessary whole-command obstruction without silently widening authority. Actual prompt/mode selection caller remains pending. Inline tests fully read, not executed.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQAf4T+l/cUUGeUbH2VkJv0rg5DJNWF9XusH5rsXdi