e all producers, consumers and invariants together; a rejected new operation must leave the predecessor usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: history beyond the reported count/byte boundaries, lock contention lasting beyond the old patience window, lost commit acknowledgements followed by later progress, torn uncommitted tails and true committed corruption, then reopen and resolve exact historical receipts. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:21:37.467Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQPZwDBdCw1ZLpnO6Pg5jOm3Evb2mWNi0ju3Z4I3EGYIuJuFJeEyhTjIylMsA9hj2jNsrVL4YBVKQDAfdICB9AQY="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2407,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:21:37.846370764Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"47065019-87de-5a1a-b1e7-b44bd777ef22","title":"[L167] Unknown receipt format versions are silently skipped during replay","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L167.\n\n- Source: `crates/app/peritus-product-runner/src/developer_tools/receipt/codec.rs:24-81`; `receipt/storage.rs:107-148`.\n- The decoder accepts an integer version and known record shape. Storage validates and retains only version 1 records, while advancing past records of every other version without an incompatibility fence. A compatible-shaped record from an unsupported version therefore contributes no remembered effect; a later admission can treat its ordinal as unseen.\n- This is a persistence compatibility defect rather than a timeout. Unknown formats should retain an explicit incompatible state or migrate with preserved effect identity. The loader also truncates a genuinely incomplete trailing frame to the last complete offset, but rejects an oversized length prefix before determining whether its body is complete.\n- **Source-confirmed; unsupported-version replay and damaged-prefix recovery have not been reproduced in this audit.**\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQHt4f+ljZ4Arqye6m4OVvq01txR9JCfl1oyuNnr/hnCvV4n2rKqPWcOJQkRdCwDegGvIYPsHFbuMQYTL0Xg6KQo="}
