ation must leave the predecessor usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: valid boundary values and values just beyond each synthetic cap, final wrapper/receipt growth, non-ASCII strings, arbitrarily split frames/pages, malformed or conflicting data, mixed-version decode and save/reopen round trips. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:21:37.467Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQFavd+vmuZ9wggA3JSblIXwSJZmwDrGqKK6I+N6XQ/FEliAXeAMlTT91OO0tTdRvWNpgu0wqrmTW+2yC833hXwg="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2411,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:21:37.855531849Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"12223f2e-e022-59f7-b683-85b363db2362","title":"[L169] Preview admission permits untimed operation but retains payload bounds and a narrower downstream process contract","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L169.\n\n- Source: `crates/app/peritus-product-runner/src/developer_tools/preview.rs:9-11,43-71,157-165`.\n- The constructor supports `None` timeout. A selected timeout must be positive and representable as u64 milliseconds; it has no ten-minute or other fixed duration ceiling. The included tests explicitly accept 601 seconds and collections above the former 256-argument/64-environment limits.\n- Admission still limits executable text to **4,096 bytes**, individual arguments/environment values to **64 KiB**, collection lengths to **65,535**, idempotency keys to **512 bytes**, and terminal dimensions to nonzero u16 values. Environment names use an ASCII identifier grammar; no length ceiling is enforced here.\n- This constructor is broader than the C2 launch contract already read in L096 (**4,096 arguments**, **1,024 environment entries**, and aggregate payload bounds). Acceptance here does not establish executable downstream admission. The error groups all failures as Apply/invalid launch profile. **Source-confirmed bounds and contract mismatch; actual preview host inputs remain to be traced.**\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQPWJq