er, split transport chunks and large streams, ambiguous acceptance and duplicate events, cancellation during recovery, adapter restart and route changes, proving same-thread reconnection and no duplicated accepted request/effect. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:21:37.467Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQEk9VwW0smmU7a8jybTwjbLMkvb3ZPZpaE7LXI7tSiaFq48HMMZ7u8DbbByhGGN4+/FwIPOidB7MpSto/2YUpgc="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2417,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:21:37.869106328Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"cccb9c35-3cf9-51cb-993a-e24360586ca1","title":"[L228] Recovery layers use incompatible retry classifications and can discard provider delay/acceptance facts","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L228.\n\n- Source: `crates/model/peritus-provider-core/src/recovery.rs:71-100,105-165`; `crates/orchestration/peritus-agent/src/developer/retry.rs:61-80,92-109,129-157`; `crates/app/peritus-product-runner/src/failover.rs:12-30,168-193`; protocol `retry.rs:124-178`.\n- The developer in-turn planner selects no elapsed horizon but has a fixed **30-second maximum delay**, and refuses Retry-After above that value. It admits both SafeNewRequest **and CallerDecision** as SafeNewRequest; generic Transport/MalformedStream core errors also become SafeNewRequest without acceptance-phase facts in that decision. The pure protocol planner itself protects ambiguous/partial submissions when those causes are supplied; relabeling them bypasses that distinction. Native tools are disabled, but provider cost and duplicated inference remain effects needing exact reconciliation.\n- Native Claude capacity failure is Never in the in-turn path (L213), so no in-turn retry occurs. The outer role loop separately permits TransientProvider by category and can make **three role invocations** (L051), before considering authorized fallbacks. Thus Never here does not mean immediate global stop. The outer error representation/recovery classification does not preserve the same certainty/retryability/delay decision; layered policies can disagree or restart promptly after the inner delay bound stopped recovery.\n- The shared ProviderTerminal classifier has yet another disposition table: capacity/transient means authorized fallback, malformed/incomplete means same-route retry, and fixed diagnostic substrings for capacity/overloaded/context take precedence over category. That helper alone does not establish the production developer path's behavior; its callers remain pending. Finite retry ceilings are distinct from necessary refusal to duplicate ambiguously accepted work.\n- **All classifier/planner/role implementation and inline tests fully read; no retry-layer scenario run.** Ontological repair should carry typed phase, identity, certainty and provider-specified retry scheduling through every layer rather than convert recovery refusal into generic category-based restart.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQPRqkE0nXhf7DVH5FXIWrk3AaNxo5og61xFLxX749H1K9cK55ZhDdnlYEHQOp6IWnaEZY6q5Mwq7kJYJmRD50Qc="}
