edecessor usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: long provider outages and Retry-After, split transport chunks and large streams, ambiguous acceptance and duplicate events, cancellation during recovery, adapter restart and route changes, proving same-thread reconnection and no duplicated accepted request/effect. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:21:37.467Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQOj5v+dok00AaSASonm/DNeiBVpdH3cjCEazbLx4oTCMySMHYpBd4IcKU5F8sdRCaFt+dcjHe8c8aJCVWUdiwAQ="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2419,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:21:37.873526187Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"4f8f71a1-0491-5b9f-a0a5-53c0a0e21e21","title":"[L243] A subscription gap has no TUI snapshot-recovery transition","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L243.\n\n- Source: `crates/app/peritus-tui/src/model/protocol.rs:12-51,188-198`; `crates/app/peritus-tui/src/model/interaction.rs`; daemon subscription handling recorded in L239.\n- On SubscriptionGap the TUI emits a notice and returns no recovery effect. The server has entered SnapshotRequired, so ordinary event pumping cannot continue. The TUI subscription Resume command does not perform the required snapshot transition. Reconnect constructs another subscription from the retained last_cursor; the gap response does not replace that cursor with a recovered snapshot position. This can strand the display and reproduce the same gap on reconnect.\n- This is a missing state/recovery transition, not justification for a new elapsed timeout. The repair must bind snapshot recovery to the same durable session and then resume from the snapshot cursor. The inspected journal query uses actual MIN/MAX positions; its 4096 bound is a query-page limit, not evidence of automatic deletion after 4096 events (L247).\n- Separately, the TUI retains at most **4096 display events**, removes their dedup identities on eviction, and shows previews of **240 input bytes** (escaped display text can be longer). Notices retain a **4096-byte prefix** and expire after **24 UI ticks** (about six seconds at the runtime's 250 ms cadence). Those presentation limits do not terminate the product run, but a disappearing notice can hide the reason the display remains stalled. **Complete client protocol and interaction files read; runtime reproduction not performed.**\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQGouYsWdtGE+s/7zRd852T9J7GQrbQ3K/v6tZWIcRuXwQdpP84sclMsIfnrXk1OoDlm8tlH/Dbz4kj3kRHayMAI="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2420,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:21:37.875881635Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"4f8f71a1-0491-5b9f-a0a5-53c0a0e21e21","comment_uuid":"968aae36-5384-4878-b64e-46005815b76e","author":"6ME5","content":"Systemic repair plan for L243: A subscription gap has no TUI snapshot-recovery transition.\n\nOwning contract and implementation boundary: crates/app/peritus-tui/src/model/protocol.rs:12-51,188-198; crates/app/peritus-tui/src/model/interaction.rs. Apply the change through the constructors, live callers, durable writer and restart reader for this boundary, not as an isolated constant increase.\n\nrepair must bind snapshot recovery to the same durable session and then resume from the snapshot cursor. The inspected journal query uses actual MIN/MAX positions; its 4096 bound is a query-page limit, not evidence of automatic deletion after 4096 events (L247).\n\nPreserve: durable logical session and run identity, exact command receipts, atomic snapshot/cursor binding, explicit authority, selected UI state, complete history retrieval and owned-effect reconciliation. Separate a physical allocation/page limit and a genuine authority or integrity check from a cumulative work allowance. Keep transient contention/capacity observable and recoverable under the existing logical task; do not discard accepted state or substitute a fresh session to get around it.\n\nCompatibility/migration: retain decoders and exact receipts for previously accepted records. If representation or lifecycle semantics change, introduce a versioned migration under exclusive ownership; verify a complete replacement frontier before atomic publication and keep the old recovery root until adoption is durable. Rebuild derived projections from authoritative evidence. Update all producers, consumers and invariants together; a rejected new operation must leave the predecessor usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: large histories and non-ASCII fields, queue/connection pressure, delayed acknowledgements, subscription gaps, disconnect/reconnect and daemon restart, proving snapshot recovery, preserved selection/context, responsive controls and no duplicate command. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:21:37.467Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQG3ZtLQVEJoEq7w7aGHsk+HDBZL3S+Z6YmO/D2eRRoSy8hRlr9RJSWAPrA4oxA+E7q3ZDjlwV00DK3B7OMaK0gM="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2421,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:21:37.878010273Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"72de9c8b-ee52-58e1-a0a1-f3f7b496e1ba","title":"[L251] Outbox attempts cannot be unlimited, and exhaustion invalidates a still-valid final lease","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L251.\n\n- Source: `crates/state/peritus-journal/src/outbox.rs:5-8,63-79,107-132`; `sqlite/outbox_store.rs:19-50,60-105,113-163`.\n- Each message requires a positive **u16 max_attempts** with no unlimited representation, an ASCII-graphic destination of **1..512 bytes**, and a payload at most **16 MiB**. Claim time and lease_until are caller-supplied positive increasing ticks; these files choose no wall-clock lease duration.\n- Before selecting a new claim, the UPDATE changes **every Pending or Claimed row with attempts >= max_attempts to Exhausted**, without checking whether a Claimed row's lease has expired. A row reaches that attempt count when the final claim is issued. Any subsequent claim can therefore exhaust it while its last worker still holds a valid lease. The worker's exact acknowledgment then fails StaleHead because state is no longer Claimed.\n- There is no reopen/requeue path in this complete adapter. Exhaustion can become permanent loss of delivery rather than an explicit recoverable outcome. A repair must distinguish an active final claim from an expired failed attempt and preserve durable delivery identity/fencing. The direct acknowledgment helper also treats an already Acknowledged row as idempotent without comparing the supplied old fence, while append-bound acknowledgments require a current exact claim; that contract difference needs caller review. **Both files fully read; production producer/dispatcher selected attempts and lease cadence remain pending.**\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQDcmE2n2MY3lQQpWBjcnyuUCgsyO1OdEudq9wjkhSiNqpuxGPiKVGxoxovPH37nzhHX8gG0hbs2kgtsKzQ33lgc="}
