oritative evidence. Update all producers, consumers and invariants together; a rejected new operation must leave the predecessor usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: renewal/adoption under the same authorized identity, revoked authority, stale epoch/revision, cross-scope requests, lost acknowledgements and restart, proving legitimate continuation without admitting unauthorized or duplicate effects. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:21:37.467Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQBTD/CPZlLSzqaP29EuMmwLdtSSqn0YHRE0MVp0dWjJ8wFV8elXADeN3O+5xBVeFh2ULTBzMrAtioW9vKALTOAo="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2423,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:21:37.882632668Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"5e34bd9e-ddd9-5686-9939-81374807ae7e","title":"[L255] Valid Git quoted paths and long source lines can disable the entire structured diff","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L255.\n\n- Source: `crates/app/peritus-app-protocol/src/workbench/review/parser.rs:30-69,202-238`; `workbench/review/diff.rs:58-63,88-101`; `workbench/review/anchor.rs`.\n- A diff header is accepted only by finding the literal delimiter ` b/`; +++/--- paths require an unquoted a/ or b/ prefix. There is no Git C-quoted path decoder. A valid quoted Git header (for example a path containing a tab or a non-ASCII filename under default Git quoting) can therefore fail the entire structured parse rather than remain accessible through a decoded exact anchor.\n- Each line and hunk header uses MAX_PRODUCT_DETAIL_BYTES (**64 KiB**) and each line rejects controls other than tab. A single larger minified/source line rejects the whole structured object. Hunk start/count fields are **u32** and reject a positive count at line zero or an entirely empty range. These are syntax/display representation gates, not elapsed deadlines.\n- Source tests cover ordinary unquoted paths, digest changes, traversal, and a small wire roundtrip; they do not demonstrate large-line, quoted-path or collection-bound behavior. A repair should preserve exact path/content identity while providing decoding and page/range access. **All six review source/test files fully read; no test executed.**\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkM