ration must leave the predecessor usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: history beyond the reported count/byte boundaries, lock contention lasting beyond the old patience window, lost commit acknowledgements followed by later progress, torn uncommitted tails and true committed corruption, then reopen and resolve exact historical receipts. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:21:37.467Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQITmpyBCFGmcqgFoaI8UrYMCovU88INh41VOYREpn+StxRTaRuNhonG4vr52IFOo4AaxTBJyoCCqJ+bNiorwSAQ="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2427,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:21:37.891761234Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"da07f412-753f-5281-90c3-6a20e3c4b90e","title":"[L257] Journal recovery categories can turn unrelated resource/identity failures into terminal blockers","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L257.\n\n- Source: `crates/state/peritus-journal/src/error.rs:103-117,149-178`.\n- Busy and generic Storage failures recommend Retry; CAS/NotFound recommend Reobserve; ambiguous commits require resolution of the same command. MissingArtifact, ReadOnly, IdempotencyConflict, CorruptJournal, UnsupportedSchema and representational overflow are all Terminal. These are categorical gates, not elapsed deadlines, and they have materially different recoverability and scope.\n- Display collapses all SQLite failures to “SQLite operation failed”; the original source is retained only through the error chain. DiskFull is separately detectable, but the generic recovery category remains Retry. A caller that drops the source or adopts Terminal as a whole-daemon fence can obscure the real cause or prevent unrelated work. Existing caller-wide fences are documented in L197/L198; no additional production consequence is inferred solely from this enum.\n- Repair should preserve exact commit/identity/integrity checks while exposing typed resource conditions and scoped recoverable outcomes. **Whole error implementation read; no new retry count or timeout selected here.**\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1M