eported count/byte boundaries, lock contention lasting beyond the old patience window, lost commit acknowledgements followed by later progress, torn uncommitted tails and true committed corruption, then reopen and resolve exact historical receipts. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:21:37.467Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQDRcX/Oqs2DPYPU1fnwF6iH2an8h4m6t+F8YN235+erUZaxmWwW7+TEuTeeviQNP3J67BYefmxDr4b7RzGetxwY="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2431,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:21:37.901024863Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"517a05c4-822b-53ce-a411-f9e59a5b0657","title":"[L267] Full journal integrity forbids prefix retention and revalidates every historical state value","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L267.\n\n- Source: `crates/state/peritus-journal/src/integrity.rs:127-163`; `integrity/scan.rs:17-72`; `integrity/validation.rs`; `integrity/artifacts.rs`; `hash_chain.rs:85-103`.\n- The complete integrity scan requires COUNT(events) == MAX(global_position), then exact global positions **1..last**. Removing any old prefix as retention is corrupt under this contract. The 4096 global-window query size is therefore not an automatic retention policy. Complete history is durable here, but no authenticated retired-prefix/checkpoint contract exists in this scan.\n- Scan loads every immutable event and aggregate head into memory, then independently resolves every command, loading its event range again. It restores and hashes **every historical state revision**, not only latest values, before comparing the complete latest-history catalog with the current catalog. Cost grows with total retained session/command history and sum of complete historical value sizes. integrity_scan returns only a summary but still constructs the same full IntegrityExport internally.\n- Artifact validation checks all artifact_references for missing/unfinalized/quarantined content **before filtering journal-owned rows**. A bad reference owned by another subsystem can therefore fail the whole journal scan. Any bad old history row also aborts it; daemon startup's before-IPC dependency was already recorded in L198.\n- journal_head_hash converts aggregate count to **u32 with expect**, so an unrepresentable count would panic rather than produce a typed error. This is a theoretical representation boundary, not an ordinary short work quota; no such large store was constructed.\n- Repair must make verification incremental and preserve exact durable identity/history while scoping damaged-owner recovery. Simply deleting old rows violates today's integrity contract; simply removing memory/time bounds does not remove repeated full-history work. **All integrity implementation and hash files fully read; no storage/performance/recovery test run.** `sqlite/history/tests.rs:288-320` verifies physical allocation below half logical history for 1024 growing values, then runs a full integrity scan; it checks deduplication savings, not reopening/verification latency as history grows. Recovery tests explicitly reject deletion of an old state revision.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQC+kLw279xK4Mj3JjZPgQ6LysbxtkL9JB0TjB+JNY/Bn2xcAWnwWeB9HuEkP48tXRFBjU2BN2YkUMZYKykpYSQ8="}
