ted records. If representation or lifecycle semantics change, introduce a versioned migration under exclusive ownership; verify a complete replacement frontier before atomic publication and keep the old recovery root until adoption is durable. Rebuild derived projections from authoritative evidence. Update all producers, consumers and invariants together; a rejected new operation must leave the predecessor usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: history beyond the reported count/byte boundaries, lock contention lasting beyond the old patience window, lost commit acknowledgements followed by later progress, torn uncommitted tails and true committed corruption, then reopen and resolve exact historical receipts. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:21:37.467Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQCzHoU0IOrmUbxFhDIEwb6aHHhJcNvDdiltdvH/97A9iwgX/NDQhR4GERE0sZl8imzvnk2o0AU87ZsuSH1MOmAY="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2433,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:21:37.905415672Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"3120378a-a23e-5b6a-b1f3-7650f830420f","title":"[L277] An interrupted command between durable admission and dispatch is permanently rejected on exact retry","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L277.\n\n- Source: `crates/app/peritus-daemon/src/command/service.rs:44-108`; `authority/owner/storage.rs:17-42`; `command/service_tests.rs:131-216`; `startup/recovery.rs:10-60`.\n- submit performs admission, domain dispatch, and terminal settlement as separate awaited owner messages. Interruption after admission can leave Pending with no domain commit. Existing Pending/Indeterminate never goes back to dispatch: it calls reconcile_command, whose DefinitelyAbsent branch durably rejects the command as **UnsupportedFamily**, irrespective of the actual submitted family.\n- Every dispatch Err also tries to mark Indeterminate and ignores any settlement error. A definitely-uncommitted retryable storage failure can therefore enter the same terminal rejection path on retry. The immutable idempotency key then retains that rejection; submitting exact intent again cannot perform the intended work.\n- This gate confuses definitely absent with unsupported and has no admitted-intent resume path. Repair must persist enough exact intent and ownership to resume/reject truthfully under the same identity, while resolving committed effects first. Changing session/window or command identity is not an equivalent repair.\n- The complete service tests preseed a domain commit before application admission and cover historical v1 committed recovery. They do not exercise the admission-before-dispatch interruption. The subsequently fully read black-box `tests/daemon_conformance_support/session/indeterminate.rs:33-94` explicitly seeds an uncommitted Indeterminate command and requires UnsupportedFamily plus durable Rejected after restart. The conformance expectation therefore codifies this no-work recovery outcome; it must change with the lifecycle contract. The complete startup recovery implementation uses the same permanent UnsupportedFamily rejection before intake for every DefinitelyAbsent request. Scheduler durability has now been fully read and uses SHA256 of the exact encoded command bytes, matching the application ledger; no scheduler digest mismatch was found. The other domain adapters remain to be traced. **Complete service, owner and startup reconciliation read; no crash/failure reproduction run.**\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQEq+KRgEelkdFDY2JjC4GRWb322nz0srGsUv0GEwogZbrL2ruehKAtRCT1pEKY8STjlPg4YD3K9/qReTvD5lRwg="}
