{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2437,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:21:37.914633524Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"49ee1e12-f56f-52c6-927e-55e83fc180ac","title":"[L285] Scheduler delivery repeatedly selects the same bounded prefix and has no separate cancellation lane","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L285.\n\n- Source: `crates/orchestration/peritus-scheduler/src/runtime.rs:226-286,289-383`; `state.rs:131-136`.\n- pending_directives scans reservations in **dispatch-identity order**, emits Dispatch for unacknowledged Reserved work and Cancel for Cancelling work, and stops when the immutable dispatch batch limit is reached (at most **256**). Every call starts at index zero; there is no continuation or rotation cursor.\n- If enough early pending reservations remain unacknowledged, later directives, including cancellations, stay outside every returned prefix. This is a source-level starvation condition; the actual effect-shell caller must be traced to determine whether it rotates independently or guarantees timely acknowledgment.\n- This function has no elapsed acknowledgment timer, worker-liveness check or independent cancellation capacity. Repair should make progress and cancellation delivery explicit without forfeiting idempotent dispatch identity. **Complete directive implementation and ordering declaration read; production poll caller and concurrency reproduction pending.**\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQHG0sa37XowjdCU3eDoZJ5Z/t5LenjXdQ6c