{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2438,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:21:37.917255519Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"49ee1e12-f56f-52c6-927e-55e83fc180ac","comment_uuid":"2887fb86-d8d5-4ad6-b949-ce942e2389e1","author":"6ME5","content":"Systemic repair plan for L285: Scheduler delivery repeatedly selects the same bounded prefix and has no separate cancellation lane.\n\nOwning contract and implementation boundary: crates/orchestration/peritus-scheduler/src/runtime.rs:226-286,289-383; state.rs:131-136. Apply the change through the constructors, live callers, durable writer and restart reader for this boundary, not as an isolated constant increase.\n\nRepair should make progress and cancellation delivery explicit without forfeiting idempotent dispatch identity.\n\nPreserve: resource reservations, dispatch fencing, dependency truth, opaque identity versus causal order, monotonic stop intent, exact historical receipts and truthful child/effect settlement. Separate a physical allocation/page limit and a genuine authority or integrity check from a cumulative work allowance. Keep transient contention/capacity observable and recoverable under the existing logical task; do not discard accepted state or substitute a fresh session to get around it.\n\nCompatibility/migration: retain decoders and exact receipts for previously accepted records. If representation or lifecycle semantics change, introduce a versioned migration under exclusive ownership; verify a complete replacement frontier before atomic publication and keep the old recovery root until adoption is durable. Rebuild derived projections from authoritative evidence. Update all producers, consumers and invariants together; a rejected new operation must leave the predecessor usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: long task/message/command histories, smaller configured bindings, saturation with cancellation and acknowledgements, delayed start/completion races, terminal roots with live descendants, lost receipts after subsequent progress, and save/reopen equivalence. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:21:37.467Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQDrq12kMm21+o9dTAxjH7RuPIQpqUU4RheeyKSNes1/JO2lSPfT3A+DjhZS8Jb9IrsFYCv3Z2Q1JLowQ73F3Dwg="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2439,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:21:37.919503972Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"b8239eeb-6aad-5ab6-bfdf-f729ebef43e1","title":"[L286] Full scheduler command history blocks cancellation, completion and finalization after 65,535 events","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L286.\n\n- Source: `crates/orchestration/peritus-scheduler/src/reducer/fences.rs:224-267`; `reducer.rs:63-82,119-136`; `state/mutation/cursor.rs:27-51`; `command/kind.rs`.\n- Every accepted event, including genesis, appends one command identity to the complete state. At **65,535 retained command identities**, the common fence rejects every new nonterminal command before inspecting its kind. Cancellation, acknowledgment, completion, abandonment, worker recovery, pause/resume, drain and finalization have no exception or reserved capacity.\n- The closed scheduler command vocabulary has no command-history retirement, checked continuation or same-aggregate rotation. Existing exact receipt resolution is a separate durability path; it cannot perform a new requested cancellation or completion.\n- Thus lifetime history saturation can strand live reservations and block the commands needed to reach terminal truth. This is an artificial lifetime limiter, distinct from bounded concurrency or canonical frame size. Repair must separate durable identity/history from the mutable scheduling frontier and preserve recovery/control capacity. **Complete fences, cursor mutation and closed command dispatcher read; no 65,535-event reproduction executed.**\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQDxGmk6SC+fBo8XzODOyYT5qTiv2gemsx58ObbDJYIOVr214oailauXZXophSiFTjRKmjDNrM3gJvQSdmbAusw0="}
