and acknowledgements, delayed start/completion races, terminal roots with live descendants, lost receipts after subsequent progress, and save/reopen equivalence. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:21:37.467Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQGCOH8trcBOAoRGigErH2peu8CYAQYhqAf09uvw70tyIAC/3LVH/OywEvEml0EEopJqrOS7OigDCA8RYsoDeXgc="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2441,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:21:37.924602380Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"793f681c-e00a-55af-babb-646034762cc4","title":"[L292] Bypass aging is a priority class, not a guarantee of dispatch at the configured bypass count","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L292.\n\n- Source: `crates/orchestration/peritus-scheduler/src/selection/scan/work.rs:19-42,163-240`; `selection/model.rs:185-221`; `reducer/apply/dispatch.rs:91-107,145-159`; `selection/{scan,capacity}.rs`.\n- Feasible bypass counters saturate at the immutable bound (at most **32,767**). Crossing it makes an item aged, which precedes unaged items. **Two aged items still compare priority before enqueue ordinal**. A lower-priority aged item can therefore be bypassed again by higher-priority aged work; the configured value is not an absolute maximum number of bypasses.\n- Selection scans all retained work and picks the first feasible worker in canonical identity order. There is no worker rotation. Each feasibility call recomputes global/per-worker resource sums and concurrency counts; dispatch then rescans all work for feasible bypass updates, with a further work lookup per item. This can accumulate substantial synchronous work as retention grows; no benchmark was run.\n- Capacity helpers return false above **4,096 reservations**, matching the compiled active-reservation ceiling. When canonical u64 aggregate arithmetic cannot represent a sum, they use exact u128 per-dimension fallback; that recovery is not a fake elapsed limiter.\n- The complete proofs establish exact selection under the current state, not a delivery-latency or fixed-bypass service guarantee. Repair should define the intended progress/fairness contract and incremental accounting explicitly. **Complete selection implementation, model, ordering, aggregation and fallback read; effect-shell dispatch caller and fairness qualification pending.**\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQD8IoS0gDp3cUyDoNJH5ugtAbj4RFggT1HDryBi7PPD25ukVVIOnybBFhypyi6RU4z4KS4k+4ztRFT4ajn4xeAc="}
