ation and acknowledgements, delayed start/completion races, terminal roots with live descendants, lost receipts after subsequent progress, and save/reopen equivalence. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:21:37.467Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQAkIya6yU+C+n2tCbOxA4tcAbsS5PduITDLKArBENr5G/EMTLcqVoh4gbs4ip//IOrQifq2zBxu6BnJj6QzEiA0="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2443,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:21:37.929122898Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"0f004765-c53b-55fd-8713-0ec927661fe6","title":"[L293] Checkpoint invariants make lifetime history retention part of the schema, so deleting old entries is not a valid repair","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L293.\n\n- Source: `crates/orchestration/peritus-scheduler/src/state/validation.rs:9-49,80-139,142-186`; `canonical.rs:30-68`; `state/mutation/cursor.rs`; `state/mutation.rs:134-164`.\n- Decoded state requires **enqueue_ordinal == retained work count**, **dispatch_ordinal == retained dispatch-ID count**, and **event sequence == retained command-ID count**. It repeats the finite retained-vector ceilings and estimated state-size gate before canonical checks. Complete hashing binds every retained record and identity.\n- Simple pruning would break these ordinals, exact digests, replay and dependencies/parents. The lifetime ceilings in L286/L287/L291 are therefore embedded in the persisted ontology, not just adjustable runtime constants. A root repair needs an explicit schema/continuation model that separates immutable historical evidence from the active scheduling frontier under durable run identity.\n- Validation also performs a fresh dependency-cycle graph walk for **every retained work item**, then checks dependency truth, reservations, ownership, terminal summary and the full digest. Long dependency histories can magnify restart/replay latency; this is source-level cost analysis, not a measured timeout.\n- **Complete validation and canonical hashing read; wire schema/migration and production qualification remain pending.**\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQEGKOzZK+TSpLQeYcZRKNI3iL1KuHEe+wBfKum5Y8RB0eMeCVNE8UwTU/DfOAqfZtdh+JUDoxpVKra4TAunVHAY="}
