maller configured bindings, saturation with cancellation and acknowledgements, delayed start/completion races, terminal roots with live descendants, lost receipts after subsequent progress, and save/reopen equivalence. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:21:37.467Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQLeOtypIxZ3QO9jV5oWBoNjlUQcfpsRK3avBUKLTahMHxuoIE9Qmd3GPEAMRwx+//FSh0QguARVVvsjqXsw+bws="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2447,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:21:37.938351609Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"47e5938f-adcd-5518-83e3-9ef37bf05504","title":"[L295] A late start acknowledgment can erase a requested cancellation, outside the existing non-resurrection proof","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L295.\n\n- Source: `crates/orchestration/peritus-scheduler/src/reducer/apply/cancellation/update.rs:198-232`; `update/activity.rs:10-38`; `state/mutation/reservation_command.rs:42-67`; `state/mutation/acknowledge_start.rs:125-221`; `work_update/apply_at.rs:70-75`; `cancellation/non_resurrection.rs:74-123`.\n- Source-traced sequence: DispatchNext creates an unstarted Reserved reservation. CancelWork sets its work to **Cancelling** while retaining that reservation and started=false. AcknowledgeStart checks only that the live reservation is not started, marks it started, and unconditionally sets the work to **Running**. No old-phase admission rejects Cancelling on that path.\n- pending_directives then stops emitting its cancellation, because the work is Running. A subsequent newly fenced CompleteWork can be accepted as success. Cancellation intent is represented only by the overwritten phase; the described path can lose the user's requested stop.\n- The existing non-resurrection theorem composes Cancel, **late CompleteWork**, AcknowledgeCancellation, then CompleteWork. Its premises exclude AcknowledgeStart between cancellation and completion. Complete graph tests likewise do not exercise this race. Proven field/ownership invariants are narrower than the required monotonic cancellation contract.\n- The subsequently read `verified/reservations/readiness/phase.rs:15-18` permits Cancelling with either start bit. `readiness/start.rs:33-58` requires an unstarted reservation but does not require a Reserved predecessor, then specifies a Running successor. Thus the actual start preservation theorem can prove its current ownership relation even while accepting the cancellation reversal. `tests/cancellation_tree.rs:384-394` checks only late success around cancellation acknowledgment. `tests/queue_recovery.rs:152-224` reuses the queue pressure released by Cancelling and then loses the worker; it does not test late start acknowledgment after that reuse.\n- Repair must preserve cancellation intent across every late acknowledgment/recovery transition, while accepting truthful owner evidence and retaining exact dispatch identity. **Complete admission/mutation chain and relevant proof scope read; no executable race reproduction or live-instance attribution claimed.**\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQLVZAn6VqQagilfg9XxOcSfOd3pqPyNBXXP/lYyQDaxIi8CPUuokNigQAwP10pGY8bYISkh7BPfY/31qwQ/2QgM="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2448,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:21:37.940830408Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"47e5938f-adcd-5518-83e3-9ef37bf05504","comment_uuid":"0841c591-e4db-4bb9-ac48-28eb9e0c7670","author":"6ME5","content":"Systemic repair plan for L295: A late start acknowledgment can erase a requested cancellation, outside the existing non-resurrection proof.\n\nOwning contract and implementation boundary: crates/orchestration/peritus-scheduler/src/reducer/apply/cancellation/update.rs:198-232; update/activity.rs:10-38; state/mutation/reservation_command.rs:42-67; state/mutation/acknowledge_start.rs:125-221; work_update/apply_at.rs:70-75; cancellation/non_resurrection.rs:74-123; verified/reservations/readiness/phase.rs:15-18; readiness/start.rs:33-58; tests/cancellation_tree.rs:384-394; tests/queue_recovery.rs:152-224. Apply the change through the constructors, live callers, durable writer and restart reader for this boundary, not as an isolated constant increase.\n\nRepair must preserve cancellation intent across every late acknowledgment/recovery transition, while accepting truthful owner evidence and retaining exact dispatch identity.\n\nPreserve: resource reservations, dispatch fencing, dependency truth, opaque identity versus causal order, monotonic stop intent, exact historical receipts and truthful child/effect settlement. Separate a physical allocation/page limit and a genuine authority or integrity check from a cumulative work allowance. Keep transient contention/capacity observable and recoverable under the existing logical task; do not discard accepted state or substitute a fresh session to get around it.\n\nCompatibility/migration: retain decoders and exact receipts for previously accepted records. If representation or lifecycle semantics change, introduce a versioned migration under exclusive ownership; verify a complete replacement frontier before atomic publication and keep the old recovery root until adoption is durable. Rebuild derived projections from authoritative evidence. Update all producers, consumers and invariants together; a rejected new operation must leave the predecessor usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: long task/message/command histories, smaller configured bindings, saturation with cancellation and acknowledgements, delayed start/completion races, terminal roots with live descendants, lost receipts after subsequent progress, and save/reopen equivalence. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:21:37.467Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQARamQEKud8Hh1U/QDsFdzfByPZHa75o/Htx/eh7vTxTfTls6tlFVrtdp6r6p1jXgA2r0O1vYejX3Q4ghTNHHAw="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2449,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:21:37.943084964Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"81f4e533-016b-57b7-a187-a311bf91d83b","title":"[L296] Scheduler ingress can durably accept state that its own restart decoder rejects","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L296.\n\n- **Source:** `crates/orchestration/peritus-scheduler/src/wire/command.rs:212-223`, `wire/domain.rs`, `wire/records.rs`, `wire/state.rs:102-210`; `command.rs:231-253`; `reducer/apply/worker_control.rs:9-34`, `reducer/apply/admission.rs:42-73`; `reducer.rs:63-82`; `durability.rs:123-207,309-338`, `durability/binding.rs:7-35`, `durability/semantics.rs:10-48`.\n- **Mechanism:** wire commands construct worker descriptors and work specifications with compiled production maxima. The authoritative aggregate may bind smaller limits. Worker registration rechecks capacity and retained-worker count but omits descriptor concurrency against the aggregate reservation limit. Work admission checks retention, queue, revision, capacity, dependency identities, parent and supporting worker, but omits the specification attempt ceiling and dependency count against aggregate limits. Typed `from_state` commands also accept an already constructed kind without rebinding those values. Reduction does not validate the complete successor; encoding and commit check schema, cross-record fences and actual byte sizes, not inert-state validity. Checkpoint decoding later constructs descriptors/specifications using the actual aggregate limits and rejects the persisted records.\n- **Concrete source traces:** an aggregate with reservation limit 1 can accept a production-valid worker with concurrency 2 when capacity and remaining checks fit. An aggregate with attempt limit 1 can accept a production-valid work specification with maximum attempts 2. A dependency ceiling of 1 can similarly be bypassed by a specification containing 2 existing dependencies, when the other admission requirements fit. These accepted records can be stored, then fail checkpoint decoding on replay/restart. This is not a claim that resource dimensions escape global capacity checks.\n- **Daily-driving effect:** a successful command can leave an aggregate that cannot reopen; the durability codec maps decode failure to Quarantine. Genesis-only wire fixtures do not exercise these transitions. These are complete source/caller traces, not executed reproductions or attribution to the live user run.\n- **Ontological repair requirement:** commands must enter a single authoritative aggregate validation boundary. Every accepted successor must satisfy the same invariant contract required for durable decoding, before append, with rejection leaving the predecessor usable. Preserve these invariants across typed commands, wire commands, replay and versioned checkpoints; qualify smaller-limit admission and save/reopen behavior.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQBzg9EjT3aLrc6/0DWXnDqi0hPDZdy5k/wWaWVx+zMDoXcCTfPYVpfnFW11W86kwMSJ6Eb/4eKIFwcGj1wcxiQU="}
