ld derived projections from authoritative evidence. Update all producers, consumers and invariants together; a rejected new operation must leave the predecessor usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: long task/message/command histories, smaller configured bindings, saturation with cancellation and acknowledgements, delayed start/completion races, terminal roots with live descendants, lost receipts after subsequent progress, and save/reopen equivalence. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:21:37.467Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQD4fipBPRxcvxa7qDhkfF4CeSNKwPY9cq5PQzuigscZCeSBeJ3304q11IyR+K1bzr1dFb5395A/nTnloVGQnBQg="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2455,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:21:37.958756548Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"e411ab54-5113-53b2-b11a-60481bf5a676","title":"[L300] Collaboration byte checks charge external payload sizes to small digest-only records","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L300.\n\n- Source: `crates/orchestration/peritus-collaboration/src/message.rs:10-23`; `reducer.rs:72-77,242-261`; `state.rs:279-293`; `canonical.rs:164-177`; `wire/mod.rs:333-355`; `reducer/apply.rs:196-234,237-254`.\n- A message stores a payload **length and digest**, plus causal IDs, media type, optional handoff and revision. Neither semantic encoding nor wire encoding contains payload content. Nevertheless command admission estimates **payload_bytes + 768**, and complete-state admission charges the entire payload_bytes again for every historical message.\n- A legal digest-only message referring to a 1 MiB payload can fail a 1 MiB command budget while its actual metadata command is much smaller. Repeated metadata messages can consume the aggregate's state budget based on the sum of external content lengths, even after delivery is acknowledged; acknowledgment changes a boolean and releases no quota.\n- This synthetic accounting can block commands and long-lived collaboration far below actual canonical storage size. Repair should distinguish actual encoded-state bytes from any separately justified external-content/storage resource policy, with an explicit recovery model. **Both encodings and every accounting/admission path read completely; no boundary test executed.**\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQHaclpMGZnsiruu9nFPtQJcjl4LT5GffJHrV3gUgJes/wVw+YYu3tTiNIy1V9eK6/IPefO5f7PRO6sflSLTaYg4="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2456,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:21:37.961100400Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"e411ab54-5113-53b2-b11a-60481bf5a676","comment_uuid":"c79575af-0717-4296-8350-f49a3d446c02","author":"6ME5","content":"Systemic repair plan for L300: Collaboration byte checks charge external payload sizes to small digest-only records.\n\nOwning contract and implementation boundary: crates/orchestration/peritus-collaboration/src/message.rs:10-23; reducer.rs:72-77,242-261; state.rs:279-293; canonical.rs:164-177; wire/mod.rs:333-355; reducer/apply.rs:196-234,237-254. Apply the change through the constructors, live callers, durable writer and restart reader for this boundary, not as an isolated constant increase.\n\nRepair should distinguish actual encoded-state bytes from any separately justified external-content/storage resource policy, with an explicit recovery model. Both encodings and every accounting/admission path read completely; no boundary test executed.\n\nPreserve: resource reservations, dispatch fencing, dependency truth, opaque identity versus causal order, monotonic stop intent, exact historical receipts and truthful child/effect settlement. Separate a physical allocation/page limit and a genuine authority or integrity check from a cumulative work allowance. Keep transient contention/capacity observable and recoverable under the existing logical task; do not discard accepted state or substitute a fresh session to get around it.\n\nCompatibility/migration: retain decoders and exact receipts for previously accepted records. If representation or lifecycle semantics change, introduce a versioned migration under exclusive ownership; verify a complete replacement frontier before atomic publication and keep the old recovery root until adoption is durable. Rebuild derived projections from authoritative evidence. Update all producers, consumers and invariants together; a rejected new operation must leave the predecessor usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: long task/message/command histories, smaller configured bindings, saturation with cancellation and acknowledgements, delayed start/completion races, terminal roots with live descendants, lost receipts after subsequent progress, and save/reopen equivalence. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:21:37.467Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQFeoVrSAqEUT7NuUnuoSa1nuZ0+eEOZOaKq7nWKC1cpbQSG9zPQi+5BNU715EKXlB15fb2Wk1h+kjMXU6dH2ewM="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2457,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:21:37.963377424Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"0a4409e5-b9e1-5b80-9639-136ecafb6eec","title":"[L301] Collaboration checks successor size before adding the command receipt and can persist an unreadable checkpoint","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L301.\n\n- Source: `crates/orchestration/peritus-collaboration/src/reducer.rs:81-86,242-250`; `state/mutation.rs:80-89`; `state.rs:279-293`; `state/validation.rs:54-75`; `wire/state.rs:45-69,128-141`; `durability/binding.rs:8-35`; `durability.rs:59-80,124-145,234-240,263-269`.\n- Every non-genesis transition checks the successor's estimated size **before** advance_cursor appends another 16-byte command ID. Final checkpoint decoding rechecks the estimate including that ID. Commit checks cross-record identities and actual encoded lengths, without invoking the checkpoint's complete inert validator.\n- Source-derived boundary: one root and the genesis command estimate **1,552 bytes** (1,024 + 512 + 16). An immutable state_bytes=1,552 binding is legal and can start; Pause passes the pre-cursor 1,552-byte check, but its final estimate is **1,568 bytes**. Its small actual canonical frame can fit the configured byte budget and be committed, then fail the checkpoint decoder after restart with Codec/Quarantine.\n- The same invariant ordering error is recorded for scheduler L297. Repair needs one authoritative final accepted-state invariant applied after all state/cursor changes, shared with decode/replay/commit; rejected transitions must preserve a usable predecessor. **Complete source chain and arithmetic inspected; no executable boundary reproduction or live attribution claimed.**\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-8