{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2461,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:21:37.972082595Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"7c50397e-e06f-5f6b-8e02-1844d48c8862","title":"[L303] Production framing imposes a hidden 65,535-command lifetime on collaboration, including cancellation and acknowledgments","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L303.\n\n- Source: `crates/foundation/peritus-codec/src/limits.rs:22-28`; `writer.rs:118-125,142-152`; `message.rs:33-39`; `crates/orchestration/peritus-collaboration/src/state/mutation.rs:80-89`; `wire/state.rs:52-64,116-123`; `durability.rs:64-72,263-269`; `command.rs:12-106`.\n- Collaboration advertises messages<=262,144 and state<=64 MiB minus 16, and its state decoder's local command bound is tasks + 2*messages + 65,535. But every durable frame uses CodecLimits::PRODUCTION: **16 MiB complete frame** and **65,535 items in any collection**. The shared writer rejects a complete used_commands vector at 65,536.\n- Every accepted command adds one retained ID; no command retires them. Once 65,535 IDs are committed, any additional command requires a 65,536-item state collection, including CancelTask, AcknowledgeCancellation, AcknowledgeMessage, Pause/Resume or Finalize. Canonical state encoding fails before append and maps the capacity failure to Codec/Quarantine. Actual frame size may block earlier; advertised larger message/state ceilings do not remove this hidden cap.\n- Repair must decouple live control/state from lifetime receipt history with a versioned durable frontier and exact retry guarantees, and reconcile aggregate limits with protocol storage. Reserving more IDs or enlarging one quota postpones the same lifetime failure. **Complete framing and commit chain read; no 65K saturation run executed.**\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQNPPLNnUEsD+mE7FRZ2+HYuy2yi14RLSZdfGE1cDac9YiZTa94gfyKJ6AlXX0UHPUlW3irGtJgQrji6Oer5kEAw="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2462,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:21:37.974397959Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"7c50397e-e06f-5f6b-8e02-1844d48c8862","comment_uuid":"adb84024-4f37-4549-a34a-2c7a06422295","author":"6ME5","content":"Systemic repair plan for L303: Production framing imposes a hidden 65,535-command lifetime on collaboration, including cancellation and acknowledgments.\n\nOwning contract and implementation boundary: crates/foundation/peritus-codec/src/limits.rs:22-28; writer.rs:118-125,142-152; message.rs:33-39; crates/orchestration/peritus-collaboration/src/state/mutation.rs:80-89; wire/state.rs:52-64,116-123; durability.rs:64-72,263-269; command.rs:12-106. Apply the change through the constructors, live callers, durable writer and restart reader for this boundary, not as an isolated constant increase.\n\nRepair must decouple live control/state from lifetime receipt history with a versioned durable frontier and exact retry guarantees, and reconcile aggregate limits with protocol storage. Reserving more IDs or enlarging one quota postpones the same lifetime failure.\n\nPreserve: resource reservations, dispatch fencing, dependency truth, opaque identity versus causal order, monotonic stop intent, exact historical receipts and truthful child/effect settlement. Separate a physical allocation/page limit and a genuine authority or integrity check from a cumulative work allowance. Keep transient contention/capacity observable and recoverable under the existing logical task; do not discard accepted state or substitute a fresh session to get around it.\n\nCompatibility/migration: retain decoders and exact receipts for previously accepted records. If representation or lifecycle semantics change, introduce a versioned migration under exclusive ownership; verify a complete replacement frontier before atomic publication and keep the old recovery root until adoption is durable. Rebuild derived projections from authoritative evidence. Update all producers, consumers and invariants together; a rejected new operation must leave the predecessor usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: long task/message/command histories, smaller configured bindings, saturation with cancellation and acknowledgements, delayed start/completion races, terminal roots with live descendants, lost receipts after subsequent progress, and save/reopen equivalence. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:21:37.467Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQLy75bJtC19VVRyfHYt6ksi73QvPS4MYyzZsyU8ItHF32CbHC+9UF4VXuWfebqF2NqFRFKS+KURMdbZoq2QJuws="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2463,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:21:37.976522849Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"a4858e8c-5048-599a-8852-cb9f35a7dcbc","title":"[L304] Collaboration finalization can wait forever on a delivery, and subtree cancellation refuses an already-terminal root","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L304.\n\n- Source: `crates/orchestration/peritus-collaboration/src/reducer/apply/terminal.rs:78-127,129-143,170-208`; `state.rs:272-277`; `reducer/apply.rs:237-254`; `command.rs:12-106`; `task.rs:299-308`.\n- Finalize requires every retained task terminal and every retained message acknowledged. Cancellation/abandonment/task completion does not settle message delivery; the vocabulary has no failed-delivery, delivery withdrawal, reconciliation or retirement command. An unavailable receiver can therefore keep the aggregate nonterminal indefinitely despite all task execution ending.\n- CancelTask rejects a Terminal target **before** traversing its descendants, paralleling scheduler L294. A failed/abandoned parent, or an AnyRequired parent that already succeeded while another child remains live, cannot be used as the cancellation subtree root. Descendants require separate owner/ancestor-authorized cancellation commands, which themselves require active owner acknowledgment to finish.\n- Waiting for truthful termination is distinct from an artificial timer; the blocker is a missing durable outcome/recovery path for unavailable delivery and already-ended parent ownership. Repair should model those outcomes explicitly while preserving truthful success and cancellation identity. **Complete domain state and command paths read; effect/runtime receiver recovery remains a separate caller audit, with no live attribution.**\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQBcZQ394CxFBnXV9u8GAbfEgtwLkerIiZL2gSg8wqs1k8Crj7uOGCG2901adJMXrtERgtpHn9FFfCRLvjYEI2gA="}
