gs, saturation with cancellation and acknowledgements, delayed start/completion races, terminal roots with live descendants, lost receipts after subsequent progress, and save/reopen equivalence. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:21:37.467Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQEbDObtLK0992cPdrFeP25t02OFYKzwOs1DUhFCYn3OccHdobpZxcS553PFynMiCKjuWu+o9C2ZtDmGK/DkuEA4="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2465,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:21:37.981167723Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"7c33c4b1-d8e2-5308-a2c3-5339e19cb613","title":"[L305] Collaboration rereads, clones and validates lifetime history synchronously, with quadratic validation paths","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L305.\n\n- Source: `crates/orchestration/peritus-collaboration/src/reducer.rs:81-86,105-129,139-145`; `canonical.rs:25-45`; `canonical/encoder.rs:5-17`; `state.rs:214-220,279-293`; `state/validation.rs:18-39,54-75,81-112`; `durability.rs:209-240`; `replay.rs:39-55`.\n- Every transition clones all retained tasks/messages/command IDs, recomputes the full size estimate and allocates a complete semantic encoding to hash. Cold loading materializes all events/checkpoint; rebuild then repeats full transitions for every prefix. Admission scans task/message history to derive fan-out, ordinals, recipients and artifacts.\n- Checkpoint validation compares every used command against its earlier prefix (quadratic duplicate checking); every task scans all tasks for unique scheduler work and scans children for fan-out. This synchronous work grows with terminal and acknowledged history, sharing the serialized daemon owner described in L274.\n- These paths can delay control/status/cancellation without any artificial elapsed deadline. A repair should preserve exact persistent history while using checked indexes, causal frontiers and responsive ownership; deleting the correctness checks or adding another timeout would not solve history growth. **Complete source cost paths read; no latency benchmark or measured live stall claimed.**\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZP