{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2477,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:21:38.007336167Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"0c22b185-a3c7-5672-9b8e-3030a9ae83cf","title":"[L311] E0 validates, serializes, and replays growing complete history synchronously","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L311.\n\n- **Source:** `crates/orchestration/peritus-orchestrator/src/reducer.rs:68-95,102-124`; `src/state/validation.rs:11-98,101-119,206-303`; `src/canonical/digests.rs:15-27`; `src/wire/state.rs:153-225`; `src/durability.rs:69-86,175-227`; `src/replay.rs:38-55`; `src/runtime/driver.rs:78-106`.\n- **Blocker:** Each transition validates and hashes the complete predecessor, clones all retained history, advances it, hashes the complete successor, then validates/hashes that successor again. Hashing materializes full canonical bytes. Validation compares every candidate/cycle to earlier history and scans retained handoffs/cycles/candidates for each activation/observation. Commit encodes the full state again. Restart decodes every event and reconstructs each complete prefix rather than resuming directly from a verified history frontier.\n- **Consequence:** Work per command grows with lifetime history; candidate/cycle uniqueness checks are pairwise, and full replay repeats growing-prefix work. These synchronous operations can monopolize their caller independently of provider progress. Raising retention ceilings without changing this representation increases the cost of ordinary controls and restart. No measured latency or live freeze is claimed.\n- **Repair direction:** Maintain checked incremental indexes and a durable compact frontier backed by append-only history. Authenticate replay/checkpoint equivalence without rebuilding every old prefix for each command, and run persistence work through an owner that can still service control requests. Retain provenance and replay truth.\n- **Evidence scope:** Complete source inspection and algorithmic cost analysis; no load benchmark was run.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQD6yMoea14sxe/Xtt63ywFC7MNLWS9GpzgqowkcuKhjaFi7ozTiwQ8Xw3u3TbFBCM3Pw4kgnh044Kgnd+8wDQQE="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2478,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:21:38.009468689Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"0c22b185-a3c7-5672-9b8e-3030a9ae83cf","comment_uuid":"eb4f65d3-f5a6-4633-a87b-f28093a550d1","author":"6ME5","content":"Systemic repair plan for L311: E0 validates, serializes, and replays growing complete history synchronously.\n\nOwning contract and implementation boundary: crates/orchestration/peritus-orchestrator/src/reducer.rs:68-95,102-124; src/state/validation.rs:11-98,101-119,206-303; src/canonical/digests.rs:15-27; src/wire/state.rs:153-225; src/durability.rs:69-86,175-227; src/replay.rs:38-55; src/runtime/driver.rs:78-106. Apply the change through the constructors, live callers, durable writer and restart reader for this boundary, not as an isolated constant increase.\n\nMaintain checked incremental indexes and a durable compact frontier backed by append-only history. Authenticate replay/checkpoint equivalence without rebuilding every old prefix for each command, and run persistence work through an owner that can still service control requests. Retain provenance and replay truth.\n\nPreserve: committed command/event identity, exact causal and digest roots, exclusive ownership, atomic publication, reference-safe artifact retention and verified recovery from the last durable frontier. Separate a physical allocation/page limit and a genuine authority or integrity check from a cumulative work allowance. Keep transient contention/capacity observable and recoverable under the existing logical task; do not discard accepted state or substitute a fresh session to get around it.\n\nCompatibility/migration: retain decoders and exact receipts for previously accepted records. If representation or lifecycle semantics change, introduce a versioned migration under exclusive ownership; verify a complete replacement frontier before atomic publication and keep the old recovery root until adoption is durable. Rebuild derived projections from authoritative evidence. Update all producers, consumers and invariants together; a rejected new operation must leave the predecessor usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: history beyond the reported count/byte boundaries, lock contention lasting beyond the old patience window, lost commit acknowledgements followed by later progress, torn uncommitted tails and true committed corruption, then reopen and resolve exact historical receipts. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:21:37.467Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQJCcfdK7RwrFIkmXRBGZ0ntLlpN4IBsa7meTdSaanbwXZtMHY6LZW0U4MuyHohVQoppDBZnPI1pNt+sLbuaVCAU="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2479,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:21:38.011995565Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"5c287225-829f-553a-aa03-07e87dce6871","title":"[L312] Unrelated E0 resources reuse artifact and directive caps, and full history has a byte ceiling","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L312.\n\n- **Source:** `crates/orchestration/peritus-orchestrator/src/candidate.rs:99-122,203-227`; `src/handoff.rs:205-235,320-359`; `src/ownership.rs:105-135`; `src/canonical/wire/observation/agent.rs:39-76`; `src/wire/state.rs:238-311,323-388`; `src/durability.rs:74-87`.\n- **Limiter:** `artifact_references` (at most 1,024) caps producer principals and paired ancestry digests as well as each handoff's artifact inputs, evidence inputs, and blocking findings. Reviewer pool size uses `child_directives` (at most 4,096). The agent observation decoder separately uses the compiled artifact ceiling for fixer responses. Complete state retains duplicated current candidate/cycle, historical candidates/cycles, embedded candidates in every handoff, observations and used commands under a mandatory actual encoded payload bound of at most 16 MiB minus header; event payloads have the same ceiling. Used commands have an additional 65,535-item limit. Six child-kind entries correspond to the closed domain enum, not a configurable work limit.\n- **Consequence:** Reducing one supposedly independent resource policy can reject a different valid input (for example producer provenance or a reviewer pool). Accumulated truthful history can prevent every next event/control checkpoint from fitting even when active work and the named count budgets have room. Byte enforcement occurs before the journal append, so this path does not establish the accepted-unreadable checkpoint defect documented in L297/L301.\n- **Repair direction:** Separate resource admission from complete lifetime evidence. Give each real active resource its own policy and represent provenance/history through digest-bound paged records rather than rejecting full aggregates at an arbitrary total byte count. Keep canonical ordering and complete finding/provenance coverage.\n- **Evidence scope:** Complete constructor, codec and persistence inspection; no large-history fixture was executed.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQFuhgJ8u2vUFJwNTXbaFGGq2qb7LHqV5GIEkRJJLJkf38Bt+H/0RD4h8fDAE7vPvNk283R8GWbbDgIQVQXbrOwc="}
