ojections from authoritative evidence. Update all producers, consumers and invariants together; a rejected new operation must leave the predecessor usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: valid boundary values and values just beyond each synthetic cap, final wrapper/receipt growth, non-ASCII strings, arbitrarily split frames/pages, malformed or conflicting data, mixed-version decode and save/reopen round trips. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:21:37.467Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQJx/AMJIFYxAQ/aWgrSgqLmMP5JcMUOvStOA3bndQMxnnthkoqtd48smb1g8xGK++Awsuz8iIeeaIqr0rnGvHg0="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2481,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:21:38.017459956Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"0c924f6d-e55b-5765-9769-ead68dc3122f","title":"[L313] E0's fixed lifecycle ends the run on candidate gate failure or B0 NeedsChanges","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L313.\n\n- **Source:** `crates/orchestration/peritus-orchestrator/src/reducer/apply/role_cycle.rs:120-161,164-217,220-262`; `src/reducer/apply/acceptance.rs:96-148,316-330`; `src/terminal.rs:25-112`; `src/reducer.rs:155-161`; `src/command.rs:18-126`; `src/product.rs:16-123`.\n- **Blocker:** Gate CandidateFailed becomes the run-level Rejected outcome. B0 NeedsChanges becomes run-level NeedsHuman via `KernelNeedsChanges`, with no check that fixer/revision budgets are actually consumed and no repair handoff. Only D2 NeedsFix opens the modeled fixer branch. Writer/fixer non-success and review NeedsHuman also commit terminal truth (or begin final child settlement), rather than retaining a resumable task phase. Once Terminal, every command is fenced closed.\n- **Consequence:** This aggregate conflates some candidate-level quality feedback with completion of the user's overall task. The comment saying B0 requested changes when no bounded autonomous fix branch remained is not a branch-condition check. A failed candidate cannot be repaired within this aggregate even if all cycle limits were removed. The separately read production quality adapter chooses Fix for failed gates and does not prove that this E0 route drives the user's current session.\n- **Repair direction:** Model candidate failure and requested changes as durable repair obligations with the same task authority/context. Distinguish final explicit rejection or unrecoverable external truth from feedback that can produce a new candidate. Keep acceptance fail-closed; changing continuation must not treat an invalid candidate as accepted.\n- **Evidence scope:** Source behavior of E0 and its adapter difference; live route and desired rejection policy still require caller evidence, not an asserted production diagnosis.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQGjoaxd+f531qR3SetlZ7dpZsmukRvtzbi7ooGG8iRfdgsUdFigOTpqDrKeeMaRimC50vTYgFUY7PrvDV4/SuAw="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2482,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:21:38.019795379Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"0c924f6d-e55b-5765-9769-ead68dc3122f","comment_uuid":"74781d56-c82e-494b-a1b3-7e74c84222bd","author":"6ME5","content":"Systemic repair plan for L313: E0's fixed lifecycle ends the run on candidate gate failure or B0 NeedsChanges.\n\nOwning contract and implementation boundary: crates/orchestration/peritus-orchestrator/src/reducer/apply/role_cycle.rs:120-161,164-217,220-262; src/reducer/apply/acceptance.rs:96-148,316-330; src/terminal.rs:25-112; src/reducer.rs:155-161; src/command.rs:18-126; src/product.rs:16-123. Apply the change through the constructors, live callers, durable writer and restart reader for this boundary, not as an isolated constant increase.\n\nModel candidate failure and requested changes as durable repair obligations with the same task authority/context. Distinguish final explicit rejection or unrecoverable external truth from feedback that can produce a new candidate. Keep acceptance fail-closed; changing continuation must not treat an invalid candidate as accepted.\n\nPreserve: exact candidate revision and artifact binding, complete finding/provenance conservation, independent reviewer evidence, truthful gate outcomes, protected user constraints and acceptance fail-closed on invalid evidence. Separate a physical allocation/page limit and a genuine authority or integrity check from a cumulative work allowance. Keep transient contention/capacity observable and recoverable under the existing logical task; do not discard accepted state or substitute a fresh session to get around it.\n\nCompatibility/migration: retain decoders and exact receipts for previously accepted records. If representation or lifecycle semantics change, introduce a versioned migration under exclusive ownership; verify a complete replacement frontier before atomic publication and keep the old recovery root until adoption is durable. Rebuild derived projections from authoritative evidence. Update all producers, consumers and invariants together; a rejected new operation must leave the predecessor usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: large and multi-file candidates, repeated valid repair cycles, changed candidate facts, delayed reviews, local/offline verification, restart mid-gate and cancellation, proving correct repair handoff without accepting a failed candidate or rereading unchanged evidence forever. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:21:37.467Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQP2I3ZnY7mJ3IZHWuuLBdWWWf8iN0XFBsyd0voHcHKiazGBrgCJueHktKivaN96xNCpBjE949jsSRcEJFTPrdQc="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2483,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:21:38.022136937Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"42057b18-7280-5ea7-bb5b-38680e3ef957","title":"[L314] E0 exact committed retries still depend on the latest checkpoint","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L314.\n\n- **Source:** `crates/orchestration/peritus-orchestrator/src/durability.rs:94-104,230-276,369-381`; `src/integration_tests/durability.rs:16-39,134-153`; `src/runtime/driver.rs:84-106`; `src/reducer.rs:155-175`.\n- **Blocker:** C0 can resolve the exact command digest and original event, but E0 also requires the current checkpoint to equal that command's original successor. If later work advanced the same run, the exact committed retry returns StaleState/Replay rather than its historical committed receipt. This is safer than the scheduler/collaboration adapters' quarantine classification (L284/L306), but still requires a separate caller recovery path. The driver itself attempts reduction before command resolution, so resubmitting an already consumed command at its current successor fails the reducer fence first.\n- **Consequence:** A delayed acknowledgment or retried request cannot be treated as successful from this API alone after progress. Blindly reissuing a new command to work around it risks duplicating semantics; blindly returning the failure can strand a caller even though its work committed. Underlying journal failures are collapsed into static External/Replay messages, losing the distinct journal recovery action.\n- **Repair direction:** Resolve exact historical command receipts independently of the mutable current checkpoint. Reconcile the driver's current state separately and preserve typed journal failure/recovery evidence. Do not weaken identity/digest conflict checks.\n- **Evidence scope:** Complete adapter/driver/tests inspection. Tests retry immediately before advancing/reopening; no delayed retry after a later commit or caller stall was executed.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQOdTi8fWEJzJvoVVwdendplN9cAzizkMEuRbvSwCM+qK7Dn9jvHdVvLWJNWvzocIoTbKoYiQY+Z/u8OxH33JDQ0="}
