{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2487,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:21:38.031598004Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"ef4b793c-6866-53d8-8daf-8beaedc5395d","title":"[L316] D0 requires seven immutable positive limits for a turn's accumulated work","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L316.\n\n- **Source:** `crates/orchestration/peritus-agent/src/limits.rs:28-93,172-234,262-276`; `src/identity.rs:145-205`; `src/state.rs:127-146`; `src/reducer.rs:38-79,109-139,251-284,355-379,523-547`; `src/command.rs:231-257` (remaining paths in the agent crate).\n- **Blocker:** AgentLimits has no unlimited representation. Every dimension must be positive and is bounded by compiled maxima: tool calls 256, provider events 1,000,000, context cycles 4,096, accumulated provider-output bytes 64 MiB, accumulated model-visible tool-result bytes 64 MiB, concurrent calls 32, and transitions 1,000,000. Limits remain fixed in the aggregate and genesis event; the closed command vocabulary cannot rebind or replenish them.\n- **Consequence:** Finishing a batch releases active concurrency but never cumulative tool/result/context/output/transition counters. ResultsRecorded discards current tools and resets ModelState, while these lifetime counters remain. Provider bytes are charged using the complete encoded C5 envelope length in the durable driver, including protocol metadata. Even a duplicate envelope increments provider_events and transitions, although its output-byte charge is zero. A productive long turn or repeated reconnection traffic eventually returns LimitExceeded/Exhausted without a durable continuation under the same binding.\n- **Repair direction:** Separate finite in-flight capacity and individual encoding bounds from lifetime execution allowance. Persist an advancing logical turn frontier with paged evidence and durable context/provider identity; admit continued work without mandatory total-work quotas. Keep checked arithmetic and authoritative effect authorization.\n- **Evidence scope:** Complete source reads; no exhaustion test executed and no proof that the installed DeveloperLoop dispatches through AgentDriver. These D0 aggregate limits are separate from DeveloperLoopLimits already cataloged in L049.\n\n- **Additional fully read fixture evidence:** tests/runtime_driver.rs:203-292 explicitly expects four charged provider events for a stream cursor of three after one duplicate. tests/budgets.rs:13-38 expects terminal Failed at the transition ceiling rather than continued execution. These tests were read, not run.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQCStLrU1QMRqmbHCOpivGHLl15qFDJ6MyS+EUmbu6rfMxJoCsHc6WA1XHbUHUMjFs3dwRjgWSOYWz+vb9fH3bww="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2488,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:21:38.033708219Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"ef4b793c-6866-53d8-8daf-8beaedc5395d","comment_uuid":"a46fa4f4-1c21-4dc7-9514-dfec47505953","author":"6ME5","content":"Systemic repair plan for L316: D0 requires seven immutable positive limits for a turn's accumulated work.\n\nOwning contract and implementation boundary: crates/orchestration/peritus-agent/src/limits.rs:28-93,172-234,262-276; src/identity.rs:145-205; src/state.rs:127-146; src/reducer.rs:38-79,109-139,251-284,355-379,523-547; src/command.rs:231-257. Apply the change through the constructors, live callers, durable writer and restart reader for this boundary, not as an isolated constant increase.\n\nSeparate finite in-flight capacity and individual encoding bounds from lifetime execution allowance. Persist an advancing logical turn frontier with paged evidence and durable context/provider identity; admit continued work without mandatory total-work quotas. Keep checked arithmetic and authoritative effect authorization.\n\nPreserve: canonical digest and schema identity, shared writer/reader admissibility, malformed-input rejection before allocation, exact causal ordering, actual provider/OS capability boundaries and preserved accepted historical evidence. Separate a physical allocation/page limit and a genuine authority or integrity check from a cumulative work allowance. Keep transient contention/capacity observable and recoverable under the existing logical task; do not discard accepted state or substitute a fresh session to get around it.\n\nCompatibility/migration: retain decoders and exact receipts for previously accepted records. If representation or lifecycle semantics change, introduce a versioned migration under exclusive ownership; verify a complete replacement frontier before atomic publication and keep the old recovery root until adoption is durable. Rebuild derived projections from authoritative evidence. Update all producers, consumers and invariants together; a rejected new operation must leave the predecessor usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: valid boundary values and values just beyond each synthetic cap, final wrapper/receipt growth, non-ASCII strings, arbitrarily split frames/pages, malformed or conflicting data, mixed-version decode and save/reopen round trips. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:21:37.467Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQJnkk2nhR5IpEFQEqBY392EacIRiHhWeBjAJjBr27conj27DvcDz74YZNp9imLZ1GTVeyDvFAY1g6bzRg9CD4QI="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2489,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:21:38.036054264Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"0cd35e25-ab79-54f4-a217-e9fae1540e46","title":"[L317] D0's shared transition allowance can prevent cancellation and terminal observation","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L317.\n\n- **Source:** `crates/orchestration/peritus-agent/src/reducer.rs:90-139,187-205,215-238,523-547,587-597`; `src/control.rs:19-120`; `src/verified.rs:276-317`; `src/runtime/driver.rs:345-377,423-474,614-625` (remaining paths in the agent crate).\n- **Blocker:** Every ordinary command increments the same transition counter before command-specific admission, including Paused, Resumed, CancellationRequested, CancellationFinished, ToolCompleted, and ResultsRecorded. At the exact ceiling there is one explicit exception: an Exhausted failure for the Transitions dimension can skip the counter increment. Other failures and cleanup commands cannot bypass exhaustion.\n- **Consequence:** If dispatch, progress, or provider observation consumes the last transition, normal settlement and cancellation cannot be recorded in that aggregate. The exception can irreversibly mark the turn Failed while retaining logically in-flight model/tool state; it does not itself terminate or reconcile external effects. drive_once simply returns the rejection and does not automatically select that exception. Process-local cancel_model is available independently, but that does not create durable cancellation or settlement truth.\n- **Repair direction:** Give durable control and effect-settlement transitions independent admission from normal work capacity. Preserve reconciliation obligations and resumable context across exhaustion instead of requiring an irreversible failure record to escape the counter ceiling.\n- **Evidence scope:** Source-derived boundary behavior only. The cancellation kernel explicitly documents that effect termination/reconciliation are caller duties. No live limit was reached or runtime changed during this audit.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQOn1oRepOO95sdv4Sfoq2ihhH796ufIYhHgdbj+KEKh5I22oibJpHCwN6s+Yls5AIkf2yJrCxzrNqG0i8t7XbQw="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2490,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:21:38.038350867Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"0cd35e25-ab79-54f4-a217-e9fae1540e46","comment_uuid":"19bdb263-da07-408e-b8c0-4a4b0145b200","author":"6ME5","content":"Systemic repair plan for L317: D0's shared transition allowance can prevent cancellation and terminal observation.\n\nOwning contract and implementation boundary: crates/orchestration/peritus-agent/src/reducer.rs:90-139,187-205,215-238,523-547,587-597; src/control.rs:19-120; src/verified.rs:276-317; src/runtime/driver.rs:345-377,423-474,614-625. Apply the change through the constructors, live callers, durable writer and restart reader for this boundary, not as an isolated constant increase.\n\nGive durable control and effect-settlement transitions independent admission from normal work capacity. Preserve reconciliation obligations and resumable context across exhaustion instead of requiring an irreversible failure record to escape the counter ceiling.\n\nPreserve: canonical digest and schema identity, shared writer/reader admissibility, malformed-input rejection before allocation, exact causal ordering, actual provider/OS capability boundaries and preserved accepted historical evidence. Separate a physical allocation/page limit and a genuine authority or integrity check from a cumulative work allowance. Keep transient contention/capacity observable and recoverable under the existing logical task; do not discard accepted state or substitute a fresh session to get around it.\n\nCompatibility/migration: retain decoders and exact receipts for previously accepted records. If representation or lifecycle semantics change, introduce a versioned migration under exclusive ownership; verify a complete replacement frontier before atomic publication and keep the old recovery root until adoption is durable. Rebuild derived projections from authoritative evidence. Update all producers, consumers and invariants together; a rejected new operation must leave the predecessor usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: valid boundary values and values just beyond each synthetic cap, final wrapper/receipt growth, non-ASCII strings, arbitrarily split frames/pages, malformed or conflicting data, mixed-version decode and save/reopen round trips. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:21:37.467Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQKQVPAtVacwHIBffFGkYO7iXP0UKRB1k5gUq+lxu+lP8BFA1QU0l2tMaVwxh9p6kTDthllemuf2roL/AiSVVygA="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2491,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:21:38.040395775Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"1ac22fac-f48e-50b1-9d90-f4076d28d545","title":"[L318] D0 cancellation changes phase before it can record outstanding effect settlement","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L318.\n\n- **Source:** `crates/orchestration/peritus-agent/src/control.rs:80-119`; `src/reducer.rs:215-238,355-379,523-547`; `src/verified.rs:206-291`; `src/runtime/driver/tool_steps.rs:156-200,237-272` (remaining paths in the agent crate).\n- **Blocker:** CancellationRequested immediately changes the aggregate from any active/paused phase to Cancelling. ToolCompleted, ToolActivated, provider observations and result recording are admitted only in their original active phases. There is no separate cancellation-reconciliation command and Cancel cannot resume the previous phase.\n- **Consequence:** A tool dispatched before cancellation can become terminal through independent cancel_tool_once, but record_tool_observation_once and classify_lost_tool_once cannot persist that terminal result while Cancelling. CancellationFinished can instead mark TerminalCancelled without checking active tool counters, model ownership or batch quiescence; all later commands are rejected. This creates a choice between a stuck cancellation aggregate and a terminal aggregate retaining unresolved effects. Paused state similarly rejects ordinary observations until it is resumed, although external effects can still finish meanwhile.\n- **Repair direction:** Model stop intent separately from the effect-observation frontier. Admit terminal truth and reconciliation during pause/cancellation; require explicit quiescence or durable unresolved obligations before final cancellation. Preserve semantic context without redispatching uncertain effects.\n- **Evidence scope:** Complete control, reducer and runtime caller reads. Caller duties documented by control.rs do not provide an API to store those results after the phase change. Source counterexample only; no live cancellation or test execution.\n\n- **Additional fully read fixture evidence:** tests/control_matrix.rs:45-62 explicitly requires TerminalCancelled to retain one active tool and the dispatched batch. This is an intentional existing aggregate contract, so the repair must change the ownership/reconciliation model and its tests, not remove a phase guard alone. No test was executed.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQAxIN+WyJvxK/J/JfB+Z27+YQ6KlgmZnfTY0+0wFX32Uqsiuo0CcpC3e4+XJ+J1RQKe4LWSQbTkghIN5n9Sohw8="}
